{"level":30,"time":1778246212755,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VQHXCB2P99PT4Z6XJJEM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have the grouping file. This is about \"Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\" - a comprehensive set of requirements around clearances from overhead electric utilities. Let me now understand:\n\n1. **What this grouping covers**: Clearance requirements between overhead electric distribution and transmission facilities and proposed site features\n2. **Key thresholds**:\n   - 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from primary, neutral, secondary conductors\n   - 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors\n   - 16 feet minimum vertical clearance for driveways without truck traffic\n   - 18 feet minimum vertical clearance for roads with truck traffic\n   - 10 lateral feet from distribution conductors for trees\n   - 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors for trees (per UCM § 1.10.10.4)\n   - 10-foot radial clearance for construction working clearances from energized lines\n   - Other specific requirements\n\n3. **Documents to Review**: Site plan sheets, building elevations, sections/profiles, survey data, landscape plans, utility plans, cover sheet\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Read the project README to understand the site plan structure and get the documentId\n2. Read facts.md to understand what infrastructure and features exist on the site\n3. Review relevant sheets to assess each checklist item\n4. Use vision_check for specific visual verification if needed\n\nLet me start by reading the project README and facts.md.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa