{"level":30,"time":1778246213152,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VQJ2D747Z79MRMTCMNPCY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I've read the grouping file. Now let me understand the key points:\n\n**Grouping Description**: Tree placement requirements near overhead electric distribution and transmission lines. The grouping covers species selection, minimum clearance distances, measurement methodology, and plan documentation.\n\n**Key Thresholds**:\n- Distribution clearances (measured from outside conductor):\n  - < 15 lateral feet: Only utility-compatible trees permitted\n  - 15-25 lateral feet: UC trees OR trees < 40 feet mature height\n  - > 25 lateral feet: All trees permitted\n- Transmission clearances: 50 lateral feet minimum, only UC trees\n- Additional prohibitions:\n  - Within transmission easement (all trees)\n  - Within 10 feet of poles\n  - Within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment\n  - Within 5 feet of underground equipment\n  - Trees within 20 feet of underground equipment need root barriers\n\n**Measurement Rules**:\n- Lateral distance from tree trunk CENTER to OUTSIDE conductor\n- NOT pole centerline\n- NOT canopy edge\n- Conductors offset 4+ feet from pole center\n\n**Documents to Review**:\n- Landscape Plan / Planting Plan\n- Site Plan\n- Plant Schedule / Plant Legend\n- Utility Plan\n- Grading Plan\n\n**Checklist Items** (15 items total): EL-2.1 through EL-2.15\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check applicability - does this project have overhead electric lines and trees?\n2. Read the project README to understand what documents are available\n3. Check facts.md for basic project info\n4. Examine relevant sheets/documents\n5. Evaluate each checklist item\n\nLet me start by reading the project README.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_