{"level":30,"time":1778246225237,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G5n29WjjXnkjEmwd3q9pA8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 4 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — This is a detailed site plan drawing showing an existing conditions survey. It includes property lines, buildings (existing slabs), trees, fences, utilities, and topographic contours. Key features include 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' on the left side, 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION' in the center, and 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS' on the right.\n     4→\n     5→The drawing represents an existing conditions survey of a property. It features detailed topographic contours, various trees marked with identifiers (e.g., +4046, +4047), and a large structure footprint labeled 'SLAB F.F.E.-686.8' within 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION VOL. 73, PG. 76 P.R.T.C.TX'. The property is bordered by 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' to the west. Various utility lines, fences (chain link, wood, crete), and easements are depicted. Adjacent properties include 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS VOL. 64, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX' and a property labeled 'WILLIAM LANCE COMSBIE, JR. (1.957 AC.) VOL. 5139, PG. 563 D.R.T.C.TX'. A scale bar and north arrow are present on the left side.\n     6→\n     7→## Block 2: notes — List of cities where Bleyl Engineering operates.\n     8→\n     9→Austin Bryan Conroe Houston\n    10→\n    11→## Block 3: notes — Information regarding the coordinate system and bearing basis used for the survey.\n    12→\n    13→BEARING BASIS:\n    14→BEARINGS, DISTANCES AND COORDINATES ARE\n    15→BASED ON THE TEXAS COORDINATE SYSTEM\n    16→OF 1983 (NAD83) CENTRAL ZONE, GRID.\n    17→\n    18→## Block 5: notes — Indicates the job number associated with the survey document.\n    19→\n    20→JOB NUMBER: 20240953\n    21→\n    22→## Block 8: notes — Certification statement and signature of the Registered Profe