ARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n    28→IF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\n    29→SUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\n    30→FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n    31→\n    32→## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n    33→\n    34→KEY NOTES:\n    35→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n    36→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n    37→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n    38→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n    39→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n    40→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n    41→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\n    42→SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    43→PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    44→P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    45→M - MITIGATION TREE\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n    48→\n    49→OWNER:\n    50→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    51→RE, LLC\n    52→\n    53→## Block 8: text_block — Name of the project.\n    54→\n    55→PROJECT NAME:\n    56→VALLEY VIEW\n    57→TOWNHOMES\n    58→\n    59→## Block 9: text_block — Address of the project location.\n    60→\n    61→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    62→3759 VALLEY\n    63→VIEW ROAD,\n    64→AUSTIN,\n    65→TEXAS 78704\n    66→\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c88cf1-2078-476d-9e24-f9a661c6a8fa","uuid":"738f3ccb-20a6-4896-91c0-e497d559e181","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n\nNORTH\n[North Arrow Symbol]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n0 10 20 50\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n\nThis block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n- Building footprints\n- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n- Sidewalks and pathways\n- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n\n## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n\nNOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\nFOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n\n## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n\nKEY NOTES:\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\nSY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nPL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nP - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\nM - MITIGATION TREE\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 8: text_block — Name of the project.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n## Block 9: text_block — Address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246230918,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018zEbmVQPgHDLBJuippyqRm","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 4: notes — Plant list section heading.\n     4→\n     5→PLANT LIST\n     6→\n     7→## Block 5: notes — Notes related to the plant list.\n     8→\n     9→NOTES:\n    10→1. THE CONTRACTORS (GENERAL AND SUBCONTRACTORS) SHALL PROVIDE UNIT COSTS FOR ALL\n    11→SOFTSCAPE AND HARDSCAPE MATERIAL SPECIFIED ON THE DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. UNIT\n    12→COSTS SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR MATERIALS AND INSTALLATION SEPARATELY. UNIT COSTS SHALL\n    13→BE: 'EACH' FOR PLANT MATERIAL, 'SQUARE FOOT' OR 'SQUARE YARD' FOR PAVEMENTS, LINEAR FOOT\n    14→FOR WALL AND FENCE, 'EACH' FOR SITE FURNISHINGS AND SITE AMENITIES, 'CUBIC YARD' OR 'CUBIC\n    15→FOOT' FOR SOIL, MULCH AND OTHER BULK PRODUCTS AND 'EACH' OR 'LUMP SUM' FOR\n    16→MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS. THE UNIT COST SHALL BE FORMATTED TO HAVE COLUMNS FOR; ITEMS, UNIT,\n    17→UNIT COST, TOTAL ITEM COST.\n    18→2. PLANT QUANTITIES ARE PROVIDED FOR OWNER CONVENIENCE ONLY. CONTRACTOR IS\n    19→RESPONSIBLE FOR VERIFYING AND PROVIDING PLANT QUANTITIES SHOWN ON THE LANDSCAPE PLAN.\n    20→3. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LOCATING AND SECURING TREE AND PLANT MATERIAL IN\n    21→ADVANCE. BECAUSE OF THE LONG LEAD TIME ON THIS INSTALLATION AND THE RECENT SHORTAGE\n    22→ON TREE CROP, CONTRACTOR SHALL RESERVE OR CONTRACT GROW TREES WITH A GROWER.\n    23→\n    24→## Block 6: notes — Notes on special construction techniques.\n    25→\n    26→SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\n    27→ECM 3.5.4 (D)\n    28→1. PRIOR TO EXCAVATION WITHIN TREE DRIP LINES OR THE REMOVAL OF\n    29→TREES ADJACENT TO OTHER TREES THAT ARE TO REMAIN, MAKE A\n    30→CLEAN CUT BETWEEN THE DISTURBED AND UNDISTURBED ROOT ZONES\n    31→WITH A ROCK SAW OR SIMILAR EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    32→2. IN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS THAT CANNOT BE PROTECTED DURING\n    33→CONSTRUCTION WITH FENCING AND WHERE HEAVY VEHICULAR TRAFFIC\n    34→IS ANTICIPATED, COVER THOSE AREAS WITH A MINIMUM OF 12 INCHES OF\n    35→ORGANIC MULCH TO MINIMIZE SOIL COMPACTION. IN AREAS WITH HIGH\n    36→SOIL PLASTICITY GEOTEXTILE FABRIC, PER STANDARD SPECIFICATION\n    37→620S, SHOULD BE PLACED UNDER THE MULCH TO PREVENT EXCESSIVE\n    38→MIXING OF THE SOIL AND MULCH. ADDITIONALLY, MATERIAL SUCH AS\n    39→PLYWOOD AND METAL SHEETS, COULD BE REQUIRED BY THE CITY\n    40→ARBORIST TO MINIMIZE ROOT IMPACTS FROM HEAVY EQUIPMENT.\n    41→3. ONCE THE PROJECT IS COMPLETED, ALL MATERIALS SHOULD BE\n    42→REMOVED, AND THE MULCH SHOULD BE REDUCED TO A DEPTH OF 3\n    43→INCHES. PERFORM ALL GRADING WITHIN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS BY\n    44→HAND OR WITH SMALL EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    45→4. WATER ALL TREES MOST HEAVILY IMPACTED BY CONSTRUCTION\n    46→ACTIVITIES DEEPLY ONCE A WEEK DURING ACCUMULATION OF THE\n    47→LEAVES.\n    48→5. WHEN INSTALLING CONCRETE ADJACENT TO THE ROOT ZONE OF A TREE,\n    49→USE A PLASTIC VAPOR BARRIER BEHIND THE CONCRETE TO PROHIBIT\n    50→LEACHING OF LIME INTO THE SOIL.\n    51→\n    52→## Block 8: notes — Notes related to tree preservation calculations.\n    53→\n    54→NOTES:\n    55→1. CHINABERRY AND BRADFORD PEAR ARE INVASIVE TREES AND REQUIRE NO MITIGATION.\n    56→2. ASH TREES REQUIRE NO MITIGATION DUE TO EMERALD ASH BORER.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 11: table — Table listing shade trees.\n    59→\n    60→SHADE TREES\n    61→\n    62→| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n    63→|---|---|---|---|\n    64→| [circle with dot] | | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PERSERVED | |\n    65→| [circle with cross] | 2 | LIVE OAK, QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n    66→| [circle with hash] | 10 | CEDAR ELM, ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n    67→\n    68→## Block 12: table — Calculations related to landscaping.\n    69→\n    70→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    71→LANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS:\n    72→\n    73→STREET YARD AREA:\n    74→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n    75→|---|---|---|\n    76→| TOTAL SITE AREA | N/A | 94,203 SF |\n    77→| TOTAL STREET-YARD AREA | N/A | 6,314 SF |\n    78→| STREET-YARD / LANDSCAPE (20%) | 1,263 SF | 5,206 SF |\n    79→\n    80→STREET YARD TREES:\n    81→EXISTING TREES CREDIT\n    82→| | | |\n    83→|---|---|---|\n    84→| 2\" DIAMETER TO 6\" DIAMETER | 0 | |\n    85→| 6\" DIAMETER OR GREATER | 4 | |\n    86→\n    87→EXISTING TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n    88→|---|---|\n    89→| | 8 CREDITS |\n    90→\n    91→PROPOSED TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n    92→|---|---|\n    93→| | 0 CREDITS |\n    94→\n    95→TOTAL STREET YARD TREES, EXISTING TREES CREDIT PLUS PROPOSED TREES CREDIT:\n    96→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n    97→|---|---|---|\n    98→| | 5 | 8 |\n    99→\n   100→LANDSCAPE IN PARKING LOTS:\n   101→90SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN SY\n   102→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   103→|---|---|---|\n   104→| | 0 | 0 |\n   105→\n   106→60SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN NON SY\n   107→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   108→|---|---|---|\n   109→| | 60 | 816 |\n   110→\n   111→LANDSCAPE ISLAND MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE, 8' MIN. INSIDE WIDTH\n   112→1 TREE MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE\n   113→\n   114→BUFFERING POINTS FOR DRIVE AISLE:\n   115→| | SIZE | QTY | PREFERRED | OTHER | PROVIDED |\n   116→|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   117→| LARGE TREE | 4\" | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n   118→| SMALL TREE | 2.5\" | 1 | YES | | 9 |\n   119→| MEDIUM SHRUB | 5 GAL. | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n   120→| LARGE SHRUB | 7 GAL. | 16 | YES | | 48 |\n   121→\n   122→BUFFER POINTS REQUIRED: 40\n   123→BUFFER POINTS PROVIDED: 57\n   124→\n   125→PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE & PEDESTRIAN AMENITIES: SUB CHAPTER E\n   126→REQUIRED (5% OF SITE AREA) (5% X 94,293) 4,715 SF\n   127→PROVIDED 5,855 SF\n   128→\n   129→## Blo