{"level":30,"time":1778246239727,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ZRh3XsP5jSYANF5Bu3jxR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 16\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for the proposed Valley View Townhomes project.\n     4→\n     5→AW\n     6→City of Austin | Austin Water\n     7→6310 Wilhelmina Delco Drive, Suite 3100\n     8→Austin, Texas 78752\n     9→http://www.austintexas.gov/SER\n    10→SER@austintexas.gov\n    11→\n    12→Mr. Jason Rodgers, P.E.\n    13→Bleyl Engineering\n    14→7701 San Felipe Blvd Ste 200\n    15→Austin, Texas 78729\n    16→\n    17→Re: Letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\n    18→3759 Valley View Townhomes Service Extension Request for Water (SER-6324)\n    19→3759 Valley View, Austin, Texas 78704\n    20→\n    21→Dear Mr. Rodgers:\n    22→\n    23→Austin Water has reviewed your submittal for the above referenced Service Extension Request (SER) project and is issuing this letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service in keeping with all current rules and regulations.\n    24→\n    25→Submitted project specifications:\n    26→39 Condo Units (6 to 24 Units/Acre)\n    27→Living Unit Equivalent (LUE): 28\n    28→Subject Tract Area: 3.59 Acres\n    29→Water Demand (Estimated Peak Hour): 60 gpm\n    30→Sprinkled Fire flow requirement of 1,500 gpm and water demand submitted in the engineering calculations received from Jason Rodgers, P.E. of Bleyl Engineering on 10/20/2025.\n    31→\n    32→Based on the submitted project specifications and the results of the Service Extension Request review, it has been determined that the existing 8-inch water main (Drawn. No. 74-0050) in Valley View Rd. is suitable and sufficient to provide service to the subject tract.\n    33→\n    34→Due to the existing suitable and sufficient water main at the subject tract, a water main extension/improvement is not required for this project.\n    35→\n    36→Water service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water plan review process. It is suggested that this letter be submitted with your site development plans.\n    37→\n    38→This letter will automatically expire 180 days after its date of issue unless a development application has been accepted by the Development Services Department (DSD). If a development application has been accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.\n    39→\n    40→If we can provide additional information, please call me at (512) 972-0035.\n    41→\n    42→Sincerely,\n    43→[Signature]\n    44→Christine Perez, P.E.\n    45→Austin Water\n    46→Utility Development Services Division\n    47→\n    48→DATE: 12/10/2025\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa-c822-4488-9300-f5bc2aee8d18","uuid":"065c3455-7786-4738-8b39-561d465f0102","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-16.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 16\n\n## text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for the proposed Valley View Townhomes project.\n\nAW\nCity of Austin | Austin Water\n6310 Wilhelmina Delco Drive, Suite 3100\nAustin, Texas 78752\nhttp://www.austintexas.gov/SER\nSER@austintexas.gov\n\nMr. Jason Rodgers, P.E.\nBleyl Engineering\n7701 San Felipe Blvd Ste 200\nAustin, Texas 78729\n\nRe: Letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\n3759 Valley View Townhomes Service Extension Request for Water (SER-6324)\n3759 Valley View, Austin, Texas 78704\n\nDear Mr. Rodgers:\n\nAustin Water has reviewed your submittal for the above referenced Service Extension Request (SER) project and is issuing this letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service in keeping with all current rules and regulations.\n\nSubmitted project specifications:\n39 Condo Units (6 to 24 Units/Acre)\nLiving Unit Equivalent (LUE): 28\nSubject Tract Area: 3.59 Acres\nWater Demand (Estimated Peak Hour): 60 gpm\nSprinkled Fire flow requirement of 1,500 gpm and water demand submitted in the engineering calculations received from Jason Rodgers, P.E. of Bleyl Engineering on 10/20/2025.\n\nBased on the submitted project specifications and the results of the Service Extension Request review, it has been determined that the existing 8-inch water main (Drawn. No. 74-0050) in Valley View Rd. is suitable and sufficient to provide service to the subject tract.\n\nDue to the existing suitable and sufficient water main at the subject tract, a water main extension/improvement is not required for this project.\n\nWater service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water plan review process. It is suggested that this letter be submitted with your site development plans.\n\nThis letter will automatically expire 180 days after its date of issue unless a development application has been accepted by the Development Services Department (DSD). If a development application has been accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.\n\nIf we can provide additional information, please call me at (512) 972-0035.\n\nSincerely,\n[Signature]\nChristine Perez, P.E.\nAustin Water\nUtility Development Services Division\n\nDATE: 12/10/2025\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246239729,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UqCUh2n7KxfhQ6cmWQdHfj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 13\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\n     4→\n     5→Electric Transmission Notes\n     6→1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n     7→2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n     8→3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n     9→4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n    10→5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n    11→6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n    12→7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n    13→8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n    14→9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n    15→10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n    16→11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n    17→12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n    18→13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n    19→14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\n    20→15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\n    21→16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    22→  · any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n    23→  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n    24→  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa-c822-4488-9300-f5bc2aee8d18","uuid":"4d2c98f8-e980-4f6c-a160-8e54503d9fbd","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 13\n\n## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\n\nElectric Transmission Notes\n1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n  · any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246239730,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019F9jHxxapvLV69nLxx8tvN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 14\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing wastewater main has adequate capacity for the proposed Valley View Townhomes project.\n     4→\n     5→AW\n     6→City of Austin | Austin Water\n     7→6310 Wilhelmina Delco Drive, Suite 3100\n     8→Austin, Texas 78752\n     9→http://www.austintexas.gov/SER\n    10→SER@austintexas.gov\n    11→\n    12→Mr. Jason Rodgers, P.E.\n    13→Bleyl Engineering\n    14→7701 San Felipe Blvd Ste 200\n    15→Austin, Texas 78729\n    16→\n    17→Re: Letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\n    18→3759 Valley View Townhomes Service Extension Request for Wastewater (SER-6325)\n    19→3759 Valley View, Austin, Texas 78704\n    20→\n    21→Dear Mr. Rodgers:\n    22→\n    23→Austin Water has reviewed your submittal for the above referenced Service Extension Request (SER) project and is issuing this letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service in keeping with all current rules and regulations.\n    24→\n    25→Submitted project specifications:\n    26→39 Condo Units (6 to 24 Units/Acre)\n    27→Living Unit Equivalent (LUE): 28\n    28→Subject Tract Area: 3.59 Acres\n    29→Wastewater Flow (Estimated Peak Wet Weather): 20 gpm\n    30→Wastewater flow submitted in the engineering calculations received from Jason Rodgers, P.E. of Bleyl Engineering on 10/20/2025.\n    31→\n    32→Based on the submitted project specifications and the results of the Service Extension Request review, it has been determined that the existing 8-inch gravity wastewater main (MH No. 15466) in Valley View Rd. is suitable and sufficient to provide service to the subject tract.\n    33→\n    34→Due to the existing suitable and sufficient wastewater main at the subject tract, a wastewater main extension/improvement is not required for this project.\n    35→\n    36→Wastewater service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water plan review process. It is suggested that this letter be submitted with your site development plans.\n    37→\n    38→This letter will automatically expire 180 days after its date of issue unless a development application has been accepted by the Development Services Department (DSD). If a development application has been accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.\n    39→\n    40→If we can provide additional information, please call me at (512) 972-0035.\n    41→\n    42→Sincerely,\n    43→[Signature]\n    44→Christine Perez, P.E.\n    45→Austin Water\n    46→Utility Development Services Division\n    47→\n    48→DATE: 12/10/2025\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa-c822-4488-9300-f5bc2aee8d18","uuid":"3a4fdc35-9663-4b5e-a1c1-1ab26535c3b5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-14.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 14\n\n## text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing wastewater main has adequate capacity for the proposed Valley View Townhomes project.\n\nAW\nCity of Austin | Austin Water\n6310 Wilhelmina Delco Drive, Suite 3100\nAustin, Texas 78752\nhttp://www.austintexas.gov/SER\nSER@austintexas.gov\n\nMr. Jason Rodgers, P.E.\nBleyl Engineering\n7701 San Felipe Blvd Ste 200\nAustin, Texas 78729\n\nRe: Letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\n3759 Valley View Townhomes Service Extension Request for Wastewater (SER-6325)\n3759 Valley View, Austin, Texas 78704\n\nDear Mr. Rodgers:\n\nAustin Water has reviewed your submittal for the above referenced Service Extension Request (SER) project and is issuing this letter of Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service in keeping with all current rules and regulations.\n\nSubmitted project specifications:\n39 Condo Units (6 to 24 Units/Acre)\nLiving Unit Equivalent (LUE): 28\nSubject Tract Area: 3.59 Acres\nWastewater Flow (Estimated Peak Wet Weather): 20 gpm\nWastewater flow submitted in the engineering calculations received from Jason Rodgers, P.E. of Bleyl Engineering on 10/20/2025.\n\nBased on the submitted project specifications and the results of the Service Extension Request review, it has been determined that the existing 8-inch gravity wastewater main (MH No. 15466) in Valley View Rd. is suitable and sufficient to provide service to the subject tract.\n\nDue to the existing suitable and sufficient wastewater main at the subject tract, a wastewater main extension/improvement is not required for this project.\n\nWastewater service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water plan review process. It is suggested that this letter be submitted with your site development plans.\n\nThis letter will automatically expire 180 days after its date of issue unless a development application has been accepted by the Development Services Department (DSD). If a development application has been accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.\n\nIf we can provide additional information, please call me at (512) 972-0035.\n\nSincerely,\n[Signature]\nChristine Perez, P.E.\nAustin Water\nUtility Development Services Division\n\nDATE: 12/10/2025\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
