{"level":30,"time":1778246240233,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VRENF7GQ6ANXYSFSPE3BG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important! The site plan DOES have:\n1. **Overhead electric transmission facilities** - There are notes throughout about transmission structures, poles, guy anchors, transmission easements, and overhead lines\n2. **Proposed overhead electric facilities for service to the building** - Block 19, item 3 mentions \"proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project\"\n\nThe notes also mention:\n- Electric transmission structures and poles within or adjacent to the site\n- Transmission easements requiring clearances\n- Down guy anchors\n- Requirements for clearances from transmission lines per NESC and OSHA\n\nNow I need to understand:\n1. Are there overhead distribution facilities for customer service to buildings?\n2. What are the spatial relationships between buildings, site features, and overhead lines?\n3. Are proper clearance dimensions shown on the plans?\n\nLet me check the landscape plan blocks and building elevation sheets to see what clearance information is actually documented.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","uuid":"9b0088c6-4a0f-44a7-800a-740ce684d04f"}
