{"level":30,"time":1778246243524,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VRGT463D9JXCVJCDQ9T99","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have the plant schedule. The trees being planted include:\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 100 gal, 4\" cal, 16' ht\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 100 gal, 4\" cal, 16' ht\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 45 gal, 2.5\" cal, 10' ht\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 45 gal, 2.5\" cal, 8' ht\n- Plus shrubs and groundcovers\n\nNow I need to check ECM Appendix F to understand which of these trees are \"utility-compatible\" (UC designation) and what their mature heights are:\n- Cedar Elm - I believe this is utility-compatible with mature height around 40 feet (NOT utility-compatible size)\n- Live Oak - Likely 40+ feet mature height (large tree)\n- Mexican Redbud - Mature height typically 25-30 feet (small to medium)\n- Texas Mountain Laurel - Mature height typically 25 feet (mentioned in the grouping as an exception to the 20-foot UC limit)\n\nThe critical question remains: Are there OVERHEAD electric facilities on this site? Let me use the vision check tool to examine the actual site plan and see if overhead electric lines are shown.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bd4df49-5a3c-4afa-8eeb-b16b6883780f","uuid":"1172442c-7c15-4afb-8fed-96ba330dadbb"}
