{"level":30,"time":1778246244666,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VRHM187C1E6Q938JSHAKF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! This is critical - Block 13 on Sheet 3 contains \"Electric Transmission Notes\" that specifically address transmission structures and their easements. This confirms that there ARE electric transmission structures (overhead facilities) on or adjacent to the site.\n\nThe notes mention:\n- \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\"\n- \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\"\n- Various requirements about clearances (20 feet for aerial equipment during construction, 25 feet for grading/digging, etc.)\n- Note 16 explicitly addresses structures that cannot be placed within transmission easements\n\nThis strongly indicates:\n1. There ARE transmission lines/structures on the site\n2. There IS a transmission easement\n3. The project must comply with clearance requirements from these transmission facilities\n\nNow I need to determine:\n1. Whether overhead DISTRIBUTION lines also exist (the grouping covers both distribution and transmission)\n2. Whether the site plan shows these transmission structures and clearances adequately\n3. Whether other checklist items apply\n\nLet me check the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) more carefully by looking for a vision check on whether overhead utility lines are actually depicted on that sheet.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa-c822-4488-9300-f5bc2aee8d18","uuid":"1d2aa593-eae8-4529-ab39-75ae75d4677d"}
