{"level":30,"time":1778246251329,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sgr4S7S7U2pYr5pv9tQDBY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 20 — Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile\n     2→\n     3→Utility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→* Proposed Pipe Segments: 47.0 lf of 8\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 5.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ -0.00% slope), 12.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 3.0 lf of 6\" C900, 5.0 lf of 6\" C900\n    11→* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\n    12→* Restraints: 52' of restraints required from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52\n    13→* Benchmarks: BM #1 = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    14→* Pressure Reducing Valve (PRV) Threshold: 65 psi\n    15→* Geologist Inspection Trench Depth Threshold: > 5 feet\n    16→\n    17→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    18→\n    19→* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n    20→* **Block 2**: drawing — Plan View of Utility Tap. Top-down layout showing the proposed connection to the existing 6\" water line, the new fire hydrant, vault, and various utility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n    21→* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n    22→* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n    23→* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n    24→* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n    25→* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n    26→* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n    27→* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n    28→\n    29→---\n    30→\n    31→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    32→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","uuid":"20deb9a2-0856-49ee-bec4-ab8b8e1bfc9b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 20 — Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile\n\nUtility tap public plan and profile for townhomes project.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the public plan and profile for a proposed utility tap (Water Line A) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the connection to an existing AC water main, the transition to new DI pipe, and the installation of a new fire demand meter, vault, and fire hydrant.\n\n**Key values:**\n* Proposed Pipe Segments: 47.0 lf of 8\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 5.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ -0.00% slope), 12.0 lf of 6\" DI (@ 0.00% slope), 3.0 lf of 6\" C900, 5.0 lf of 6\" C900\n* Flowline Elevations: FL 8\" = 674.33', FL In 6\" = 674.42', FL Out 6\" = 674.42'\n* Restraints: 52' of restraints required from Sta 0+00 to Sta 0+52\n* Benchmarks: BM #1 = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n* Pressure Reducing Valve (PRV) Threshold: 65 psi\n* Geologist Inspection Trench Depth Threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n* **Block 1**: drawing — Profile View of Water Line A (Wtr-Ln-A). Shows the vertical alignment of the proposed water line from station 0+00 to 0+75, including the transition from AC to DI pipe, reducers, and the meter vault. Use VISION to examine the pipe slopes and relationship to the existing/proposed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n* **Block 2**: drawing — Plan View of Utility Tap. Top-down layout showing the proposed connection to the existing 6\" water line, the new fire hydrant, vault, and various utility crossings. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the proposed infrastructure and intersections with existing easements and lines.\n* **Block 3**: notes — Restrained Joints Specification. Details the requirement to restrain all bends, tees, and valves using specific SPL standards (WW-27F or WW-27A). READ the block content for the approved mechanical joint restraint standards.\n* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n* **Block 5**: notes — Water Tap Note. Contains instructions for replacing the existing AC pipe with DI pipe. READ the block content for strict asbestos handling and disposal requirements.\n* **Block 6**: notes — Legend. Defines linetypes and symbols used in the plan view. READ the block content to accurately interpret the utility lines (Water, Wastewater, Storm, Electric) in Block 2.\n* **Block 7**: notes — PRV Note. READ the block content for the specific pressure threshold (65 psi) that requires the installation of a pressure reducing valve.\n* **Block 9**: notes — Void and Water Flow Mitigation. READ the block content for the trenching depth threshold (> 5 feet) that triggers a mandatory inspection by a licensed geologist.\n* **Blocks 8, 10, 11, 12, 13**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Includes the legal description, standard disclaimers regarding existing utility locations, general verification notes, the PE Seal for Jason K. Rodgers, and the Texas 811 logo. READ the block content only if verifying administrative details, legal descriptions, or standard utility coordination notes.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246251330,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015DbX1S8Bzp1HTmkv2XguEC","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 17 — Conveyance Cross Sections\n     2→\n     3→Conveyance cross-section graphs and corresponding site plan view.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the conveyance cross-sections and a corresponding site plan snippet for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to model and display the hydraulic performance (water surface elevations, velocities, and channel depths) of the site's drainage conveyance system during 25-year and 100-year storm events at three distinct cross-section locations (XS 1, XS 2, and XS 3).\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Manning's Roughness Coefficient (n):** 0.03 used for all cross-sections\n    11→*   **Design Flow Rates (Q):** 16.49 cfs (25-Year event), 21.97 cfs (100-Year event) across all sections\n    12→*   **Maximum 100-Year Velocity:** 8.70 ft/s (at cross-section XS 3)\n    13→*   **Maximum 100-Year Depth:** 0.48 ft (at cross-section XS 3)\n    14→*   **Benchmark 1:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n    15→*   **Benchmark 2:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n    16→*   **Finished Floor Elevations (FFE):** Bldg. 5 = 683.0 ft, Bldg. 6 = 683.0 ft\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 7: site plan — Multi-family development plan view**\n    21→    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, grading contours, drainage easements, and the specific locations of the cross-section cut lines (XS 1, XS 2, XS 3) relative to buildings 5 and 6 and existing retaining walls.\n    22→*   **Blocks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6: diagrams — Cross-section profile graphs**\n    23→    Use VISION to examine the channel profiles, side slopes, and plotted water surface elevations for cross-sections XS 1, XS 2, and XS 3 under both 25-year and 100-year storm conditions. \n    24→*   **Blocks 14, 15, 16, 17, 19, 20: tables — Hydraulic data tables**\n    25→    READ for exact hydraulic parameters corresponding to each cross-section graph, including Depth (ft), Flow Rate Q (cfs), Area (sqft), Velocity (ft/s), Wetted Perimeter Wp (ft), Critical Depth Yc (ft), Top Width (ft), and Energy Head (ft).\n    26→*   **Block 21: text_block — Hydraulic modeling note**\n    27→    READ to verify the Manning's roughness coefficient used in the calculations.\n    28→*   **Block 12: notes — Benchmarks**\n    29→    READ for exact elevation values and physical descriptions of the survey benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2).\n    30→*   **Block 8: notes — Legend**\n    31→    READ for definitions of line types and symbols used in the plan view, such as existing/proposed contours, storm drain lines, and limits of construction.\n    32→*   **Block 9: notes — Construction and landscape notes**\n    33→    READ for curb construction grading instructions (catch curb vs. spill curb) and references to the tree list.\n    34→*   **Blocks 10, 11, 13, 18: various — Boilerplate, Title Block & Administrative**\n    35→    READ for the legal description of the property, project title (Valley View Townhomes), engineer seal (Bleyl Engineering), standard utility/Texas 811 warnings, and city submittal disclaimers.\n    36→\n    37→---\n    38→\n    39→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    40→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","uuid":"f56cc0da-a636-401c-bf45-4cea0f7b5b62","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-17/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 17 — Conveyance Cross Sections\n\nConveyance cross-section graphs and corresponding site plan view.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the conveyance cross-sections and a corresponding site plan snippet for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to model and display the hydraulic performance (water surface elevations, velocities, and channel depths) of the site's drainage conveyance system during 25-year and 100-year storm events at three distinct cross-section locations (XS 1, XS 2, and XS 3).\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Manning's Roughness Coefficient (n):** 0.03 used for all cross-sections\n*   **Design Flow Rates (Q):** 16.49 cfs (25-Year event), 21.97 cfs (100-Year event) across all sections\n*   **Maximum 100-Year Velocity:** 8.70 ft/s (at cross-section XS 3)\n*   **Maximum 100-Year Depth:** 0.48 ft (at cross-section XS 3)\n*   **Benchmark 1:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   **Benchmark 2:** Mag Nail in Asphalt, Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   **Finished Floor Elevations (FFE):** Bldg. 5 = 683.0 ft, Bldg. 6 = 683.0 ft\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 7: site plan — Multi-family development plan view**\n    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, grading contours, drainage easements, and the specific locations of the cross-section cut lines (XS 1, XS 2, XS 3) relative to buildings 5 and 6 and existing retaining walls.\n*   **Blocks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6: diagrams — Cross-section profile graphs**\n    Use VISION to examine the channel profiles, side slopes, and plotted water surface elevations for cross-sections XS 1, XS 2, and XS 3 under both 25-year and 100-year storm conditions. \n*   **Blocks 14, 15, 16, 17, 19, 20: tables — Hydraulic data tables**\n    READ for exact hydraulic parameters corresponding to each cross-section graph, including Depth (ft), Flow Rate Q (cfs), Area (sqft), Velocity (ft/s), Wetted Perimeter Wp (ft), Critical Depth Yc (ft), Top Width (ft), and Energy Head (ft).\n*   **Block 21: text_block — Hydraulic modeling note**\n    READ to verify the Manning's roughness coefficient used in the calculations.\n*   **Block 12: notes — Benchmarks**\n    READ for exact elevation values and physical descriptions of the survey benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2).\n*   **Block 8: notes — Legend**\n    READ for definitions of line types and symbols used in the plan view, such as existing/proposed contours, storm drain lines, and limits of construction.\n*   **Block 9: notes — Construction and landscape notes**\n    READ for curb construction grading instructions (catch curb vs. spill curb) and references to the tree list.\n*   **Blocks 10, 11, 13, 18: various — Boilerplate, Title Block & Administrative**\n    READ for the legal description of the property, project title (Valley View Townhomes), engineer seal (Bleyl Engineering), standard utility/Texas 811 warnings, and city submittal disclaimers.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}}}
