{"level":30,"time":1778246255479,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018JwLRYdfAPBFwzcoHT9op7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — General Notes\n     2→\n     3→Comprehensive general notes, sequence of construction, and project legend.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides a comprehensive collection of general notes, standard specifications, utility capacity approvals, and the site's legend for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish project-wide regulatory constraints, outline the construction sequence, and document the City of Austin's confirmation of sufficient water and wastewater service.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Project Scope: 39 Condo Units, 28 Living Unit Equivalents (LUE), 3.59 Acres\n    11→*   Water Demand: 60 gpm (Estimated Peak Hour), requiring connection to existing 8-inch main\n    12→*   Fire Flow Requirement: 1,500 gpm\n    13→*   Wastewater Flow: 20 gpm (Estimated Peak Wet Weather), requiring connection to existing 8-inch gravity main\n    14→*   Benchmark 1 (Mag Nail in Asphalt): Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n    15→*   Benchmark 2 (Mag Nail in Asphalt): Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n    16→*   Fire Department Paving Requirement: 80,000 lb. live-vehicle load capability\n    17→*   Fire Apparatus Vertical Clearance: 14 feet\n    18→*   Fire Hydrant Placement: Center of 4-inch opening must be at least 18 inches above finished grade\n    19→*   Electric Transmission Clearances: No digging/grading/trees within 25 feet of transmission structures; 20-foot clearance for aerial equipment/staging\n    20→*   Transmission Easement Road Requirement: Must support a 46,000 lb. tandem axle\n    21→*   ROW Work Zone Peak Hours: 6:00 a.m. to 9:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m.\n    22→*   ROW Violation Fee: $250 per specific violation type\n    23→\n    24→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    25→\n    26→*   **Blocks 12 & 15:** Austin Water \"Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\" approval letters for water and wastewater. READ the block content for the approved project specifications, demand calculations, and the specific existing 8-inch mains designated for the tap.\n    27→*   **Block 17:** Benchmark data. READ for exact elevations and locations to be used as control points for the site.\n    28→*   **Block 19:** Sequence of Construction. READ the block content for the strict 13-step chronological order of operations, particularly regarding when erosion controls and pond grading must occur.\n    29→*   **Block 6:** Project Legend. READ for the text descriptions of utilities, and use VISION to familiarize yourself with the symbol shapes (e.g., property lines, utility lines, tree protection zones) to interpret subsequent plan sheets accurately.\n    30→*   **Block 9:** Fire Department requirements. READ for strict design constraints regarding emergency access, pavement load ratings, and fire hydrant placement.\n    31→*   **Block 16:** Electric Transmission Notes. READ for critical safety clearances, structural load requirements for roads in easements, and barricade rules required by Austin Energy.\n    32→*   **Block 7:** Right-of-Way Management Standard Notes. READ for traffic control rules, restricted working hours, and permit violation penalties.\n    33→*   **Block 8:** General Construction Notes and Developer Information. READ to identify the property owner (WM 41 Austin RE LLC) and general engineering responsibilities.\n    34→*   **Blocks 14 & 18:** Electric Notes and Austin Energy standard requirements. READ for tree pruning, easement access, and code compliance constraints.\n    35→*   **Block 11:** Site Plan Release Notes. READ for general City of Austin demolition and utility relocation policies. \n    36→*   **Block 20:** Legal Description. READ to verify the exact lot and subdivision references (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision).\n    37→*   **Blocks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 13:** Various administrative and boilerplate content (Title block info, Engineer's seal, Texas 811 logo, ADA disclaimers). READ the block content briefly for project tracking metadata, otherwise these can be safely skipped.\n    38→\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→- `block-6.md` — table: Legend for existing utility and feature symbols used on the site plan.\n    42→- `block-9.md` — text_block: Standard notes for managing construction within the Right-Of-Way, covering violations, permitting, t\n    43→- `block-10.md` — text_block: List of 13 steps detailing the construction sequence, from installing temporary erosion controls to \n    44→- `block-13.md` — text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines a\n    45→- `block-14.md` — text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing wastewater main has adequate capacit\n    46→- `block-16.md` — text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for\n    47→- `block-17.md` — text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion c\n    48→- `block-19.md` — text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements \n    49→\n    50→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    51→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bbc8513-4a76-42d1-91f8-a8d89a310ed5","uuid":"07deb2aa-a5a2-411e-b897-aa204e72d681","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — General Notes\n\nComprehensive general notes, sequence of construction, and project legend.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides a comprehensive collection of general notes, standard specifications, utility capacity approvals, and the site's legend for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish project-wide regulatory constraints, outline the construction sequence, and document the City of Austin's confirmation of sufficient water and wastewater service.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Project Scope: 39 Condo Units, 28 Living Unit Equivalents (LUE), 3.59 Acres\n*   Water Demand: 60 gpm (Estimated Peak Hour), requiring connection to existing 8-inch main\n*   Fire Flow Requirement: 1,500 gpm\n*   Wastewater Flow: 20 gpm (Estimated Peak Wet Weather), requiring connection to existing 8-inch gravity main\n*   Benchmark 1 (Mag Nail in Asphalt): Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark 2 (Mag Nail in Asphalt): Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Fire Department Paving Requirement: 80,000 lb. live-vehicle load capability\n*   Fire Apparatus Vertical Clearance: 14 feet\n*   Fire Hydrant Placement: Center of 4-inch opening must be at least 18 inches above finished grade\n*   Electric Transmission Clearances: No digging/grading/trees within 25 feet of transmission structures; 20-foot clearance for aerial equipment/staging\n*   Transmission Easement Road Requirement: Must support a 46,000 lb. tandem axle\n*   ROW Work Zone Peak Hours: 6:00 a.m. to 9:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m.\n*   ROW Violation Fee: $250 per specific violation type\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Blocks 12 & 15:** Austin Water \"Suitable and Sufficient Existing Service\" approval letters for water and wastewater. READ the block content for the approved project specifications, demand calculations, and the specific existing 8-inch mains designated for the tap.\n*   **Block 17:** Benchmark data. READ for exact elevations and locations to be used as control points for the site.\n*   **Block 19:** Sequence of Construction. READ the block content for the strict 13-step chronological order of operations, particularly regarding when erosion controls and pond grading must occur.\n*   **Block 6:** Project Legend. READ for the text descriptions of utilities, and use VISION to familiarize yourself with the symbol shapes (e.g., property lines, utility lines, tree protection zones) to interpret subsequent plan sheets accurately.\n*   **Block 9:** Fire Department requirements. READ for strict design constraints regarding emergency access, pavement load ratings, and fire hydrant placement.\n*   **Block 16:** Electric Transmission Notes. READ for critical safety clearances, structural load requirements for roads in easements, and barricade rules required by Austin Energy.\n*   **Block 7:** Right-of-Way Management Standard Notes. READ for traffic control rules, restricted working hours, and permit violation penalties.\n*   **Block 8:** General Construction Notes and Developer Information. READ to identify the property owner (WM 41 Austin RE LLC) and general engineering responsibilities.\n*   **Blocks 14 & 18:** Electric Notes and Austin Energy standard requirements. READ for tree pruning, easement access, and code compliance constraints.\n*   **Block 11:** Site Plan Release Notes. READ for general City of Austin demolition and utility relocation policies. \n*   **Block 20:** Legal Description. READ to verify the exact lot and subdivision references (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision).\n*   **Blocks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 13:** Various administrative and boilerplate content (Title block info, Engineer's seal, Texas 811 logo, ADA disclaimers). READ the block content briefly for project tracking metadata, otherwise these can be safely skipped.\n\n---\n\n- `block-6.md` — table: Legend for existing utility and feature symbols used on the site plan.\n- `block-9.md` — text_block: Standard notes for managing construction within the Right-Of-Way, covering violations, permitting, t\n- `block-10.md` — text_block: List of 13 steps detailing the construction sequence, from installing temporary erosion controls to \n- `block-13.md` — text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines a\n- `block-14.md` — text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing wastewater main has adequate capacit\n- `block-16.md` — text_block: Copy of a letter from Austin Water confirming that the existing water main has adequate capacity for\n- `block-17.md` — text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion c\n- `block-19.md` — text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements \n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246255481,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C1tnMJGfeiHEjys6mNLPAW","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 22 — Construction Details 1\n     2→\n     3→Construction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains standard construction details, primarily City of Austin (COA) standard specifications, for site civil elements. Its primary purpose is to provide the required dimensions, reinforcement, and installation procedures for curbs, gutters, sidewalks, driveways, bicycle parking, and bumper curbs.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Driveway Thickness:** Passenger vehicle parking lots = 150 mm (6\") min.; All others = 175 mm (7\") min.\n    11→*   **Driveway Reinforcement:** 125 mm (5\") min. concrete with one layer 13M (#4) bars placed at max 450 mm (18\") O.C. both directions.\n    12→*   **Driveway Allowable Grades:** >1500 ADT = 5% max; 500-1500 ADT = 6% max; <500 ADT = 8% (up to 15% max for emergency access).\n    13→*   **Type I Driveway Slope:** Elevation typically min. 150 mm (6\") plus 20 mm/m (2\"/100') over distance.\n    14→*   **Sidewalk Reinforcement:** 152x152xMW9xMW9 welded wire fabric or one layer 10M (#3) bars max 450 mm (18\") C.C. both directions.\n    15→*   **Bicycle Rack Base Plates:** 6.35 mm (1/4\") plates, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 low carbon prime steel.\n    16→*   **Bicycle Rack Siting:** Must be within 7.32m (24') of main building entry; minimum clearance from utilities is 0.9m (3').\n    17→*   **Bumper Curb Concrete:** Class \"A\" in accordance with Item 403S.\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 1: diagram — Sidewalk Dowel Detail (COA 432S-1)**. Shows dowel specifications for sidewalk expansion joints. Use VISION for spatial layout and dimensions.\n    22→*   **Block 2: diagram — Curb and Gutter Section (COA 430S-1)**. Displays laydown and catch curb profiles. Use VISION to examine curb slope requirements and radii.\n    23→*   **Block 3: diagram — Sidewalk Plan and Section (COA 432S-1)**. Shows sidewalk layout with adjacent curb. READ for exact reinforcement requirements (WWM or #3 bars) and VISION for joint spacing layout.\n    24→*   **Block 4: table and text — Type II Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Contains structural specifications and layout rules for driveways. READ for exact driveway thickness, reinforcement specs, allowable grade tables, and general driveway notes.\n    25→*   **Block 5: diagram — Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail (COA 430S-3)**. Elevation and cross-section of the dowel joint. Use VISION to examine the positioning of the dowel sleeve and joint dimensions.\n    26→*   **Block 6: diagram — Type I Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Plan and section views for standard driveways. Use VISION for geometric layout and READ for specific slope calculation notes.\n    27→*   **Block 7: diagram — Sidewalk Over Utility Service Lines (COA 432S-1)**. Details the PVC pipe sleeve and sand cushion arrangement. Use VISION to verify utility crossing protection details.\n    28→*   **Block 8: diagram — Class III Style Bicycle Parking (COA 710S-1)**. Rack fabrication details. VISION for rack dimensions and READ for base plate material thickness and steel grade requirements.\n    29→*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n    30→*   **Block 10: diagram — Bicycle Rack Installation (COA 710S-4)**. Concrete anchor details. Use VISION for mechanical expansion anchor bolt setup and READ the note regarding anti-theft bolt deformation.\n    31→*   **Block 11: diagram — Parking Lot Bumper Curb (COA 439S-1)**. Plan, section, and profile of concrete wheel stops. Use VISION for rebar placement/dimensions and READ for the required concrete class specification.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→- `block-11.md` — diagram: City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type II Driveway. It includes a table for allowable grades\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bbc8513-4a76-42d1-91f8-a8d89a310ed5","uuid":"dfe70bdd-6431-4956-b633-0147ae46e987","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-22/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 22 — Construction Details 1\n\nConstruction details for curbs, sidewalks, driveways, and bicycle parking.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains standard construction details, primarily City of Austin (COA) standard specifications, for site civil elements. Its primary purpose is to provide the required dimensions, reinforcement, and installation procedures for curbs, gutters, sidewalks, driveways, bicycle parking, and bumper curbs.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Driveway Thickness:** Passenger vehicle parking lots = 150 mm (6\") min.; All others = 175 mm (7\") min.\n*   **Driveway Reinforcement:** 125 mm (5\") min. concrete with one layer 13M (#4) bars placed at max 450 mm (18\") O.C. both directions.\n*   **Driveway Allowable Grades:** >1500 ADT = 5% max; 500-1500 ADT = 6% max; <500 ADT = 8% (up to 15% max for emergency access).\n*   **Type I Driveway Slope:** Elevation typically min. 150 mm (6\") plus 20 mm/m (2\"/100') over distance.\n*   **Sidewalk Reinforcement:** 152x152xMW9xMW9 welded wire fabric or one layer 10M (#3) bars max 450 mm (18\") C.C. both directions.\n*   **Bicycle Rack Base Plates:** 6.35 mm (1/4\") plates, ASTM A-36 1010-1018 low carbon prime steel.\n*   **Bicycle Rack Siting:** Must be within 7.32m (24') of main building entry; minimum clearance from utilities is 0.9m (3').\n*   **Bumper Curb Concrete:** Class \"A\" in accordance with Item 403S.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Sidewalk Dowel Detail (COA 432S-1)**. Shows dowel specifications for sidewalk expansion joints. Use VISION for spatial layout and dimensions.\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Curb and Gutter Section (COA 430S-1)**. Displays laydown and catch curb profiles. Use VISION to examine curb slope requirements and radii.\n*   **Block 3: diagram — Sidewalk Plan and Section (COA 432S-1)**. Shows sidewalk layout with adjacent curb. READ for exact reinforcement requirements (WWM or #3 bars) and VISION for joint spacing layout.\n*   **Block 4: table and text — Type II Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Contains structural specifications and layout rules for driveways. READ for exact driveway thickness, reinforcement specs, allowable grade tables, and general driveway notes.\n*   **Block 5: diagram — Curb Expansion Joint Dowel Detail (COA 430S-3)**. Elevation and cross-section of the dowel joint. Use VISION to examine the positioning of the dowel sleeve and joint dimensions.\n*   **Block 6: diagram — Type I Driveway (COA 433S-2)**. Plan and section views for standard driveways. Use VISION for geometric layout and READ for specific slope calculation notes.\n*   **Block 7: diagram — Sidewalk Over Utility Service Lines (COA 432S-1)**. Details the PVC pipe sleeve and sand cushion arrangement. Use VISION to verify utility crossing protection details.\n*   **Block 8: diagram — Class III Style Bicycle Parking (COA 710S-1)**. Rack fabrication details. VISION for rack dimensions and READ for base plate material thickness and steel grade requirements.\n*   **Block 9: diagram — Furnishing Location for Bicycle Racks (COA 710S-6C)**. Shows linear and parallel rack installation footprints. READ for strict spacing rules, utility clearances, and building entry proximity limits; VISION for spatial arrangement diagrams.\n*   **Block 10: diagram — Bicycle Rack Installation (COA 710S-4)**. Concrete anchor details. Use VISION for mechanical expansion anchor bolt setup and READ the note regarding anti-theft bolt deformation.\n*   **Block 11: diagram — Parking Lot Bumper Curb (COA 439S-1)**. Plan, section, and profile of concrete wheel stops. Use VISION for rebar placement/dimensions and READ for the required concrete class specification.\n\n---\n\n- `block-11.md` — diagram: City of Austin standard detail 433S-2 for Type II Driveway. It includes a table for allowable grades\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246255482,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Qkr1AqzsQWfDQh7BM59t3","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bbc8513-4a76-42d1-91f8-a8d89a310ed5","uuid":"c859bb28-addb-4fb2-8cc9-ae9db66d7e84","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
