ding Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   **Bldg 1**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 687.50\n*   **Bldg 2**: 4,830 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 3**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 4**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 5**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 6**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 7**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.00\n*   **Bldg 8**: 4,997 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **ADA Ramp Maximum Slope**: 8.33%\n*   **Level Landing Maximum Slope**: 2%\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n*   **Block 7**: Plan legend detailing line types and symbols for contours, limits of construction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778246255523,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011n8ohvgfKoYs24s6HNtiwY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n     2→\n     3→Plan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n    11→* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n    12→* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n    13→* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n    14→* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n    15→* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n    16→* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n    17→* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n    18→* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n    19→* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n    20→* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    23→\n    24→* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n    25→* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n    26→* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n    27→* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n    28→* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n    29→* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n    30→* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n    31→* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","uuid":"26dc244d-21bf-4fb5-8409-1490ad75cc71","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n\nPlan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
