/guide.md:    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/guide.md:  READ for exact elevation values and locations of Benchmarks 1 and 2.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:This sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:    *Use VISION to trace drainage flow paths, examine the spatial relationship between infrastructure and building footprints, and READ for specific pipe dimensions, slopes, and structure elevations.*\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:    Details the vertical control points used for the site plan, specifying the elevations of BM #1 and BM #2.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:    *READ for exact survey elevation references.*\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md:    Defines the line types and symbols used on the drawing, such as existing/proposed contours, spot elevations, and limits of construction. It also notes maximum slopes for ADA ramps and landings.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:*   Use VISION to examine the spatial layout and relationships between pond elements. READ for specific spot elevations (e.g., Top of Biofiltration Media at 672.00) and pipe specifications (e.g., 24\" HDPE @ 1.35%).\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:*   READ the block content for exact storage volumes at given elevations and to verify the required vs. provided WQV elevations (675.57 vs 675.65).\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-15/guide.md:*   READ the block content for peak outflow rates (up to 15.60 cfs) at specific event elevations.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:*   **Outfall Weir**: 4.5' wide at elevation 675.65'\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md:    Cross-sectional profile detailing the pond's left and right concrete retaining walls, pipe inlet, rock flow spreader, rock rip-rap, and biofiltration media elevations.\n/verce