ed ground surfaces, and READ for exact flowline elevations, lengths, and the 52' restraint dimension.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/guide.md:* **Block 4**: notes — Benchmarks. Provides the elevation reference points for the site. READ the block content for exact elevations and datum (NAVD 88).\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-23/guide.md:*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md:*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md:*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:    Side elevation view of the grinder pump station. Use VISION to understand the vertical layout of the pumps, 10' min fiberglass well, and lifting chains. READ for specific component sizes (2\" valves, 3\" vent, 12\" concrete fill base).\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:    Shows plan and elevatio