8.52' and 681.08').\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-23/guide.md:*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md:*   **Block 2**: diagram — Section A-A view showing longitudinal vertical elevation. Use VISION for final grade relationships, concrete pad locations, and support stand configurations.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/guide.md:*   **Block 1**: diagram — Section B-B view showing transverse vertical elevation. Use VISION for alternative structural details and vertical clearance perspectives.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:    Side elevation view of the grinder pump station. Use VISION to understand the vertical layout of the pumps, 10' min fiberglass well, and lifting chains. READ for specific component sizes (2\" valves, 3\" vent, 12\" concrete fill base).\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-27/guide.md:    Shows plan and elevation views of standard, U-shaped, and bench inverts. Use VISION for the geometry of the flowlines. READ for specific benching criteria (18\" min for 30\"-36\" pipes) and the 1:12 slope requirement.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:This sheet contains the Addressing Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, illustrating the layout, numbering, and finished floor elevations of the proposed residential buildings. Its primary purpose is to define the unit addressing scheme, building square footages, and spatial relationships between the structures, property boundaries, and existing site features like easements.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:*   **Block 1: drawing** — Main site addressing plan showing the townhome layout, individual unit locations, building dimensions, and property lines. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of buildings, unit addressing sequences, finished floor elevations (FFEs), and locations of surrounding easements and utility infrastructure. \n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:*   **Block 2: notes** — Information regarding the primary elevation control points for the project. READ the block content for the exact benchmark elevations, datum (NAVD 88), and point descriptions.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md:    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-37/guide.md:*   **Block 3: diagram — City of Austin Tree Planting Detail**: Comprehensive cross-section and specification list for new tree installations. READ the block content for extensive text instructions covering rootball preparation, acceptable pruning, hardware specifics (Arborbrace webbing, Stakesafe protectors), and soil settling methods. Use VISION to examine the 4'-6\" stake height above ground, the 3x rootball width pit dimensions, and the rootball elevation relative to the finished grade.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md:* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
