 pole symbol, there is a proposed tree center (indicated by a small '+' symbol). The distance between the center of the utility pole symbol and the center of this tree is visually shorter than the \"10\" foot segment on the graphic scale. Additionally, the drawn canopy circle for this tree, which is associated with a label containing an **\"M\"** (which the KEY NOTES define as \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"), overlaps the location of the utility pole."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87ad5ecd-4cf7-4b80-b04f-ff327308d79b","uuid":"0357f00a-3774-434d-84e8-da004aafa3cd","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here is the information regarding overhead electric utility poles and tree placement:\n\n**Locations of Overhead Electric Utility Poles:**\n\nUtility poles are identified on this plan by a symbol consisting of a small circle with an \"X\" or cross inside it, located along a line designated for overhead electric utilities.\n\nLooking at the southern (bottom) boundary of the site plan, there is a line clearly labeled **\"- OHE -\"** running horizontally from left to right. Along this line, there are three distinct utility pole symbols:\n\n1.  **Bottom Left:** One pole symbol is located on the \"- OHE -\" line near the southwest corner of the property lines shown.\n2.  **Bottom Middle:** A second pole symbol is located on the \"- OHE -\" line roughly midway across the bottom boundary.\n3.  **Bottom Right:** A third pole symbol is located on the \"- OHE -\" line near the southeast corner of the property lines shown.\n\n**Trees Positioned Within Approximately 10 Feet of Poles:**\n\nTo determine a 10-foot distance, I am referencing the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner labeled **\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"**, specifically looking at the visual width of the segment from \"0\" to \"10\".\n\nAnalyzing the area around each identified pole:\n\n*   **Pole 1 (Bottom Left):** The nearest trees