{"level":30,"time":1778246413805,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VW5Y0EBRXDQWMTMCNP18J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014DxrGyjAKb2ExgkJjP7LhY","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary area within 15 lateral feet of OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees marked as 'M' (Mitigation) and 'P' (Parking Buffer) are positioned 5-10 feet from the overhead electric (OHE) line on the landscape plan, which falls within the < 15 lateral feet distribution restriction zone requiring utility-compatible species only. However, the landscape plan does not identify which specific species are labeled with these symbols, and the plant list on Sheet 35 does not indicate which of the four proposed shade/ornamental species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are the 'M' and 'P' trees. Without species identification linked to tree symbol locations, and without ECM Appendix F utility-compatible designations, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed trees marked 'M' and 'P' are positioned 5-10 feet from the OHE line. Landscape plan legend defines 'M' and 'P' as functional categories but provides no cross-reference to botanical species. Plant list on Sheet 35 lists four tree species but does not indicate which are 'M', 'P', 'SY', or 'PL' trees.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that only utility-compatible trees are permitted within 15 feet of distribution conductors. The plan shows trees in this zone but provides no verifiable link between the tree symbols on the drawing and the species listed in the schedule, and no documentation of ECM Appendix F UC status. This creates an unresolvable verification gap—we cannot confirm the species of the nearby trees, and therefore cannot confirm their UC status.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement or transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are present on the site. The grading plan shows only 5-foot electric easements and broader utility/drainage easements; no transmission-level infrastructure is depicted. Therefore, this requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of grading plan (Sheet 11) confirmed no transmission easements are labeled or shown. All electric easements are 5 feet wide, consistent with distribution-level facilities. Facts.md lists only distribution and utility easements, with no transmission infrastructure noted.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are present or proposed. The site shows distribution-only infrastructure per the easement widths and voltage classification. The applicability gate is not met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary area within 25 lateral feet of OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are positioned within 25 feet of the overhead electric line. The requirement prohibits large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) within this zone. However, the landscape plan does not differentiate which trees are 'large trees' (40+ feet mature height). Sheet 35 lists species with their container size specifications but does not document mature heights per ECM Appendix F. Without mature height documentation linked to tree locations on the plan, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed trees at 5-10 feet from OHE line (within the 25-foot zone). Landscape plan symbols 'M' and 'P' are not differentiated by size or mature height. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 shows container specifications (100 GAL., 45 GAL., etc.) and planting heights (8'-16'), but not ECM Appendix F mature heights.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates specific action (prohibit large trees ≥40 ft) within a specific distance zone (25 feet). The plan shows trees in the zone but provides no documentation of mature heights per the controlling standard (ECM Appendix F). Without this documentation, we cannot verify whether large trees are or are not present in the restricted zone.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities are present on the site; therefore this requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan shows no transmission easements or transmission-level infrastructure.","reasoning":"Applicability gate not met—transmission facilities are not present.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on the site. The grading plan shows only 5-foot electric easements and broader utility/drainage easements. Therefore, this requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed no transmission easement boundaries are shown on grading plan. Only 5-foot electric and broader utility easements are depicted.","reasoning":"Applicability gate is not met—transmission easement is not present on site.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary area along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric poles are shown on the landscape plan as circular symbols with 'x' marks along the OHE line on the southern boundary. Trees marked 'M' and 'P' are positioned 5-10 feet from the OHE line. The requirement prohibits trees within 10 lateral feet of utility poles. However, the landscape plan does not provide exact dimensions from tree trunk centers to pole centerlines, and the 'M' and 'P' tree species are not identified on the plan. Without exact measurements and species identification, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check identified utility poles on the OHE line and estimated trees at 5-10 feet away. However, these are visual estimates from the plan drawing at scale, not dimensioned measurements. The tree symbols are not linked to specific species on the landscape drawing.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates a 10-foot minimum distance from poles. The plan shows trees in the approximate 5-10 feet range, which may or may not comply depending on exact measurements from trunk centers to pole centers. Without dimensioned measurements and identification of which species are in this proximity, verification is not possible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows only underground electrical infrastructure including transformers, pull boxes, and underground distribution lines. No pad-mounted electric equipment is visible on the site plan, electrical plan, or landscape plan. Therefore, this requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 guide states that the electrical plan details 'underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes.' Vision checks of the site plans show no pad-mounted transformer or equipment symbols on the landscape or utility plans.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when pad-mounted equipment is present. The site shows underground-only electrical infrastructure, making this applicability gate unmet.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical plan shows underground pull boxes and distribution lines only. No duct banks, vaults, or other underground electric equipment requiring the 5-foot clearance are identified as separate entities from the general underground distribution system. The requirement typically applies to isolated underground equipment. This applicability is marginal, but no evidence of applicable equipment triggering this requirement is present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 describes underground electric lines, transformers, and pull boxes as part of the distribution system. No separate underground equipment locations (vaults, isolated transformers) are identified.","reasoning":"The requirement applies when discrete underground electric equipment is proposed. The site shows integrated underground distribution lines and pull boxes but no isolated equipment that would trigger this specific 5-foot clearance requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No discrete underground electric equipment (vaults, isolated transformers, equipment boxes) requiring root barriers is identified on the electrical plan. The site shows only underground distribution lines and pull boxes integrated into the utility system, not isolated equipment that would trigger the 20-foot root barrier requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground lines and pull boxes as part of the integrated distribution system. Landscape plan shows no root barrier details or isolated underground equipment requiring root barrier protection.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when trees are within 20 feet of discrete underground electric equipment. The site shows distribution-level lines rather than isolated equipment, so the applicability gate is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan near overhead electric facilities (southern boundary area)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed near the overhead electric line on the landscape plan are labeled with functional designations ('M' for Mitigation, 'P' for Parking Buffer) but the landscape plan does not directly identify the botanical or common names of these specific trees. The plant list on Sheet 35 specifies species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but does not cross-reference which species are labeled 'M' or 'P' on the actual drawing. A reviewer must reference multiple sheets and cannot directly correlate tree symbols on the landscape plan to specific species. Provide a clear plant legend on the landscape plan that identifies the species of each labeled tree, or clearly reference the plant schedule with species names linked to drawing symbols.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan legend (Sheet 31, Block 5) defines 'M', 'P', 'SY', 'PL' as functional categories (Mitigation Tree, Parking Buffer Point Tree, etc.) but does not list botanical or common names. Plant list (Sheet 35, Blocks 11, 17) specifies species and quantities but does not indicate which trees are 'M', 'P', 'SY', or 'PL' on the landscape drawing.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates clear identification of tree species on the plant legend or plant schedule for trees near electric facilities. While the information exists across two sheets, the landscape plan itself—where trees are depicted—does not include legible species information. This is a documentation deficiency requiring clarification on the plan drawing itself.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan near overhead electric facilities (southern boundary area)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan does not differentiate or designate large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) from smaller trees. Tree symbols on the plan are marked by functional category ('M', 'P', 'SY', 'PL') but include no notation, color-coding, or legend entry identifying which trees are 'large' (≥40 feet mature height). The plant schedule on Sheet 35 does not document mature heights per ECM Appendix F. Large trees positioned within 25 feet of overhead distribution facilities require specific clearance compliance; without identification of large trees on the plan, such compliance cannot be verified. Provide a clear designation (notation, color, legend symbol) on the landscape plan identifying trees with mature heights of 40 feet or greater per ECM Appendix F.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Tree symbols on landscape plan use functional designations ('M', 'P', etc.) only. No size classes, height notations, or legend entries distinguish large trees from others. Sheet 35 plant schedule shows container sizes and planting heights but does not list ECM Appendix F mature heights.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that large trees be identifiable on the plan to allow verification of clearances from overhead facilities. The current plan provides no such distinction. This is a documentation deficiency requiring addition of large tree designations to either the landscape plan legend or the tree symbols themselves.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary area along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan does not provide dimension lines or measurements from tree trunk centers to the overhead electric line or from the OHE line to utility poles. While pole symbols are shown on the OHE line, no dimensions or calculations are provided to demonstrate that clearances are measured from the outside conductor (not pole centerline). Without dimensional evidence on the plan, the measurement methodology cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows OHE line and pole symbols but contains no dimension lines, distance callouts, or measurements from trees to conductors or poles.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies measurement methodology (from trunk center to outside conductor). Plans must either show dimensioned proof or provide calculations/notes confirming proper methodology. The absence of any measurements prevents verification that the correct methodology was used.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary area along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan does not provide dimension lines or measurements from tree locations. Without dimensioned evidence showing whether measurements originate at tree trunk centers (planting locations) or at projected canopy edges, the measurement methodology cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan contains no dimension lines, distance callouts, or analytical notes specifying measurement origins for tree clearances.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies that measurements must originate from tree trunk centers, not canopy edges. The absence of dimensioned evidence prevents verification of methodology.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan (entire site)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows the overhead electric (OHE) line and poles along the southern boundary. However, the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows only underground electrical infrastructure; the two plans do not clearly cross-reference or align. While the OHE line is present on the landscape plan, a reviewer must cross-reference between sheets to verify that all overhead conductors and poles are depicted on the landscape plan. The electrical plan should be referenced or overlaid on the landscape plan to provide complete clarity on overhead facility locations and ensure all conductors are shown relative to tree locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) displays OHE line with pole symbols. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows only underground infrastructure. No note on either plan cross-references the electrical plan to the landscape plan or vice versa.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that trees be shown in relation to overhead facilities with sufficient clarity to verify clearances. While the OHE line is present, the lack of explicit cross-reference between the underground-focused electrical plan and the landscape plan leaves open the possibility that some overhead facilities are not depicted. The plans should clearly state that Sheet 21 (electrical) covers underground only, and that overhead facilities are shown only on Sheet 31 (landscape).","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary area within 15 lateral feet of OHE line and near utility poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are positioned within restricted clearance zones (5-10 feet from the OHE line and utility poles along the southern boundary). The plans do not provide evidence of Austin Energy written approval for these placements. No approval letters, correspondence, or notes in the submitted site plan documents indicate that Austin Energy has authorized the tree placement in these restricted zones. If trees within prohibited zones are proposed, documented written approval from Austin Energy must be provided on or attached to the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of landscape plan (Sheet 31), electrical plan (Sheet 21), and general notes (examined across available sheets) revealed no approval letters, correspondence, or notes from Austin Energy authorizing tree placement in the < 15 feet distribution or < 10 feet pole clearance zones.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates that any trees proposed within prohibited zones must include documented Austin Energy written approval. The absence of such documentation, combined with evidence that trees are positioned in these zones, indicates that either the trees must be relocated to comply zones, or approval must be obtained and submitted.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c88cf1-2078-476d-9e24-f9a661c6a8fa","uuid":"fba0b923-f065-4a57-8537-38646558d819"}
