{"level":30,"time":1778246440610,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AYPePeQuMM5aWfxtW1r8xr","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (which is labeled as Sheet **28 of 35** in the bottom right corner, not Sheet 31 as noted in the prompt), here is the exact information regarding the tree symbols and the legend.\n\n### Legend Definitions\nThe definitions for the letter codes used to label trees are located on the right side of the page, directly below the \"KEY NOTES\" section. Transcribed exactly as they appear, they are:\n\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n*(Note: While \"P\" is listed in the legend, a visual scan of the plan does not readily show any trees labeled with a standalone \"P\" on this specific sheet.)*\n\n### Graphical Tree Symbols on the Plan\nThe plan view utilizes circular graphics to represent trees, which feature different center marks. These are often, but not always, paired with the letter codes defined above. \n\n**CRITICAL NOTE:** There is **no legend on this page** that explicitly defines the meaning of the graphical center marks (the crosses versus the dots/small circles). \n\nBased strictly on visual observation of the plan, the symbols appear as follows:\n\n*   **Circles with a cross (+):** There are circular tree symbols containing a cross or \"plus\" mark in the center. \n    *   Where labeled, these are frequently tagged with **M** (visible along the top edge and bottom right edge) and **SY** (visible along the left edge).\n*   **Circles with a small inner circle/dot:** There are circular tree symbols containing a smaller, distinct circle or dot in the center. \n    *   Where labeled, these are frequently tagged with **PL** (visible along the top interior edge near the parking area)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bd4df49-5a3c-4afa-8eeb-b16b6883780f","uuid":"cda6aaec-6a60-4ca3-a77f-1866f0e5e1d4","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (which is labeled as Sheet **28 of 35** in the bottom right corner, not Sheet 31 as noted in the prompt), here is the exact information regarding the tree symbols and the legend.\n\n### Legend Definitions\nThe definitions for the letter codes used to label trees are located on the right side of the page, directly below the \"KEY NOTES\" section. Transcribed exactly as they appear, they are:\n\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n*(Note: While \"P\" is listed in the legend, a visual scan of the plan does not readily show any trees labeled with a standalone \"P\" on this specific sheet.)*\n\n### Graphical Tree Symbols on the Plan\nThe plan view utilizes circular graphics to represent trees, which feature different center marks. These are often, but not always, paired with the letter codes defined above. \n\n**CRITICAL NOTE:** There is **no legend on this page** that explicitly defines the meaning of the graphical center marks (the crosses versus the dots/small circles). \n\nBased strictly on visual observation of the plan, the symbols appear as follows:\n\n*   **Circles with a cross (+):** There are circular tree symbols containing a cross or \"plus\" mark in the center. \n    *   Where labeled, these are frequently tagged with **M** (visible along the top edge and bottom right edge) and **SY** (visible along the left edge).\n*   **Circles with a small inner circle/dot:** There are circular tree symbols containing a smaller, distinct circle or dot in the center. \n    *   Where labeled, these are frequently tagged with **PL** (visible along the top interior edge near the parking area)."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778246444337,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VXRWQ9ZMF3692DSZP4145","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze what I've gathered so far:\n\n1. **Project**: Valley View Townhomes - 39 multi-family townhome units across 8 buildings on 2.16 acres\n2. **Overhead Electric Facilities**: CONFIRMED present on the site\n   - Western boundary (Valley View Road): OHE line runs along western property line\n   - Northern boundary: OHE line runs along northern property line  \n   - Southern boundary: OHE line runs along southern boundary\n   - Utility poles are shown at these locations\n\n3. **Key Findings from Vision Checks**:\n   - Buildings 1 and 2 are approximately 25.8-26.1 feet from the western property boundary where the OHE line is located\n   - Fences are shown (pond perimeter fence in northeast, wood fence on eastern boundary) but NO specific distance dimensions are provided between fences and OHE lines\n   - Retaining walls are present along southern, eastern, and northeast boundaries. NO specific distance dimensions are provided between walls and OHE lines\n   - The landscape plan Sheet 31 does NOT show the OHE lines on western and northern boundaries (visibility issue or drawing limitation)\n\n4. **Critical Observations**:\n   - The site plan shows OHE lines on Sheets 4 (existing conditions survey) and 9 (main site plan), but overhead electric conductor elevations and clearance verification are MISSING\n   - No building elevation sheets are included showing vertical clearances from overhead conductors\n   - No profile sections showing clearance dimensions from conductors to buildings, fences, walls, or other site features\n   - No surveyed pole locations or conductor elevations documented\n   - The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) addresses UNDERGROUND electrical utilities (transformer