uildings are positioned roughly 25+ feet from the property boundary where overhead lines exist, so no direct conflicts appear. Water meter clearances from service drops aren't shown or documented. Similarly, water line clearances from distribution lines lack verification. Foundation placement near property lines requires examination.\n\nBuildings maintain more than 5 feet of clearance from the property line. A registered surveyor's documentation of pole locations and mid-span clearances is missing entirely, which is a critical gap. The overhead lines run along boundaries rather than crossing roadways at angles. Only one overhead line routing is documented per boundary. No marquee signage is proposed. Underground conversion for new power poles is shown in the electrical design. Decorative lighting clearances from overhead lines aren't documented in the plans. Trees throughout the site lack species identification, particularly those within 10 feet of overhead lines—the landscape plan doesn't reference the utility-compatible species list required by code. Meter locations appear on the drawings but without any obstruction or clearance analysis to verify they're accessible.\n\nThe development doesn't document clearances from existing streetlights, and down guy wires aren't shown on the plans at all, making it impossible to verify they won't conflict with accessible routes. Guy easements for transmission lines would only apply if transmission infrastructure is confirmed. No down guy anchor easement exhibits have been provided. Since the transformers serve the underground system rather than overhead lines, overhead clearance requirements don't apply to them. Transformers in niche configurations aren't relevant to this project. Construction staging areas lack clear delineation on the site plan, so I can't verify the required 10-foot radial clearance. The plans appear to be missing the mandatory 48-hour notification note—I need to verify this against the cover sheet and general notes. Service masts through roofs don't apply since the project uses underground service.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a9c15c-2133-427c-a1ff-4e415da2ee73","uuid":"522a2608-c434-4859-a67c-96756681895d"}
