orientations are not indicated on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed 'No, the symbols used for the transformer pads are simple rectangles... There are no architectural door swing symbols, labels, or specific directional markings to indicate which side the access doors are located on.'","reasoning":"Clearance requirements under UCM § 1.10.4 differ based on access door orientation and side characteristics. Without documented access door locations, compliance with side-specific clearances cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations near sidewalks"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown adjacent to transformer pad areas on the site plan, but the required minimum 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalk is not documented with dimension lines or measurements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan sheets show sidewalk layout with transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions from transformer pads to sidewalk edges.","reasoning":"Required minimum clearances must be documented on plans to demonstrate compliance. Without explicit dimensions, the 2-foot separation cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The transformer pad hot-stick use area access door orientations are not indicated on the plans, making it impossible to verify the required minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent structures. No dashed clearance zones, arc markings, or access door symbols shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check explicitly stated 'No, the symbols used for the transformer pads are simple rectangles... There are no architectural door swing symbols... no dashed lines, arcs, shading, or text labels indicating a 10-foot clearance zone around any of the transformer pads.'","reasoning":"The 10-foot clearance requirement applies from the access door side. Without documented access door location, this fundamental clearance requirement cannot be verified for any transformer pad.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan shows trees and vegetation symbols but does not identify any species as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F column designations. Utility compatibility cannot be verified for any trees potentially within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of landscape plan found tree legend identifies only codes (SY, PL, P, M) for mitigation categories but 'There is no text in this legend or elsewhere on the page explicitly identifying any of these as utility-compatible species.'","reasoning":"ECM Appendix F requires utility-compatible species designation. The landscape plan's failure to cross-reference tree species against the 'UC' column of Appendix F means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations with adjacent shrubs or vegetation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrubs and low-lying vegetation are shown on the landscape plan near transformer locations, but transformer access door orientations are not documented, making it impossible to verify the required 10-foot clearance from access door side or 5-foot clearance from other sides.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows vegetation placement but transformer pad locations are not marked on landscape sheet, and access door orientations are not documented on electrical sheet.","reasoning":"Shrub clearance requirements differ by side (10 feet vs 5 feet). Without documented access door orientation, side-specific clearance compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan, but required root barrier details (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment) are not shown on any plan or detail sheet for trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape and detail sheets reviewed; no root barrier specifications or details are documented for areas near transformer equipment.","reasoning":"Root barriers are a specific requirement for trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Absence of barrier details means this requirement cannot be demonstrated as satisfied.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Multiple transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan, but minimum 5-foot clearances between pads are not documented. No dimension lines or measurements show distances between the multiple transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision inspection identified five distinct transformer pads at various locations but 'there are no dimension lines, measurements, or text values indicating the distances from any of the electrical transformer pads' to other pads.","reasoning":"With multiple transformer pads shown on the project, inter-pad clearance compliance must be documented. Absence of these dimensions is a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on the utility plan, but minimum 5-foot horizontal clearances from transformer pads to water lines are not documented with dimensions or annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water line routing across site, and Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions are provided between these utilities.","reasoning":"Austin Water infrastructure separation is required per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2. Required clearances must be documented to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines are shown on the utility plan, but minimum 5-foot horizontal clearances from transformer pads to wastewater lines are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 shows wastewater line routing and Sheet 21 shows transformer pads, but no clearance dimensions between them.","reasoning":"Austin Water wastewater separation requires documented clearances per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain lines are shown on the site and storm sewer plans, but minimum 5-foot horizontal clearances from transformer pads to storm drain lines are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Storm sewer infrastructure shown on multiple sheets, transformer pads identified, but no clearance dimensions between features.","reasoning":"Required separation from storm infrastructure must be documented per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple underground utilities are shown on the utility and site plans, but minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads to all other underground utilities (except gas, fuel, steam) are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plans show water, wastewater, and storm infrastructure, but no 12-inch separation dimensions from transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Universal 12-inch clearances from other utilities are required per UCM § 1.10.5.A and must be documented on plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on the landscape plan along the property perimeter, but minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead conductors are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows 'OHE' (overhead electric) line along property boundary; transformer pads identified on electrical plan; no clearance dimensions shown.","reasoning":"Overhead line separation requires documented clearances per UCM § 1.10.3.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are present on the site, but minimum 15-foot radius clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline) are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line shown on landscape plan but no 15-foot radius clearance zones, dimensions, or annotations relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance is a specific requirement under UCM § 1.10.3 and must be explicitly documented on plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to recorded easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Facts.md identifies two critical recorded easements (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement, Instrument 2010070731; City of Austin Drainage Easement, Instrument 2011021137) totaling ~0.44 acres in the NE portion of the site, but these easements are NOT depicted on the submitted site plan. Transformer pad locations cannot be verified as outside these undocumented easements. Additionally, multiple plat-dedicated easements (25' drainage, 7.5' PUE, 10' wastewater, 10' drainage) are noted in GIS but not confirmed on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md explicitly states 'NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer' for both critical easements; facts further note other easements from plats are 'Not verified on site plan.'","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.4 footnote 4, transformer equipment cannot be located in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, electrical under overhead lines) without written AE Design approval. Undocumented easements covering ~19% of site in the NE area (where some transformers are located) means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on the site plan or electrical plan. Per UCM § 1.10.3, transformer easements with widths adequate for Austin Energy accessibility requirements must be depicted around all pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all plan sheets shows transformer pad locations but no easement boundaries, dimensions, or callouts for transformer access easements.","reasoning":"Transformer easements are a required element per code and must be shown on plans. Absence of documented easements is a deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions (width × length) are not provided on the electrical plan or detail sheets. Additionally, no references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are shown, and service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not documented. Per UCM § 1.5.2.6, pad dimensions must match AE Design-approved specifications for the specified service type.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check explicitly found 'No specific dimensions or detailed construction notes for the transformer pads are shown on this page... there are no visible references to Austin Energy Design detail sheets on this specific plan page.'","reasoning":"AE Design approval of transformer pad dimensions is a code requirement. Absence of pad specifications and AE Design detail callouts means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations within 4 feet of parking or vehicle routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads located within the parking and vehicle circulation areas of the site lack required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts (bollards) per AE Design equipment pad details. The main 5 labeled transformer pads do not show documented bollard protection, and no spacing details confirm that bollards allow equipment door access.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check found 'There is only one feature explicitly labeled \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" on the site plan... There are NO bollards shown around this specific, explicitly named transformer pad.' Other unmarked pads near parking show bollards, but main transformer pads lack documented bollards.","reasoning":"When transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking areas (as shown in site layout), bollards are required per code. Absence of documented bollards is a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d23ed0d-287b-46bb-a723-f7b26bb1858c","uuid":"4daac2ab-420a-4589-b2d4-efaf4b2590d3"}
