{"level":30,"time":1778246479117,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VYT6HPSWJRAJ68KTS2BFQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan documents, I'll now evaluate all checklist items for this grouping. Let me document my findings systematically.\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure:**\n- OHE (overhead electric distribution) line documented on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) running along southern property boundary with three utility poles\n- Vision analysis confirms trees positioned 5-10 feet from OHE line and within ~10 feet of at least one utility pole\n- Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3 indicate transmission infrastructure may be present (requiring 25-foot clearance zones)\n- No dimension lines or clearance annotations on landscape plan\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\n- Sheet 35 Plant Schedule identifies: 10 Cedar Elm (UC, mature height ~50-60 ft), 2 Live Oak (NOT UC, mature height 40+ ft), 6 Mexican Redbud (UC, ~25-30 ft), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (UC, ~20-25 ft)\n- Sheet 31 shows trees with functional abbreviations only (SY=Street Yard, PL=Parking Lot, P=Buffer Point, M=Mitigation)\n- No individual tree species labels visible on landscape plan itself\n- No differentiation for large trees (40+ feet) on landscape plan\n- Tree locations shown adjacent to overhead electric infrastructure\n\n**Documentation Review:**\n- No dimension lines showing clearances to overhead facilities\n- No Austin Energy approval documentation visible in plan set\n- Sheet 3 contains detailed transmission and electric notes but no verification of compliance on landscape plan\n- Mature heights listed in plant schedule but not identified on landscape plan\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Exact conductor locations (only pole line shown, not individual conductor positions)\n- Transmission easement boundaries (despite transmission notes referencing them)\n- Underground electric equipment locations and configuration\n- Pad-mounted electric equipment (if any)\n- Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment\n- Austin Energy written approval for any trees in restricted zones\n- Specific distance measurements from trees to conductors"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87ad5ecd-4cf7-4b80-b04f-ff327308d79b","uuid":"0765a8e9-9bcb-41d5-88be-882e7d3b0331"}
