), and property features but contains no section views or enlarged plan details with dimension lines originating from the outside conductor and extending to the outermost edge of buildings or projections. No cross-section drawings show vertical or horizontal clearance verification.","reasoning":"The requirement is applicable because buildings and building projections are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities. The explicit absence of section and plan view exhibits with clearance dimensions from the outside conductor constitutes a failure to provide required documentation.","tools_used":["vision","read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8 and all building projections shown on site plan near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead electric lines but no section views or enlarged details with clearance dimensions from outside conductor to building edges are provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fencing symbols (marked 'X' and 'F' per legend) along property boundaries where overhead electric lines are located per existing conditions survey. However, no dimensions annotate the clearance between the outside conductor and the fence line. The plans do not identify whether fence height is labeled or if vertical clearance from finished grade to the outside conductor is documented.","reasoning":"Fences are proposed adjacent to overhead electric lines, making the requirement applicable. However, without clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the fence structure, or verification that the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance is maintained, compliance cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision","read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Perimeter fencing shown on property boundaries near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fencing is shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor are documented. Clearance compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fencing (marked 'F' and 'X' on boundaries) and utility pole symbols (U.P.) on the existing conditions survey. However, the site plan does not provide explicit horizontal dimension annotations between fence post locations and electric pole locations.","reasoning":"The requirement is applicable if fences with posts are proposed near electric poles. The existence of both elements is confirmed, but the plans lack explicit dimension documentation showing the horizontal distance between fence posts and pole locations, preventing verification of the 10-foot minimum separation.","tools_used":["vision","read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence posts near utility poles on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence and pole locations are shown but horizontal clearance dimensions between fence posts and electric poles are not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plans and easement information on Sheet 4 and facts.md identifies no existing Austin Energy substation facilities on or immediately adjacent to the property. Fencing is proposed on property boundaries, but the easement documents reference electric transmission facilities, not substation properties.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when fences connect to or are adjacent to existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation property adjacency is documented, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No substation fences are shown adjacent to proposed fencing. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes confirm that electric transmission facilities exist on or adjacent to the site, with notes requiring 25-foot clearance from transmission structures and restricting certain activities. Site plan shows fencing on property boundaries. However, the plans do not specify whether the proposed fencing is located beneath or adjacent to transmission lines, what material is proposed for fence construction, or whether grounding specifications are documented.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are confirmed to exist, making the requirement potentially applicable if fencing is proposed beneath or adjacent to transmission lines. However, the plans lack sufficient documentation identifying the fencing location relative to transmission line routing, fence material specifications, or grounding details, preventing verification of compliance.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Fencing proposed on property boundaries near transmission line easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fencing is shown but no documentation addresses whether it is beneath transmission lines or specifies material (conductive vs. non-conductive) and grounding details."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows no vehicle barrier posts or specialized barrier fencing proposed beneath overhead electric lines. Perimeter fencing is shown, but no barriers designed to restrict vehicle access under overhead lines are depicted.","reasoning":"Vehicle barrier fencing is not proposed as part of this residential development. The requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing proposed beneath overhead lines. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 confirms that retaining walls up to 14 feet in height are proposed on the site, as detailed in wall plan and section drawings. Existing conditions survey and site plan show overhead electric lines on property boundaries. However, no dimension annotations link the retaining wall alignments to the outside conductor location or document the horizontal sky-to-ground clearance.","reasoning":"Retaining walls are proposed adjacent to overhead electric facilities, making the requirement applicable. However, the plans do not provide clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the wall face, preventing verification of the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls (up to 14 feet) proposed around site perimeter near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor to wall face are documented on site plan or section views."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md and site plan review confirm no Austin Energy substation property is adjacent to the site. Retaining walls are shown on property boundaries, but no substation adjacency is documented.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when retaining walls are adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. No substation adjacency exists, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No substation property is adjacent to retaining walls. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review reveals no emergency access bridges or elevated platforms are proposed as part of the Valley View Townhomes residential development. Standard pedestrian walkways are shown, but no structures specifically designed as emergency access facilities with vertical structural supports are depicted.","reasoning":"Emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are not proposed. The requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access bridges or elevated platforms proposed. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are confirmed on site plan (Sheet 9) and detailed on Sheets 38-39. The existing conditions survey and site plan show overhead electric lines on property boundaries. However, no section views with dimension annotations from the outside conductor to the outermost edge of any retaining wall are provided. The wall sections on Sheets 38-39 do not reference or dimension clearances to overhead electric conductors.","reasoning":"Retaining walls are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities. The requirement explicitly requires section exhibits showing clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the wall face. The absence of such exhibits constitutes a failure to provide required documentation.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls (up to 14 feet) shown on Sheets 38-39 and located near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall sections are provided but do not include clearance dimension annotations from outside conductor to wall face. Required section exhibits with clearance dimensions are missing."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show internal driveways and parking areas. Existing conditions survey and site plan depict overhead electric lines on property boundaries. However, no vertical clearance dimensions are documented between the finished driveway grade and the lowest point of overhead electric facilities, and no determination of truck traffic expectations (which determines whether 16-foot or 18-foot clearance applies) is evident on the plans.","reasoning":"Driveways are proposed and overhead electric facilities exist, making the requirement applicable. However, the plans lack the section views and vertical clearance dimensions necessary to verify that 16-foot (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot (with truck traffic) clearances are maintained. Without surveyed mid-span clearance data, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Internal driveways and parking areas shown on site plan near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways and parking areas are shown but no section views or vertical clearance dimensions are documented. Surveyed mid-span clearance data is not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking areas with parking spaces but does not explicitly depict concrete pads with vehicles parked beneath overhead electric lines or show vehicle display areas. The plans do not contain vertical clearance dimensions or notes about clearance requirements for vehicles in parking areas.","reasoning":"The requirement is applicable only if vehicles parked or displayed on concrete pads are shown beneath overhead electric lines with specific clearance verification. The plans do not adequately document whether this scenario applies or provide the necessary clearance dimensions, preventing verification.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Parking areas shown on site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Parking areas are shown but no documentation addresses vehicle clearance from overhead lines or indicates which areas have overhead line crossing concerns."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes confirm transmission facilities are present on site. However, the grading plan (Sheet 11) does not contain annotations identifying where transmission lines cross roadways or driveways, nor are vertical clearance dimensions (30-foot minimum from transmission line to ground surface) documented. The plans do not label transmission facilities with voltage (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV) or distinguish transmission from distribution lines.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are confirmed to exist on-site. However, the grading plan lacks the specific identification of transmission line crossing locations and the vertical clearance dimensions required to verify the 30-foot minimum clearance. Without this documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Roads and driveways shown on site plan where transmission lines may cross"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission facilities are noted on Sheet 3 but grading plan does not identify transmission line crossing locations or document 30-foot vertical clearance dimensions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 notes reference transmission structures and facilities. However, the grading plan and site plan do not explicitly identify or label locations where distribution lines are 'underbuilt' on transmission structures (distribution lines running beneath transmission structures on the same or adjacent poles). Without this identification, the applicability condition cannot be confirmed.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to highway/freeway grades with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures. The plans do not clearly identify whether this specific configuration exists, preventing determination of applicability.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway grading is shown on site plan. Requirement not applicable to this local street/residential project."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows internal driveways and parking areas, and the existing conditions survey depicts utility pole symbols on property boundaries. However, the plans do not explicitly identify any conflicts between proposed driveway locations and existing electric pole positions, nor do they show pole relocation notes or revised pole locations if conflicts exist.","reasoning":"The applicability condition requires identification of conflicts between proposed driveways and existing pole locations. The plans do not provide sufficient detail or conflict analysis to determine whether this scenario applies. Without explicit conflict identification or relocation documentation, applicability cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway and pole locations are shown but conflict analysis and clearance dimensions are not documented. Conflicts, if any exist, are not identified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) contains dimension annotations for various site features (e.g., '26.1'' near Bldg. 1, '21.3'' near Bldg. 5) representing building setbacks from property lines. However, the dimension annotations do not originate from the outside conductor location but instead reference property line distances. No dimension lines extend from the outside conductor to any site features, confirming that clearance dimensions are measured from pole centerline or property lines rather than from the actual conductor position.","reasoning":"The requirement explicitly demands that all clearance dimensions be measured from the outside conductor, not from the utility pole or pole centerline. The complete absence of any dimension annotations extending from conductor locations, combined with the presence of dimensions from property lines, constitutes a failure to properly document required clearances. This is one of the most common violation patterns identified in the regulatory guidance.","tools_used":["vision","read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All clearance dimensions shown on site plan for buildings and site features near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions, if any, are measured from property lines or pole centerline rather than from the outside conductor as required by code. Dimension annotations must originate from the actual conductor position."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of lighting plans and site plan documentation reveals no new streetlight poles are proposed for installation on this site. Site plan shows building-mounted and area lighting but no dedicated streetlight poles are indicated.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when new streetlight poles are proposed. No streetlight poles are shown on the site plan, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No streetlight poles proposed. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows sidewalk improvements along the right-of-way on Sheet 9. Existing conditions survey shows utility poles on property boundaries at the intersection with Valley View Road. However, the plans do not provide explicit documentation showing whether existing power poles at property ends along the ROW frontage conflict with proposed sidewalk alignments, or whether clearance is maintained.","reasoning":"The requirement applies if new or modified sidewalks intersect existing power poles at property limits along ROW. The plans show sidewalks and poles but do not provide sufficient detail or conflict analysis to determine whether clearance is maintained from poles at each property end.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks proposed along Valley View Road at property frontage boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown at property frontage where utility poles exist, but conflict resolution or clearance dimensions are not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash collection areas or trash enclosure locations, but the plans do not explicitly identify whether trash enclosures are located beneath overhead electric facilities. Additionally, the plans do not document whether trash bin raised heights during service operation have been evaluated against overhead conductor heights.","reasoning":"The requirement is applicable if trash enclosures are placed beneath overhead lines. The plans do not provide sufficient documentation to determine whether trash areas conflict with overhead lines or whether clearance considerations have been addressed during trash bin service operations.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash collection areas shown on site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash collection areas are shown but no documentation addresses whether they are beneath overhead lines or whether trash bin service clearances have been verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings (customer facilities) proposed within the electric transmission easement area per Sheet 3 transmission notes which identify easement boundaries and state that certain permanent structures are prohibited. The transmission notes explicitly state that 'Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain' permanent habitable structures within the transmission easement. Buildings are shown on the site plan without documented coordination showing they are outside the easement or with documented exception from Austin Energy.","reasoning":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes (Item 16) explicitly prohibit permanent structures within the transmission easement. If the proposed buildings are located within this easement, this represents an absolute prohibition violation regardless of clearance distances. The plans do not demonstrate that buildings are positioned outside the easement or provide Austin Energy approval for their location within the easement.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8 shown on site plan relative to electric transmission easement boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed on site without documented verification that they are outside transmission easement boundaries. Transmission easement restrictions are noted on Sheet 3 but building compliance is not addressed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows water meter locations as part of utility infrastructure on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan). However, the plans do not document the location of these meters relative to overhead electric service drop conductors (the overhead secondary voltage lines from Austin Energy infrastructure to the customer service point), nor are clearance dimensions provided.","reasoning":"Water meter locations are shown but their relationship to overhead electric service drops is not documented. Without clearance dimension annotations showing the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of service-drop lines, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations shown on utility plan relative to overhead electric service lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations are shown but clearance from overhead electric service drop conductors is not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 21 and possibly Sheet 19) shows underground water line routing for private domestic water branches (2\" HDPE) as noted on the plan. Existing conditions survey shows overhead electric distribution poles and lines on property boundaries. However, the plans do not provide cross-section details or explicit clearance dimension annotations showing the vertical and horizontal relationship between water line locations and overhead distribution poles and conductors.","reasoning":"Water lines are proposed and overhead distribution facilities exist. The plans lack sufficient section views and clearance documentation to verify that water lines maintain required clearances from overhead distribution conductors and poles.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Underground water lines shown on utility plan near overhead electric distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown but clearance dimensions from overhead distribution facilities are not documented on site plan or utility sections."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building foundation locations and property line positions. Existing conditions survey confirms overhead electric facilities on adjacent right-of-way. However, the plans do not explicitly identify which foundations are located within 5 feet of property lines, nor do they provide documented coordination with Austin Energy regarding space necessary for electric facility installation, maintenance, and clearance.","reasoning":"Some permanent structure foundations appear to be proposed near property lines based on site layout. Without explicit documentation identifying all foundations within 5 feet of the property line and without coordination notes addressing clearance space for adjacent electric facilities, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations shown on site plan near property line boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building locations and property lines are shown but no documentation identifies foundations within 5 feet of property line or addresses clearance space for adjacent electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Driveway and parking area grades are shown on the grading plan (Sheet 11) and site plan (Sheet 9). Existing conditions survey and site plan depict overhead electric lines on property boundaries. Comparing estimated overhead line heights from utility pole structures to proposed driveway grades suggests that vertical clearances may be marginal. However, no registered surveyor mid-span clearance data documenting actual conductor heights at locations where driveways pass beneath lines is provided.","reasoning":"Visual comparison of site features and overhead line positions indicates potential clearance concerns that would trigger the requirement for registered surveyor verification. However, the actual surveyed mid-span clearance data is absent. Without this data, the vertical clearance adequacy cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway grades shown on site plan passing beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway grades may have marginal vertical clearance from overhead lines, but registered surveyor mid-span clearance verification is not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows Valley View Road along the western property boundary. Existing conditions survey depicts overhead electric lines crossing or running parallel to this roadway. However, the plans do not include utility plan details or notes documenting whether overhead electric line crossings of the roadway are oriented perpendicular (90-degree angle) to the road centerline.","reasoning":"Overhead line crossing angles relative to roadway alignments are not documented on the plans. Without explicit notation of crossing angles, compliance with the 90-degree orientation requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossings of roadways at property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead line crossings of Valley View Road are not documented with angle annotations to verify 90-degree crossing orientation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility plan details do not explicitly document secondary and primary overhead electric line crossing configurations. While the plans show overhead electric facilities, the distinction between secondary (lower voltage service lines) and primary (higher voltage distribution lines) conductor types and their vertical relationships is not identified through crossing details or section views.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only if both secondary and primary overhead lines cross each other. The plans do not provide sufficient documentation to determine whether this condition exists or whether secondary lines cross above primary lines (a violation).","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric utility line routing shown on site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but does not document secondary vs. primary conductor types or their crossing relationships."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and building elevation review reveals no marquee signs are proposed as part of the Valley View Townhomes residential development. Standard signage for the project may exist, but no marquee-style signs with canopy structures are shown.","reasoning":"Marquee signs are not proposed. The requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are shown on site plan. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and electrical design plan show proposed underground service routing with transformers and pull boxes. However, the plans do not indicate new power poles being installed for underground service conversion. The project is designed with underground electrical service, not overhead poles requiring relocation.","reasoning":"New power poles for underground service conversion are not proposed. The requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Project utilizes underground electrical service. No new poles for underground service conversion are proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows landscape lighting locations as part of the site design on Sheet 31. Overhead electric lines are depicted on property boundaries per existing conditions survey and site plan. However, the plans do not document whether decorative lighting fixtures are located beneath overhead lines or provide clearance verification dimensions from conductors to light fixture heights.","reasoning":"Decorative lighting is shown but its spatial relationship to overhead lines is not documented. Without explicit clearance dimensions or relocation notes, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape and decorative lighting shown on lighting and landscape plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Decorative lighting locations are shown but clearance from overhead electric lines is not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols and landscape planting areas but does not list the species of proposed trees or identify their locations relative to overhead electric lines. The blocks reference the tree list for surveyed existing trees but do not provide a species list for proposed plantings. Without species identification and specific lateral distance measurements from overhead conductors, the utility-compatibility requirement cannot be verified.","reasoning":"Proposed landscaping is shown, but the plans lack critical information: (1) species identification for proposed trees, (2) lateral distance measurements from overhead distribution (10-foot standard) and transmission (50-foot standard) conductors, and (3) utility-compatibility verification against ECM Appendix F. The absence of these elements prevents verification of tree clearance compliance.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plantings shown on landscape plan near overhead electric distribution and transmission facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows plantings but does not identify proposed tree species or verify lateral clearance distances from overhead electric lines. Utility-compatibility verification is not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows electric meter locations as part of the preliminary electrical design (Sheet 21). However, the plans do not provide enlarged meter area details or documentation showing meter installation clearances relative to adjacent site features (fences, walls, buildings, landscaping) or verification that the required 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom working clearances are maintained.","reasoning":"Meter locations are shown but insufficient detail is provided to verify that required working clearances (per UCM § 1.10.9) are maintained free from obstructions. Without enlarged detail views or clearance dimension annotations, obstruction conflicts cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations shown on electrical design plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Meter locations are shown but no enlarged details verify that required working clearances (30\" × 36\" × 6.5'h) are maintained free from obstructions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building locations and existing utility poles on property boundaries per existing conditions survey. However, the plans do not explicitly document clearance dimensions between building structures and existing streetlight poles, nor do they provide verification that buildings maintain required clearances from these existing fixtures.","reasoning":"Existing streetlight poles may be present on or near the property, but the plans do not document clearance verification. Without explicit clearance dimension annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings shown on site plan near existing streetlight pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building locations and pole locations are shown but clearance dimensions from buildings to streetlight poles are not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey shows utility poles (U.P.) with down guy anchor locations potentially indicated, though guy wire symbols and anchor point locations are not explicitly labeled on the survey. Site plan shows proposed driveways and accessible pedestrian paths. However, the plans do not provide explicit documentation identifying whether down guy wires conflict with proposed accessible routes or driveways.","reasoning":"The utility infrastructure (poles and potential guy anchors) is shown on existing conditions, and driveways/paths are proposed on the site plan. However, the plans lack explicit conflict identification or resolution notes (pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles). Without this documentation, conflict resolution status cannot be verified. The guidance notes that electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway and accessible path locations shown on site plan relative to utility poles with potential guy wire anchors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles are shown on existing conditions survey but down guy wire locations are not clearly identified. Conflict resolution with proposed driveways is not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows the property with utility information and existing easements. Sheet 3 references electric transmission facilities with associated easements. However, the easement exhibit on Sheet 2 (Plat) and site plan do not explicitly show guy easement boundaries (10-foot-wide strip 10 feet on each side of guy wire plus 50-foot extension beyond anchor point) for angled guy anchors from transmission structures.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are confirmed to exist. If angled guy anchors exist, dedicated easements are required, but the plans do not explicitly depict guy easement boundaries. Without this documentation, easement compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Easement areas shown on plat and site plan related to transmission structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission facilities are noted but guy easement boundaries (10' wide ± 50' extension) are not explicitly shown on easement exhibit or site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey shows utility poles on property boundaries and site plan references electrical facilities. However, the easement exhibit does not explicitly identify down guy anchor locations from distribution poles with dedicated easement boundaries (10-foot width extending 5 feet past where down guy enters ground per Austin Energy standards).","reasoning":"If down guy anchors from distribution poles exist on or adjacent to the property, dedicated easements are required. The plans do not provide explicit documentation of down guy anchor locations or associated easement boundaries, preventing verification of easement compliance.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations from distribution poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles are shown but down guy anchor locations and dedicated easement boundaries (10' wide × 5' extension) are not explicitly documented on easement exhibit."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transformer/electrical equipment locations on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) but does not provide section views documenting the vertical relationship between transformer equipment heights and overhead electric line conductor locations. No clearance dimension annotations from conductors to transformer tops are provided.","reasoning":"Transformers are shown on the electrical design plan, but the plans lack section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to the top of transformer equipment. Without this documentation, the 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations shown on electrical design plan relative to overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer locations are shown but section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to transformer tops are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical design plan and site plan reveals no transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations with structures or canopies above equipment) are proposed. Equipment is shown on the electrical design plan but not in niche configurations requiring the specialized 35-foot clearance.","reasoning":"Niche service configurations are not proposed. The requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations are proposed. Requirement not applicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and site logistics information show construction staging areas would be necessary for a project of this scope. Overhead electric lines exist on property boundaries as confirmed by existing conditions survey. However, the submitted plan set does not include a construction logistics plan, site staging plan, or equipment operation zone diagram documenting the 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines during construction.","reasoning":"Construction activities are planned and overhead lines exist, making the OSHA/UCM requirement applicable. However, the submitted documents do not include a construction staging or logistics plan with marked clearance boundaries from overhead lines. Without this documentation, construction-phase clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas and equipment operation zones during project construction"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but no construction staging plan or equipment operation zone diagram documents 10-foot radial clearance during construction."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes) explicitly includes Note 3 stating: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153...' This documents the 48-hour notification requirement for work near transmission lines.","reasoning":"The required notification note is present on the general notes sheet addressing the 48-hour pre-construction coordination requirement with Austin Energy. The requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["read","vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["General notes sheet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes (Note 3) includes the required 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before commencement of construction near transmission lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of building elevation and electrical design plans reveals no service-mast through-roof installations are shown for individual units. The electrical design plan shows underground service distribution throughout the site.","reasoning":"Service-mast through-roof installations are not proposed. The requirement does not apply to underground service delivery systems.","tools_used":["read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electrical service is proposed. No service-mast through-roof installations are shown. Requirement not applicable."}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa-c822-4488-9300-f5bc2aee8d18","uuid":"e807edd5-a8d2-4836-96ad-8c193528d922"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246491599,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CXVskYEKapW7NmeGHmQaA4","type":"tool_result","content":"Structured output provided successfully"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e64c35fa-c822-4488-9300-f5bc2aee8d18","uuid":"a7a74ed9-3d83-440f-9e09-7ccbb88cc005","tool_use_result":"Structured output provided successfully"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246492002,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VZMA31HC75W4DAXNVDR56","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping 13 (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes project. \n\n## Summary of Review\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping applies to the project. Five (5) transformer pads are clearly shown on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), indicating that electrical utility infrastructure is a relevant component of this site plan.\n\n**Critical Findings:**\n\nI identified **18 significant deficiencies** where required transformer pad clearances, specifications, and protective measures are not documented on the submitted plans:\n\n**Major Deficiencies:**\n1. **Missing Clearance Documentation** - No dimension lines or measurements showing distances from transformer pads to buildings, structures, utilities, or site features\n2. **Undocumented Access Door Orientation** - Transformer access doors are not marked, preventing verification of the mandatory 10-foot hot-stick clearance zone\n3. **Missing AE Design Specifications** - No transformer pad dimensions or references to Austin Energy Design-approved detail sheets provided\n4. **No Transformer Easements** - Required easement areas around pads not depicted on site plan\n5. **Missing Bollard Protection** - No documented bollards protecting transformer pads located near parking and vehicle circulation areas\n6. **Undocumented Utilities Separation** - Clearances from water, wastewater, storm drain, and other underground utilities not shown\n7. **Overhead Line Clearances Not Documented** - No marked clearances from overhead distribution lines\n8. **Vegetation Utility Compatibility Not Verified** - Trees on landscape plan not identified as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F standards\n9. **Easement Conflict Risk** - Two critical recorded easements (Greenbelt Access and City of Austin Drainage) totaling ~0.44 acres are not depicted on the site plan; transformer locations cannot be verified as avoiding these restricted areas\n\n**Structured Output Submitted:** 18 deficiency findings with detailed code citations, locations, and evidence have been submitted in the required format for further applicant response and design corrections."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d23ed0d-287b-46bb-a723-f7b26bb1858c","uuid":"7e9c793d-2e28-462c-a56c-8882d44920d3"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246492018,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":287818,"duration_api_ms":158973,"num_turns":26,"result":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping 13 (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes project. \n\n## Summary of Review\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping applies to the project. Five (5) transformer pads are clearly shown on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), indicating that electrical utility infrastructure is a relevant component of this site plan.\n\n**Critical Findings:**\n\nI identified **18 significant deficiencies** where required transformer pad clearances, specifications, and protective measures are not documented on the submitted plans:\n\n**Major Deficiencies:**\n1. **Missing Clearance Documentation** - No dimension lines or measurements showing distances from transformer pads to buildings, structures, utilities, or site features\n2. **Undocumented Access Door Orientation** - Transformer access doors are not marked, preventing verification of the mandatory 10-foot hot-stick clearance zone\n3. **Missing AE Design Specifications** - No transformer pad dimensions or references to Austin Energy Design-approved detail sheets provided\n4. **No Transformer Easements** - Required easement areas around pads not depicted on site plan\n5. **Missing Bollard Protection** - No documented bollards protecting transformer pads located near parking and vehicle circulation areas\n6. **Undocumented Utilities Separation** - Clearances from water, wastewater, storm drain, and other underground utilities not shown\n7. **Overhead Line Clearances Not Documented** - No marked clearances from overhead distribution lines\n8. **Vegetation Utility Compatibility Not Verified** - Trees on landscape plan not identified as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F standards\n9. **Easement Conflict Risk** - Two critical recorded easements (Greenbelt Access and City of Austin Drainage) totaling ~0.44 acres are not depicted on the site plan; transformer locations cannot be verified as avoiding these restricted areas\n\n**Structured Output Submitted:** 18 deficiency findings with detailed code citations, locations, and evidence have been submitted in the required format for further applicant response and design corrections.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1d23ed0d-287b-46bb-a723-f7b26bb1858c","total_cost_usd":0.2948287,"usage":{"input_tokens":15075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116678,"cache_read_input_tokens":452562,"output_tokens":17730,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":116678},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":15075,"outputTokens":17730,"cacheReadInputTokens":452562,"cacheCreationInputTokens":116678,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2948287,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan but required minimum 5-foot clearance dimensions to buildings and building foundations are not documented. No dimension lines, measurements, or clearance callouts appear on any plan sheet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision inspection of Sheet 21 identified five transformer pads but found 'no dimension lines, measurements, or text values indicating the distances from any of the electrical transformer pads to the nearest building structures.'","reasoning":"Required clearance dimensions are documented deficiencies when absent from plans per review guidelines. The applicant must demonstrate compliance with minimum clearances through explicit dimensions or verified spatial relationships on the plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations adjacent to fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are shown on the site plan adjacent to transformer pad areas, but required clearances (5 feet for sides with operators/controls, 3 feet for sides without) cannot be verified because transformer access door orientations are not indicated on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed 'No, the symbols used for the transformer pads are simple rectangles... There are no architectural door swing symbols, labels, or specific directional markings to indicate which side the access doors are located on.'","reasoning":"Clearance requirements under UCM § 1.10.4 differ based on access door orientation and side characteristics. Without documented access door locations, compliance with side-specific clearances cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations near sidewalks"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown adjacent to transformer pad areas on the site plan, but the required minimum 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalk is not documented with dimension lines or measurements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan sheets show sidewalk layout with transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions from transformer pads to sidewalk edges.","reasoning":"Required minimum clearances must be documented on plans to demonstrate compliance. Without explicit dimensions, the 2-foot separation cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The transformer pad hot-stick use area access door orientations are not indicated on the plans, making it impossible to verify the required minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent structures. No dashed clearance zones, arc markings, or access door symbols shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check explicitly stated 'No, the symbols used for the transformer pads are simple rectangles... There are no architectural door swing symbols... no dashed lines, arcs, shading, or text labels indicating a 10-foot clearance zone around any of the transformer pads.'","reasoning":"The 10-foot clearance requirement applies from the access door side. Without documented access door location, this fundamental clearance requirement cannot be verified for any transformer pad.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan shows trees and vegetation symbols but does not identify any species as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F column designations. Utility compatibility cannot be verified for any trees potentially within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of landscape plan found tree legend identifies only codes (SY, PL, P, M) for mitigation categories but 'There is no text in this legend or elsewhere on the page explicitly identifying any of these as utility-compatible species.'","reasoning":"ECM Appendix F requires utility-compatible species designation. The landscape plan's failure to cross-reference tree species against the 'UC' column of Appendix F means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations with adjacent shrubs or vegetation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrubs and low-lying vegetation are shown on the landscape plan near transformer locations, but transformer access door orientations are not documented, making it impossible to verify the required 10-foot clearance from access door side or 5-foot clearance from other sides.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows vegetation placement but transformer pad locations are not marked on landscape sheet, and access door orientations are not documented on electrical sheet.","reasoning":"Shrub clearance requirements differ by side (10 feet vs 5 feet). Without documented access door orientation, side-specific clearance compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan, but required root barrier details (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment) are not shown on any plan or detail sheet for trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape and detail sheets reviewed; no root barrier specifications or details are documented for areas near transformer equipment.","reasoning":"Root barriers are a specific requirement for trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Absence of barrier details means this requirement cannot be demonstrated as satisfied.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Multiple transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan, but minimum 5-foot clearances between pads are not documented. No dimension lines or measurements show distances between the multiple transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision inspection identified five distinct transformer pads at various locations but 'there are no dimension lines, measurements, or text values indicating the distances from any of the electrical transformer pads' to other pads.","reasoning":"With multiple transformer pads shown on the project, inter-pad clearance compliance must be documented. Absence of these dimensions is a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on the utility plan, but minimum 5-foot horizontal clearances from transformer pads to water lines are not documented with dimensions or annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) shows water line routing across site, and Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions are provided between these utilities.","reasoning":"Austin Water infrastructure separation is required per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2. Required clearances must be documented to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines are shown on the utility plan, but minimum 5-foot horizontal clearances from transformer pads to wastewater lines are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 shows wastewater line routing and Sheet 21 shows transformer pads, but no clearance dimensions between them.","reasoning":"Austin Water wastewater separation requires documented clearances per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain lines are shown on the site and storm sewer plans, but minimum 5-foot horizontal clearances from transformer pads to storm drain lines are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Storm sewer infrastructure shown on multiple sheets, transformer pads identified, but no clearance dimensions between features.","reasoning":"Required separation from storm infrastructure must be documented per UCM § 2.9.1.B.2.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple underground utilities are shown on the utility and site plans, but minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads to all other underground utilities (except gas, fuel, steam) are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plans show water, wastewater, and storm infrastructure, but no 12-inch separation dimensions from transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Universal 12-inch clearances from other utilities are required per UCM § 1.10.5.A and must be documented on plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on the landscape plan along the property perimeter, but minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead conductors are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows 'OHE' (overhead electric) line along property boundary; transformer pads identified on electrical plan; no clearance dimensions shown.","reasoning":"Overhead line separation requires documented clearances per UCM § 1.10.3.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are present on the site, but minimum 15-foot radius clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline) are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line shown on landscape plan but no 15-foot radius clearance zones, dimensions, or annotations relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance is a specific requirement under UCM § 1.10.3 and must be explicitly documented on plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to recorded easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Facts.md identifies two critical recorded easements (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement, Instrument 2010070731; City of Austin Drainage Easement, Instrument 2011021137) totaling ~0.44 acres in the NE portion of the site, but these easements are NOT depicted on the submitted site plan. Transformer pad locations cannot be verified as outside these undocumented easements. Additionally, multiple plat-dedicated easements (25' drainage, 7.5' PUE, 10' wastewater, 10' drainage) are noted in GIS but not confirmed on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md explicitly states 'NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer' for both critical easements; facts further note other easements from plats are 'Not verified on site plan.'","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.4 footnote 4, transformer equipment cannot be located in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, electrical under overhead lines) without written AE Design approval. Undocumented easements covering ~19% of site in the NE area (where some transformers are located) means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on the site plan or electrical plan. Per UCM § 1.10.3, transformer easements with widths adequate for Austin Energy accessibility requirements must be depicted around all pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all plan sheets shows transformer pad locations but no easement boundaries, dimensions, or callouts for transformer access easements.","reasoning":"Transformer easements are a required element per code and must be shown on plans. Absence of documented easements is a deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions (width × length) are not provided on the electrical plan or detail sheets. Additionally, no references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are shown, and service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not documented. Per UCM § 1.5.2.6, pad dimensions must match AE Design-approved specifications for the specified service type.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check explicitly found 'No specific dimensions or detailed construction notes for the transformer pads are shown on this page... there are no visible references to Austin Energy Design detail sheets on this specific plan page.'","reasoning":"AE Design approval of transformer pad dimensions is a code requirement. Absence of pad specifications and AE Design detail callouts means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations within 4 feet of parking or vehicle routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads located within the parking and vehicle circulation areas of the site lack required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts (bollards) per AE Design equipment pad details. The main 5 labeled transformer pads do not show documented bollard protection, and no spacing details confirm that bollards allow equipment door access.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check found 'There is only one feature explicitly labeled \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" on the site plan... There are NO bollards shown around this specific, explicitly named transformer pad.' Other unmarked pads near parking show bollards, but main transformer pads lack documented bollards.","reasoning":"When transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking areas (as shown in site layout), bollards are required per code. Absence of documented bollards is a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c9f0ee0e-ee03-48b4-ba72-40ab67d5c45c"}
