{"level":30,"time":1778246499597,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3VZSWAYH8XTK3VRWA5W479","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my research so far, let me now document my findings and evaluate each checklist item. Let me create a summary of what I've found:\n\n## Research Summary - Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\n**Applicability Gate:**\n- The site plan includes an overhead electric (OHE) distribution line shown on Sheets 9 and 31\n- Trees are proposed for planting per the plant schedules on Sheet 35\n- Therefore, this grouping IS APPLICABLE\n\n**Infrastructure Present:**\n- Overhead Electric (OHE) line: Present, shown on Sheets 9 and 31, runs along south and east property boundaries\n- Utility poles: Shown on the plan but not dimensioned\n- Distribution vs. Transmission: The grouping guidance indicates typical Austin facilities are distribution (12.47kV or 34.5kV) unless specifically labeled as transmission. No voltage designation is shown on these plans, so default assumption is distribution.\n- Underground electric: Also present per Sheet 21 (transformers, pull boxes)\n- Transmission easements: Facts.md shows no transmission easement on site; only the 5' electric easements are plat-dedicated\n\n**Trees Proposed:**\nPer Sheet 35 Plant Schedule:\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 100 gal., 4\" cal., shade tree\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 100 gal., 4\" cal., shade tree\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 45 gal., 2.5\" cal., ornamental tree\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 45 gal., 2.5\" cal., ornamental tree\n- Plus: shrubs and groundcovers per Sheet 35\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Utility-compatible (UC) status for proposed tree species cannot be verified from submitted documents (ECM Appendix F not included)\n- Mature heights for proposed species not specified on the plan (Sheet 35 mentions minimum container specifications but not mature heights)\n- Exact species location mapping on landscape plan (Sheet 31 uses letter codes M, SY, PL but doesn't correlate them to the botanical names on Sheet 35)\n- Clearance dimensions from trees to overhead electric conductor (no dimensions shown)\n- Pole locations with coordinates (shown graphically but not dimensioned)\n- Conductor location information (only the general utility line is marked)\n- Whether the OHE line is distribution or transmission voltage\n- Root barrier details for trees near underground equipment\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:\n\n**EL-2.1** (Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution conductor):\n- **Applicability**: YES - distribution line present\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: Cannot determine UC status of proposed species without ECM Appendix F; cannot determine distances without clearance dimensions\n\n**EL-2.2** (Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission conductor):\n- **Applicability**: NO - no transmission line present or indicated\n- **Status**: N/A\n\n**EL-2.3** (Large trees within 25 ft of distribution conductor):\n- **Applicability**: YES - distribution line present\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: Mature heights not specified for proposed trees; cannot determine distances without dimensions\n\n**EL-2.4** (Large trees within 50 ft of transmission conductor):\n- **Applicability**: NO - no transmission line present\n- **Status**: N/A\n\n**EL-2.5** (Trees within transmission easement):\n- **Applicability**: NO - no transmission easement on site\n- **Status**: N/A\n\n**EL-2.6** (Trees within 10 ft of utility pole):\n- **Applicability**: YES - poles shown on plans\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: Pole locations not dimensioned; cannot verify distances\n\n**EL-2.7** (Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment):\n- **Applicability**: UNCLEAR - underground equipment shown on Sheet 21 but pad-mounted equipment not clearly identified\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: Cannot clearly identify pad-mounted equipment locations or confirm if any are present\n\n**EL-2.8** (Trees within 5 ft of underground electric equipment):\n- **Applicability**: YES - underground electric equipment shown on Sheet 21\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: Underground equipment locations and tree proximity not dimensioned\n\n**EL-2.9** (Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment lacking root barriers):\n- **Applicability**: YES - underground equipment present\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: No root barrier details provided on landscape plan; cannot verify proximity\n\n**EL-2.10** (Plant legend doesn't identify species):\n- **Applicability**: YES - trees proposed near overhead facilities\n- **Status**: FAIL\n- **Reason**: Landscape plan (Sheet 31) uses letter codes (M, SY, PL, P) but provides no cross-reference to botanical names. The plant schedule exists on Sheet 35, but the landscape plan itself does not identify which species is planted where.\n\n**EL-2.11** (Large trees not differentiated on plans):\n- **Applicability**: YES - trees proposed\n- **Status**: FAIL\n- **Reason**: Landscape plan does not indicate mature heights for any proposed trees; cannot distinguish large trees (40+ ft) from other trees on the plan\n\n**EL-2.12** (Clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor):\n- **Applicability**: YES - clearances would be applicable if trees are proposed near poles\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: No clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan at all; cannot verify the method of measurement\n\n**EL-2.13** (Clearances measured from tree canopy instead of trunk):\n- **Applicability**: YES - if clearances were to be shown\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: No clearance dimensions shown; cannot verify measurement method\n\n**EL-2.14** (Trees not shown in relation to overhead facilities):\n- **Applicability**: YES - overhead facilities present\n- **Status**: FAIL\n- **Reason**: While trees ARE shown on the landscape plan and the OHE line IS shown, the plans do not provide sufficient clarity to verify clearances because: (1) no dimension lines or measurements from trees to OHE conductor, (2) no species identification on the landscape plan for trees near OHE, (3) no pole locations dimensioned, (4) insufficient relationship documentation to verify compliance\n\n**EL-2.15** (Trees within prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval):\n- **Applicability**: YES - if any trees are in prohibited zones\n- **Status**: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- **Reason**: Cannot determine if any trees are in prohibited zones without clearance dimensions and species/height identification\n\nNow let me compile the structured output with all findings (pass, fail, not-verifiable, and n/a):"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bd4df49-5a3c-4afa-8eeb-b16b6883780f","uuid":"a632ff15-6264-4718-a94f-70f11dbdfa36"}
