{"level":30,"time":1778246507091,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W0B56112XVW1JVX80Z4FN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping 13 (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Total Checklist Items Evaluated:** 39\n\n**Breakdown by Status:**\n- **FAIL:** 4 items (10%)\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE:** 26 items (67%)\n- **N/A:** 9 items (23%)\n- **PASS:** 0 items\n\n### Critical Deficiencies (FAIL Items):\n\n1. **EL-13.31** — No cross-section drawings provided showing vertical clearances in access paths despite multi-story buildings (up to 40 feet) with parking garages present on site.\n\n2. **EL-13.34** — Transformer pad locations not verified against recorded easements. Facts.md identifies two critical perpetual easements NOT depicted on submitted plans: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 acres NE interior, no-build zone) and City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 acres NE corner). Additionally, GIS-confirmed easements from Cortez Heights plat (25-foot drainage, 7.5-foot PUE at NE boundary) not verified on submitted plans.\n\n3. **EL-13.35** — No transformer easements depicted on plat or site plan. Required easement boundaries and accessibility width for Austin Energy maintenance not documented.\n\n4. **EL-13.37** — Transformer pad detail sheets per Austin Energy Design standards completely absent. Pad dimensions, construction specifications, and service type (single-phase vs. three-phase) not provided.\n\n### Primary Documentation Gaps Preventing Verification:\n\n- No clearance dimensions documented between any transformer and buildings, structures, utilities, or site features\n- No transformer pad detail drawings with AE Design specifications\n- No specification of transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n- No cross-referenced utility coordination showing clearances to water, wastewater, or storm drain lines\n- No electrical routing verification showing 100% private property path from transformer to meters\n- No cross-section drawings for overhead distribution line clearances\n- Transformers not overlaid on landscape plan; tree proximity cannot be assessed\n\nThe review has been completed and all 39 checklist items have been evaluated with detailed reasoning provided in the structured output above."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bbc8513-4a76-42d1-91f8-a8d89a310ed5","uuid":"2c580ef6-fc54-4945-a224-5772e208b706"}
