istance from this hydrant to transformer pads is not dimensioned, preventing verification of minimum 5-foot clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 shows one private fire hydrant location. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. No dimension lines or distance callouts connect the hydrant to any transformer pad.","reasoning":"While a fire hydrant exists on site (applicability condition met), measured distance from the hydrant to each transformer pad is not provided, making compliance verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4; ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations where trees are within 10 lateral feet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not depicted on landscape plan (Sheet 31), preventing verification of tree species utility-compatibility for trees within 10 feet of pads or 15 feet of overhead distribution lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and vegetation symbols but does not include transformer pad location overlays. Transformer pad locations from Sheet 21 cannot be cross-referenced with tree locations.","reasoning":"Without transformer pads depicted on the landscape plan, proximity relationships between trees and transformer equipment cannot be assessed. Tree species identification and utility-compatibility certification cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations adjacent to landscaping"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door orientation is not identified on any plan. Shrub and low-lying vegetation clearance requirements (10 feet from access door, 5 feet from other sides) cannot be verified without transformer pad details showing door location.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows landscaping details but transformers are not overlaid for proximity comparison. Sheet 21 shows transformers without access door orientation markings.","reasoning":"Access door orientation is fundamental to applying the different clearance requirements (10 feet vs. 5 feet). Without this designation, compliance cannot be assessed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are not shown on landscape plan. Root barrier specifications (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) cannot be verified for trees within 20 feet of transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) contains no root barrier details or transformer pad location references. Tree proximity to underground transformer equipment cannot be determined.","reasoning":"Without transformer locations overlaid on the landscape plan or root barrier callouts on detail sheets, this requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plans (Sheets 9 and 21) show building layouts and utilities. No dumpster or trash receptacle symbols are identified near transformer pads.","reasoning":"The triggering condition (dumpster proximity) is not present on the plans. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bicycle racks are shown on site plan but not adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 31 identify bicycle parking locations (long-term and short-term). These are not positioned near any transformer pad.","reasoning":"Bike racks exist on site but not within triggering proximity to transformers. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations where light poles may be adjacent"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations relative to transformer pads are not documented or dimensioned on the electrical or site plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 references exterior lighting and Figure 34 showing fixture types, but specific light pole locations and distances from transformer pads are not provided.","reasoning":"Without light pole location callouts on the electrical plan or site plan, proximity to transformers cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations near fire lanes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows fire lanes, but measured distance from fire lane centerline or striping to transformer pads on Sheet 21 is not dimensioned.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 depicts fire lanes with red curb striping and signage notes. Sheet 21 shows transformer locations. No dimension lines or callouts measure distance between fire lanes and transformers.","reasoning":"While fire lanes are clearly defined on the site, the specific clearance distance from each transformer to fire lane boundaries is not documented, preventing compliance verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Spacing between multiple transformer pads on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on electrical plan but no dimensions or callouts indicate the distances between individual pads. Minimum 5-foot separation cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 depicts 5 transformer pads in different locations. No dimension lines connect pads to show inter-pad spacing.","reasoning":"Multiple transformers are shown (applicability condition met), but clearance between them is not documented. Compliance cannot be verified without dimensions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water utility lines are shown on utility tap plan (Sheet 19) but no overlay on electrical plan (Sheet 21) or dimension callouts verify the 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance between transformer pads and water service lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 depicts water line routing. Sheet 21 shows transformer locations. The two documents are not spatially coordinated with dimension lines showing distance between water lines and transformers.","reasoning":"While utilities are shown on different sheets, no cross-referenced dimensions or clearance callouts on a single integrated utility plan demonstrate the required 5-foot separation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater service lines are shown on utility tap plan (Sheet 19) but clearance distance from transformer pads is not dimensioned or verified on an integrated utility plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 shows wastewater service routing at 6-inch PVC. Sheet 21 shows transformer pads. No coordinated dimension lines between the two sheets indicate separation distances.","reasoning":"Utilities are documented on separate sheets without integrated spatial verification of the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain infrastructure is shown on storm sewer plan (Sheet 12) but no overlay or dimension callouts verify minimum 5-foot clearance between transformer pads and storm lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Storm drain layout is depicted on Sheet 12. Transformer locations are on Sheet 21. The two documents are not coordinated with dimension lines showing transformer-to-storm-drain distances.","reasoning":"Separate utility systems are documented on separate sheets. Without integrated spatial coordination, clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service infrastructure is shown on the utility plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) and grading plan (Sheet 11) depict water, wastewater, storm drain, and electric utilities. No gas lines or meters are identified.","reasoning":"Gas infrastructure is not present on the site. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-referenced dimensions on utility sheets verify the minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to underground utilities (conduits, communication cables, etc.).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utilities are shown on separate sheets (19, 21) with no coordinated dimension callouts indicating 12-inch minimum separations.","reasoning":"Without integrated utility coordination drawings or dimension callouts showing 12-inch clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No utility coordination drawing, conflict analysis, or cross-section details verify that transformer pads are not located over/under other utility lines or that customer structures are not installed over AE underground facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformers and utilities on plan view without vertical cross-sections or utility conflict callouts.","reasoning":"Three-dimensional utility relationships require cross-section drawings or explicit coordination notes. Neither is provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations where overhead distribution lines are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric (OHE) lines are indicated on plans (shown as dashed lines), but no cross-section drawings or dimension callouts document the 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from transformer pads to overhead distribution conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines are depicted on Sheets 21 and 31. No cross-section views or vertical clearance annotations are provided.","reasoning":"Vertical clearance compliance requires cross-section drawings showing conductor height above grade and clearance distance. These documents are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations near overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution conductors and poles are shown on site plan but no radial clearance dimensions (15-foot radius measured from conductor centerline) are provided to verify compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows overhead electric lines and poles. No radial dimension callouts indicate the 15-foot separation distance.","reasoning":"Radial clearance requirement requires explicit dimension callouts from conductor location to transformer or site features. These are absent.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pad is indicated to be located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint) or enclosed area configuration.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads at grade level adjacent to open areas. No niche or enclosed installation is noted.","reasoning":"Niche service configuration is not documented on the plans. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transformer is shown in a building niche or enclosed configuration on any sheet.","reasoning":"Niche service is not a proposed feature. Requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad access paths; parking garage areas; overhead structures above or adjacent to transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances in access paths are provided. Buildings on site are multi-story structures (up to 40 feet in height) with parking areas and overhanging elements. Cross-sections demonstrating clearance from transformer locations to overhead structures and parking garage ceilings are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows 8 buildings up to 40 feet tall with parking garages. Sheet 21 shows transformer locations at grade. No vertical cross-section drawings are provided in the plan set to show clearance relationships.","reasoning":"Multi-story structures with parking garages are present above or adjacent to transformer locations. Cross-section drawings are mandatory for verification of vertical clearances per UCM. Their absence is a deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations and adjacent grading"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan. If transformers are oil-filled, drainage direction away from buildings must be verified on grading plan; grading plan does not document surface flow direction around transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformers without type specification. Sheet 11 shows grading with contours and flow arrows but transformer locations are not labeled, preventing verification of drainage direction.","reasoning":"Without equipment type documentation, the applicability condition cannot be determined. If oil-filled equipment is proposed, grading analysis is incomplete.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Easement exhibit (Sheet 2, plat) does not show transformer easement boundaries. Transformer pad locations on Sheet 21 are not cross-referenced with the plat to verify 100% installation on private property and not on property lines or in right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat sheet (2) shows easements and property boundaries. Electrical sheet (21) shows transformer locations. No overlay or cross-reference verifies property line relationship.","reasoning":"Without coordinated plat and electrical overlays showing transformer location relative to property lines, private property requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations; drainage easements; water easements; sewer easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Facts.md documents two critical unrecorded easements NOT depicted on submitted site plan: (1) Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres in NE interior, perpetual no-build zone); (2) City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 acres in NE corner). Transformer pad locations relative to these easements are not verified. Additionally, GIS-confirmed easements (25-foot drainage, 7.5-foot PUE from Cortez Heights plat at NE boundary) are not confirmed on submitted plans. Transformer placement in prohibited easement areas cannot be ruled out.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md identifies perpetual easements recorded in Travis County that are NOT shown on site plan submitted for review. Electrical sheet (21) shows transformer locations without easement overlay.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.4 requires transformers to not be located in prohibited easements without written AE Design approval. The presence of undepicted easements and lack of easement-transformer overlay creates a compliance gap that cannot be resolved from submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements are depicted on plat or site plan. Easement width and accessibility requirements for Austin Energy maintenance and inspection access are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat sheet (2) shows utilities easements but no transformer-specific easement callouts. Electrical sheet (21) shows transformer locations without surrounding easement boundaries.","reasoning":"UCM requires transformer easements for AE Design accessibility. Complete absence from easement exhibit and site plan is a documentation deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformer to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformers to meter locations is shown on Sheet 21 but no notation or overlay indicates whether routing is 100% on private property. Routing does not cross right-of-way or public easements cannot be verified without property line overlay.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer and meter locations with connecting lines. Property lines are not clearly marked relative to routing on this sheet.","reasoning":"Without property line overlay on the electrical plan or explicit notation stating 100% private property routing, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6; UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad detail sheets per Austin Energy Design standards are not included in the plan set. Pad dimensions and construction specifications required by UCM § 1.18.0 and AE Design are absent. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) is not documented to allow verification of pad size compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis and review of all sheets confirms no transformer pad detail drawing or specification sheet exists in the 39-sheet set. Sheet 21 shows locations only as basic rectangles.","reasoning":"Complete absence of AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets is a critical documentation deficiency. Pad dimensions cannot be verified to match service type and load requirements.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No bollard specifications or details are provided. Proximity of transformer pads to parking spaces, drive aisles, and vehicle circulation areas is not dimensioned, preventing determination of whether bollard protection is required or adequately specified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows parking layout. Sheet 21 shows transformer locations. No dimension lines indicate distance from transformers to parking edges or drive aisles. No bollard detail drawings are present.","reasoning":"Without documented distances from transformers to parking/vehicle areas and without bollard details, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, structures) in relation to overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution line locations are shown on site plan but no cross-section drawings or explicit clearance callouts verify that building structures, parking garages, and other customer improvements are not installed under or over these overhead facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows overhead electric (OHE) lines as dashed lines. Buildings and parking structures are depicted on site plan. No vertical cross-section or conflict callout verifies clearance compliance.","reasoning":"Three-dimensional spatial relationships require cross-section views or explicit clearance verification. These are not provided.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c0fed34c-3799-4431-8df8-61b97f104dc2"}
