{"level":30,"time":1778246550018,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W1NYYH9BEJWYF3C7VDPYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). Here's a summary of my findings:\n\n## Review Summary\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping IS APPLICABLE. The site has:\n- An overhead electric distribution line (OHE) shown on Sheets 9 and 31\n- Proposed trees listed in the plant schedule (Sheet 35)\n- No transmission easements or transmission facilities\n- Underground electrical equipment\n\n**Key Deficiencies Found:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)** — Plant legend incomplete: The landscape plan uses letter codes (M, SY, PL, P) to identify trees by functional category but provides no species identification on that sheet. The plant schedule exists on Sheet 35 but is not cross-referenced to plan locations.\n\n2. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)** — Large trees not differentiated: The landscape plan shows tree symbols but does not indicate mature heights. Without height designation, viewers cannot identify which trees are \"large trees\" (40+ feet) subject to more restrictive clearance requirements.\n\n3. **EL-2.14 (FAIL)** — Insufficient relationship documentation: While the OHE line and trees are shown on the landscape plan, clearance verification is prevented by: (a) no dimension lines showing distances from trees to the conductor; (b) no species identification on the plan; (c) no dimensioned pole locations.\n\n**Major Verification Gaps:**\n\n- **No clearance dimensions:** No measurements are shown from any trees to the overhead electric conductor, poles, or equipment\n- **Utility-compatible status unknown:** Cannot verify UC designation of proposed species (ECM Appendix F not provided)\n- **Mature heights not specified:** Sheet 35 provides container sizes but not mature heights needed to identify large trees\n- **Equipment overlay missing:** Underground electrical equipment locations (Sheet 21) are not cross-referenced with tree locations (Sheet 31)\n\n**Items Not Applicable:**\n- EL-2.2, EL-2.4: Transmission facilities not present\n- EL-2.5: No transmission easement on site\n\n**Items Not Verifiable (due to missing clearance dimensions and documentation):**\n- EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.12, EL-2.13, EL-2.15\n\nThe structured findings output has been provided with detailed agent traces and citations for each item."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bd4df49-5a3c-4afa-8eeb-b16b6883780f","uuid":"5e8cd1ff-16b7-4154-9c0a-f77d05074acf"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246550059,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":345880,"duration_api_ms":182754,"num_turns":25,"result":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). Here's a summary of my findings:\n\n## Review Summary\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping IS APPLICABLE. The site has:\n- An overhead electric distribution line (OHE) shown on Sheets 9 and 31\n- Proposed trees listed in the plant schedule (Sheet 35)\n- No transmission easements or transmission facilities\n- Underground electrical equipment\n\n**Key Deficiencies Found:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)** — Plant legend incomplete: The landscape plan uses letter codes (M, SY, PL, P) to identify trees by functional category but provides no species identification on that sheet. The plant schedule exists on Sheet 35 but is not cross-referenced to plan locations.\n\n2. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)** — Large trees not differentiated: The landscape plan shows tree symbols but does not indicate mature heights. Without height designation, viewers cannot identify which trees are \"large trees\" (40+ feet) subject to more restrictive clearance requirements.\n\n3. **EL-2.14 (FAIL)** — Insufficient relationship documentation: While the OHE line and trees are shown on the landscape plan, clearance verification is prevented by: (a) no dimension lines showing distances from trees to the conductor; (b) no species identification on the plan; (c) no dimensioned pole locations.\n\n**Major Verification Gaps:**\n\n- **No clearance dimensions:** No measurements are shown from any trees to the overhead electric conductor, poles, or equipment\n- **Utility-compatible status unknown:** Cannot verify UC designation of proposed species (ECM Appendix F not provided)\n- **Mature heights not specified:** Sheet 35 provides container sizes but not mature heights needed to identify large trees\n- **Equipment overlay missing:** Underground electrical equipment locations (Sheet 21) are not cross-referenced with tree locations (Sheet 31)\n\n**Items Not Applicable:**\n- EL-2.2, EL-2.4: Transmission facilities not present\n- EL-2.5: No transmission easement on site\n\n**Items Not Verifiable (due to missing clearance dimensions and documentation):**\n- EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.12, EL-2.13, EL-2.15\n\nThe structured findings output has been provided with detailed agent traces and citations for each item.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8bd4df49-5a3c-4afa-8eeb-b16b6883780f","total_cost_usd":0.33031069999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":3065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111548,"cache_read_input_tokens":965657,"output_tokens":18249,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":111548},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3065,"outputTokens":18249,"cacheReadInputTokens":965657,"cacheCreationInputTokens":111548,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.33031069999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Bottom and east property boundaries where overhead electric distribution line is present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric distribution line (OHE) is present on the site. Proposed tree species are listed on Sheet 35 (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but utility-compatible (UC) status cannot be verified from submitted documents as ECM Appendix F is not included. Additionally, no clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan to verify whether any non-utility-compatible trees are within the required 15-foot lateral distance from the distribution conductor.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line marked 'OHE' is shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31). Four tree species are listed in the plant schedule (Sheet 35). The landscape plan shows tree symbols with letter codes (M, SY, PL) but no species identification. No clearance dimensions are shown from trees to the OHE line.","reasoning":"To evaluate this deficiency, one must: (1) identify proposed tree species locations, (2) cross-reference each species against ECM Appendix F for UC designation, and (3) measure lateral distance from tree trunk center to conductor. Steps (2) and (3) cannot be completed from the submitted documents—ECM Appendix F is not provided, and clearance dimensions are not shown on the plan. Therefore, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead electric transmission line (60kV or higher) is indicated on the site plan. The OHE line shown is a distribution facility. Therefore, transmission clearance requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plans (Sheets 9 and 31) show only one overhead electric line labeled 'OHE' running along property boundaries. No transmission easement, transmission line, or transmission voltage designation is present in the site plan or facts.md. Facts.md confirms no transmission easement.","reasoning":"The grouping explicitly states that transmission requirements apply only when transmission facilities (60kV or higher, typically with dedicated easements and larger structures) are present or proposed. This project has only distribution facilities, so transmission clearance requirements are not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near the overhead electric distribution line along south and east property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed tree species list does not include mature height specifications. Sheet 35 provides minimum container sizes (100 gal., 45 gal.) and caliper inches (4\", 2.5\") but not the mature heights required to determine which trees are 'large trees' (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Without mature height data and clearance dimensions, compliance with the 25-foot distribution clearance requirement for large trees cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists four tree species with container and caliper specifications but no mature heights. The grouping requires consulting ECM Appendix F for mature heights to identify 'large trees.' The landscape plan shows tree locations but no dimensions to the OHE line.","reasoning":"Evaluating this deficiency requires: (1) identifying mature heights of each proposed species, (2) locating which trees are large (40+ feet), and (3) measuring lateral distance from those trees to the conductor. The submitted documents lack (1) and (3). Even though species are identified in the plant schedule, their mature heights are not provided, making it impossible to determine which are large trees.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead electric transmission line is present on the site. Therefore, transmission clearance requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows only distribution-level overhead electric line. Facts.md confirms no transmission easement. No voltage designation or transmission infrastructure indicators are present.","reasoning":"Transmission facility clearance requirements are gated behind the applicability condition that transmission facilities must be present. This condition is not met on this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on the site. Facts.md confirms the property is not subject to any transmission easement boundaries. The 5-foot electric easements shown in easement section of facts.md are plat-dedicated distribution easements, not transmission easements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md lists easements present on the property, including 5-foot electric easements (plat-dedicated from Mecey Subdivision). No transmission easement is listed or described.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only when a transmission easement is present on the site. The easement applicability gate is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where utility poles are shown along the overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility pole symbols are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) and site plan (Sheet 9) along the OHE line, but their exact locations are not dimensioned. Proposed tree locations are shown but no clearance dimensions are provided from trees to the poles. Therefore, the 10-foot lateral clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Pole symbols (circles with crosses) are visible on Sheets 9 and 31 along the OHE line. Trees are also shown on the landscape plan. However, no coordinate dimensions are provided for pole positions, and no distance measurements are shown from trees to poles.","reasoning":"Verifying compliance requires knowing: (1) exact pole locations and (2) exact tree locations, then measuring the lateral distance. The landscape plan shows graphical positions but lacks the dimensional information needed for precise verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where pad-mounted electrical equipment may be located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, electrical meters) but does not clearly distinguish pad-mounted equipment from other electrical elements. The landscape plan does not show electrical equipment locations in relation to proposed trees. Therefore, compliance with the 10-foot clearance requirement from pad-mounted equipment cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical design plan indicates transformers and pull boxes but does not specifically identify which are pad-mounted versus other types. Sheet 31 landscape plan does not show electrical equipment overlaid with tree locations.","reasoning":"To verify this deficiency, one must: (1) identify pad-mounted equipment locations, (2) identify tree locations, (3) measure distance. The submitted documents do not clearly accomplish steps (1) and (2) in a way that allows dimensional verification.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where underground electrical equipment is located near proposed trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical elements but the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not overlay electrical equipment locations with proposed tree locations. Clearance dimensions from trees to underground equipment are not shown. The 5-foot lateral clearance requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electrical infrastructure. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows proposed trees. The two plans are not cross-referenced with dimensional callouts showing distances from trees to equipment.","reasoning":"Verification requires overlaying the two plans and measuring distances. The lack of dimensional cross-reference or clearance callouts prevents verification.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While underground electrical equipment is shown on Sheet 21, the landscape plan does not provide root barrier specifications or details. No clearance dimensions are shown from trees to underground equipment to determine whether any trees fall within the 20-foot threshold requiring root barriers. Root barrier requirements therefore cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 landscape calculations and notes do not mention root barriers for electric equipment. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows no root barrier details or callouts. Sheet 21 shows underground equipment but does not indicate proximity to trees.","reasoning":"This deficiency applies only when trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment. Without clearance dimensions and without identification of which trees (if any) meet this proximity threshold, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan areas near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) uses abbreviation codes to label tree locations (M = Mitigation Tree, SY = Street Yard Tree, PL = Parking Lot Tree, P = Parking Buffer Point Tree) but provides no legend on that sheet correlating these codes to the specific botanical names. The plant schedule with species identification is located on a separate sheet (Sheet 35). A reader cannot determine which species is planted at which location on the landscape plan without cross-referencing multiple sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 Block 5 provides a legend defining M, SY, PL, and P as tree categories (function type) but not species names. Sheet 35 lists botanical names for proposed trees but these are not keyed to the location symbols on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"A complete plant legend must allow a reader to identify the species of each tree shown on the landscape plan. Splitting the identification across two sheets without cross-reference symbols prevents verification of species at specific plan locations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan showing proposed trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan does not indicate mature heights for any of the proposed trees. Sheet 35 provides minimum container specifications and caliper sizes but does not specify the mature height for any tree species. Without mature height information on or cross-referenced to the landscape plan, large trees (those with mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) cannot be differentiated from smaller trees, making it impossible to verify clearance compliance for large trees from overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows tree symbols but no mature height labels or notes. Sheet 35 plant schedule lists species names and container sizes (100 gal., 45 gal., etc.) and caliper (4\", 2.5\") but not mature heights.","reasoning":"The grouping specifies that large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are subject to more restrictive clearance requirements (25 feet from distribution, 50 feet from transmission). Without mature height designation on the landscape plan, viewers cannot identify which proposed trees are large trees requiring this special scrutiny.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan areas where clearance dimensions are or should be shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan from trees to the overhead electric conductor or poles. Because no dimensions are present, the method of measurement (whether from pole centerline versus conductor, whether from trunk center versus canopy edge) cannot be evaluated. If clearance dimensions were to be added to the plan, they must originate from the outside conductor position, not pole centerline.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan contains no dimension lines, labels, or measurements indicating distance from trees to the OHE line or to pole locations.","reasoning":"This deficiency can be evaluated only if clearance dimensions are shown on the plans. Since no such dimensions exist, the specific method of measurement cannot be assessed. This is a prerequisite verification gap rather than a measurement error.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan areas where clearance dimensions are or should be shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan. Because dimensions are absent, it cannot be determined whether any dimensions that may exist elsewhere originate from tree trunk centers (correct) or tree canopy edges (incorrect). Proper clearance measurement must originate from tree trunk center (planting location).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan contains no clearance dimension callouts or measurements to utility features.","reasoning":"Without dimensions present on the plans, the measurement reference point (trunk vs. canopy edge) cannot be evaluated. This deficiency is not-verifiable pending the addition of clearance dimensions to the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Bottom and east property boundaries where the overhead electric line is located and trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While the overhead electric line (OHE) is shown on the landscape plan and tree symbols are present, the plans do not provide sufficient information to verify clearances. Specifically: (1) no dimension lines or distance measurements are provided from trees to the OHE conductor; (2) the tree symbols on the landscape plan are not identified by species (only by functional category: M, SY, PL), so utility-compatibility cannot be assessed; (3) utility pole locations are shown graphically but not dimensioned. The lack of dimensional cross-reference and species identification prevents verification that trees comply with required clearance distances from overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows the OHE line and tree symbols. Vision checks confirmed: (a) no clearance dimensions from trees to OHE, (b) no species identification on the landscape plan for trees near utilities, (c) poles shown but not dimensioned, (d) no notes addressing utility clearances.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires that when overhead facilities are present and trees are proposed, the landscape plan must show sufficient relationship information to verify compliance. The submitted plan shows the general presence of both but lacks the specific dimensional and species identification information needed for verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Anywhere trees are proposed within restricted clearance zones (less than 15 ft from distribution conductor, less than 50 ft from transmission conductor, less than 25 ft for large trees from distribution, less than 10 ft from poles, less than 10 ft from pad-mounts, less than 5 ft from underground equipment, or within transmission easement)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine whether any trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones without: (1) species identification with UC status verification against ECM Appendix F, (2) mature height identification to determine if trees are large (40+ feet), (3) clearance dimensions from trees to conductors and equipment. Therefore, it cannot be determined whether Austin Energy written approval is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show trees and utilities but lack the dimensional and species-identification documentation needed to identify prohibited zone violations. No correspondence from Austin Energy regarding approvals is evident in the visible plan documents.","reasoning":"This deficiency can only be evaluated after determining whether trees are actually in prohibited zones (which requires the missing information above). Without that determination, the need for Austin Energy approval cannot be assessed.","tools_used":[]}}],"grouping":"2"},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"3da028a3-cc68-479e-9200-fd85f570f149"}
