conductor elevations are provided, and no vertical clearance dimensions document the 30-foot minimum clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transmission requirements in Block 13 suggest transmission lines affect site. Driveway grade elevations shown on Sheet 11 but no conductor elevation data provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 requires 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines to road surface. Without surveyed conductor elevations, clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This is a local residential development, not a highway or freeway project. No distribution underbuilt on transmission structures applies to this site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Valley View Townhomes is a 39-unit residential townhome project on a 2.16-acre local property.","reasoning":"Applicability condition not met - highway or freeway grading not proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["if poles conflict with driveway locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and site plan (Sheet 9). Proposed driveway alignments are shown on the site plan. No explicit conflict is visible between pole locations on adjacent ROW and proposed driveway locations, but no relocation notes or updated pole locations are documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Poles are shown on Sheets 4 and 9 on/near property boundary. Proposed driveways shown on Sheet 9 appear not to conflict with visible pole locations.","reasoning":"No apparent conflict between poles and driveways visible on site plan. If conflict exists, relocation notes or updated pole locations would be required but are not documented.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all locations where clearance dimensions should be shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets from overhead electric conductors to site features. Where clearance dimensions should exist (showing measurement from outside conductor, not pole center), they are absent entirely. Critical measurement annotations are missing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of site plan, grading plan, wall details, and other sheets shows zero dimension annotations measuring clearances from overhead conductors to any site features.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (not pole centerline). Since no clearance dimensions are documented at all, this critical deficiency cannot be assessed for proper measurement origin.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Photometric plan and site plan reviewed. No streetlight poles are shown to be located directly beneath the routing of overhead electric lines shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan and landscape plan show building-mounted lighting and area lighting locations. No streetlights are positioned under OHE line routes.","reasoning":"Applicability condition effectively met - no streetlight poles placed under overhead lines on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["property ends along Valley View Road ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are shown along the western property boundary (Valley View Road). Existing power poles are shown on the survey near property corners. Relationship between sidewalk alignment and pole locations at property ends is not dimensioned or verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Poles are marked on existing survey (Sheet 4). Proposed sidewalk alignments shown on site plan (Sheet 9) but no dimension lines show distance between sidewalk and poles at property line intersections.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires sidewalks cleared from poles at each end. Without dimension documentation of sidewalk to pole clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["trash collection and enclosed trash areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash collection is addressed in site plan notes (Block 9 of Sheet 3). Trash enclosure locations are shown on site plan. Clearance verification from trash receptacle locations to overhead electric lines is not documented, and raised height considerations during service are not addressed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash areas but provides no dimension showing distance from OHE lines. No note specifies clearance requirement for raised trash bins during pickup.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention addresses safety of raised trash containers under overhead lines. Clearance verification and 7.5-foot minimum requirement not documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["site-wide"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis confirms that no buildings, overhangs, canopies, or other customer facilities are shown positioned directly beneath or over the routed overhead electric lines. All buildings maintain setback from property boundaries where OHE lines are located, with Buildings 1-2 setback approximately 25.8-26.1 feet from western property line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of site plan shows building layouts relative to OHE line routing. All structures are setback from OHE lines; none are directly beneath them.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 absolute prohibition against structures under overhead distribution is not violated. Setbacks appear adequate at plan view.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed water meter connection point, but no dimension shows clearance from water meter location to any overhead electric service drops. Clearance verification is absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 marks water meter tap location but provides no dimension to overhead conductors. No overhead service drop elevation survey is provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 and § 1.10.6.2 require 7.5-foot clearance from service drops to water meters. Clearance documentation is missing.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["water line routing near poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water utility plan shows water line routing, but clearance dimensions from water lines to overhead electrical distribution poles and conductors are not provided. Clearance verification is absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 20-21 show water utility routing but no dimension lines show distance from water lines to OHE poles or conductors.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires documentation of clearances between utilities. Clearance documentation is missing.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["permanent structure foundations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows all permanent structure foundations (buildings 1-8) setback significantly more than 5 feet from the property lines where electric facilities might be located. Buildings 1-2 are setback 25.8-26.1 feet from western property boundary, exceeding the 5-foot clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of site plan shows all buildings setback approximately 25+ feet from property boundary.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires 5-foot clearance space for electric facilities. Building setbacks significantly exceed this minimum.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["driveways and other site features beneath overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities exist on multiple boundaries of the site. Proposed driveways, parking areas, and retaining walls are located in proximity to overhead lines. No registered surveyor data is provided showing pole locations, mid-span clearances, or conductor elevations. Survey of electrical infrastructure clearances is entirely absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows OHE lines on western, northern, and southern boundaries. Driveways and site features run parallel to these boundaries. No survey data documentation for conductor elevations or mid-span clearances exists in the site plan package.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyor data when vertical clearances appear marginal. Given proximity of site features to OHE lines, registered surveyor mid-span clearance documentation is necessary but absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines shown on site plan run parallel to property boundaries (western, northern, and southern). No overhead electric lines cross roadways on the site; they border the perimeter. Orientation of line crossings is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE lines on site run along property boundaries, not crossing proposed roadways or driveways internally.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires 90-degree orientation for line crossings. No line crossings of roadways exist on this site.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows underground electrical service infrastructure. Utility plan does not clearly distinguish between primary and secondary overhead electric lines where they cross each other. Documentation of overhead line crossing details is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site electrical design (Sheet 21) addresses underground infrastructure. No detail view of overhead line crossing configurations is provided.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires secondary over primary orientation. Without documented crossing details, compliance cannot be verified, but this may be inapplicable if no secondary/primary crossings exist.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on this residential townhome development.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows no marquee or large signage structures.","reasoning":"Applicability condition not met - no marquee signs proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows underground electrical service conversion. No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed. Applicability condition not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical design shows underground service with transformers and pull boxes, not new poles.","reasoning":"Applicability condition not met - no new power poles for underground service conversion proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["building-mounted and area lighting"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) addresses exterior lighting requirements noting full cut-off fixture requirements. Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows lighting locations. However, no dimension annotations show clearance distances from decorative lighting fixtures to overhead electric lines, and no relocation notes are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows lighting note requirement for cut-off fixtures. Sheet 10 shows fixture locations. No dimensions from fixtures to OHE lines are shown.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires clearances from lighting to overhead lines. Clearance verification or relocation documentation is absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape areas, parking lot trees, street yard trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows proposed tree plantings throughout site, including areas in proximity to overhead electric lines on western, northern, and southern boundaries. However, tree species are not cross-referenced against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible (UC) list, and no lateral distance annotations show distance from proposed trees to overhead conductors. Compliance with tree species restrictions cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows tree plantings with plant list. No reference to ECM Appendix F UC list for utility-compatible species. No dimension annotations show distance from trees near OHE lines to the conductors.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires utility-compatible trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission and within 10 lateral feet of distribution. Tree species verification and distance documentation are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["proposed electric meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows meter pad locations. However, no enlarged detail views verify that working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9) are maintained. No analysis of obstructions from buildings, fences, walls, or landscaping is provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 marks meter locations but provides no detail showing working clearance spaces or obstruction analysis.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.9.3.1 requires obstruction-free meter access. Verification of clearance spaces and obstruction analysis are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["if streetlight poles exist adjacent to site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed buildings are located near Valley View Road where streetlight poles may exist. No dimension shows clearance distance from building locations to existing streetlight pole locations. Clearance verification is absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Buildings 1-2 are adjacent to Valley View Road ROW where streetlights likely exist, but no clearance dimensions are documented.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires clearance maintenance from development to existing streetlights. Clearance documentation is missing.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["if down guy wires from poles near driveways or accessible paths"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles on and adjacent to property. Down guy wires from these poles are not explicitly depicted on any plan sheet, though such infrastructure frequently exists at utility pole locations. Potential conflicts with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features cannot be verified without complete down guy wire documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Poles shown on Sheets 4 and 9. Down guy anchors not explicitly marked on plans. Site notes acknowledge that electric utility infrastructure details may be omitted.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.17.0 requires resolution of down guy conflicts. Down guy documentation is absent, preventing verification of conflict resolution.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Angled guy easements for transmission structures are not applicable unless transmission angled guys from towers are present and require dedicated easements. If transmission facilities affect the site, this would be addressed through transmission easement documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transmission notes in Block 13 address transmission structure requirements but do not indicate angled guy anchor easements are required.","reasoning":"Applicability dependent on specific transmission structure type. No angled guy easements appear to be required for this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["if down guy anchors exist on property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat sheet (Sheet 2) shows easement boundaries but does not explicitly identify down guy anchor easements. If down guy anchors from poles near the property exist, dedicated 10-foot-wide easements extending 5 feet past ground entry points are required but not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat shows various easements but no specific down guy anchor easement exhibits are provided.","reasoning":"Reviewer Convention requires dedicated down guy easements. Documentation is absent, preventing verification of down guy easement compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed transformers are for underground electrical service per Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan). Pad-mounted transformers do not have overhead electric lines above them. Overhead clearance requirement does not apply to underground service transformers.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground service design with pad-mounted transformers, not pole-mounted transformers beneath overhead lines.","reasoning":"Applicability condition not met - transformers are underground service installations, not beneath overhead lines.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed transformers are pad-mounted underground service installations, not niche service configurations with covered installations. Applicability condition not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical design shows pad-mounted transformers for underground service.","reasoning":"Applicability condition not met - transformers are not in niche configurations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["construction staging areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sequence of construction is outlined on Sheet 3. Erosion control plan (Sheet 5) shows temporary controls, but a detailed construction staging area plan showing equipment placement, crane swing radius, and material storage locations is not provided. Verification that staging areas maintain 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines cannot be determined.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 3 and 5 describe construction sequence and temporary controls, but no detailed site logistics plan showing staging area boundaries and equipment locations is provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 requires 10-foot radial clearance during construction. Staging area plan with clearance verification is absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["site-wide"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3, Block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes), Item #3 includes the required 48-hour notification: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.' This requirement applies to work near high-voltage transmission lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Block 13 Item #3 of Sheet 3 explicitly states '48 hours before commencement of construction' with specific Austin Energy contact information for pre-construction safety meeting.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 incorporates Texas Health & Safety Code requirement for 48-hour notification. Block 13 Item #3 provides required notification language for transmission facility work.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical service. No service-mast through-roof installations are proposed. Applicability condition not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground service configuration with pad-mounted transformers, not overhead service masts through roofs.","reasoning":"Applicability condition not met - underground service proposed, no through-roof masts.","tools_used":[]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a9c15c-2133-427c-a1ff-4e415da2ee73","uuid":"5254cc01-28f8-4fbf-94c2-87c0182072cf"}
