{"level":30,"time":1778246605599,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W3D2P253MR15WWQA050PN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed a comprehensive site plan review for the **Valley View Townhomes** project (39 townhome units on 2.16 acres at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin) against the **EL-MD-EXP: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** grouping.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Overhead Electric Facilities Confirmed:**\n- Overhead electric (OHE) lines exist along the western (Valley View Road), northern, and southern property boundaries\n- Utility poles are documented on the existing conditions survey and site plan\n- Transmission facilities appear to affect the site based on extensive transmission notes in Block 13 of Sheet 3\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n\n1. **Missing Building Elevation Documentation** (FAIL - EL-1.7): No building elevation sheets exist in the 39-sheet site plan package. Surveyed conductor elevations are entirely absent.\n\n2. **Missing Clearance Dimension Exhibits** (FAIL - EL-1.8): Section views showing dimension lines from outer conductors to building edges and other site features are not provided.\n\n3. **Missing Retaining Wall Clearance Sections** (FAIL - EL-1.17): Wall sections show structural details but do not include overhead conductor elevations or clearance dimensions.\n\n4. **No Clearance Dimensions Documented** (FAIL - EL-1.23): Not a single clearance dimension line extends from overhead conductors to any site feature on any plan sheet reviewed.\n\n5. **Missing Mid-Span Clearance Survey** (FAIL - EL-1.31): No registered surveyor data documents pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearances despite site features (driveways, walls, fences) being in proximity to overhead lines.\n\n**Additional Not-Verifiable Items (29 total):** Including clearances for fences, retaining walls, driveways, tree plantings near utilities, meter access, and various site features where visual proximity to overhead lines is apparent but clearance documentation is absent.\n\n**Positive Finding:**\nThe site plan includes a 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting requirement for work near transmission facilities (Sheet 3, Block 13, Item #3), satisfying the Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752 notification requirement.\n\nAll findings have been documented in the structured output above with specific sheet references, code citations, and detailed agent trace reasoning for each item."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a9c15c-2133-427c-a1ff-4e415da2ee73","uuid":"050bd9d9-0f75-4f67-9bb5-d670c90f17f8"}
