{"level":30,"time":1778246632378,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W4BGX1K0YPXA692J7RAJJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I've provided the structured output with all 47 checklist items evaluated. Let me verify I've covered the key findings:\n\n**FINDINGS SUMMARY:**\n\n**FAIL/NOT-VERIFIABLE ITEMS (8 total):**\n1. **EL-1.7** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n2. **EL-1.8** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): No section/profile views showing vertical clearances\n3. **EL-1.18** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): No driveway vertical clearance sections\n4. **EL-1.20** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): No 30-foot transmission clearance verification\n5. **EL-1.23** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): Clearance measurement origin (conductor vs pole) not specified\n6. **EL-1.31** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey\n7. **EL-1.37** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): Trees near overhead lines - species not identified\n8. **EL-1.45** (NOT-VERIFIABLE): Construction staging clearance not documented\n\n**PASS ITEMS (1):**\n1. **EL-1.46** (PASS): 48-hour notification requirement met in Sheet 3\n\n**N/A ITEMS (38):**\nAll distribution facility requirements (EL-1.1 through EL-1.6, EL-1.9-EL-1.10, etc.) and items where applicability conditions are not met.\n\nThe key issue is that the site has **transmission facilities** (not distribution), which has different clearance requirements. However, the more critical issue is the complete absence of **vertical clearance documentation** - no section views, no building elevations showing conductor heights, no mid-span clearance survey, etc.\n\nThe output has been successfully submitted.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","uuid":"6226b603-777e-4e45-96d2-3ddb40efeed7"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246638371,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W4BGX1K0YPXA692J7RAJJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping 1 (Electric Clearances - EL-1). Here's a summary of key findings:\n\n## REVIEW SUMMARY\n\n**Project**: Valley View Townhomes | **Grouping**: 1 — Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\n### Critical Findings\n\n**Infrastructure Type**: The site has **overhead electric TRANSMISSION facilities** (≥60kV per Sheet 3 \"Electric Transmission Notes\"), not distribution facilities. This is a critical distinction because transmission facilities have different clearance requirements under **UCM § 1.14.0** rather than distribution requirements under **UCM § 1.10.3**.\n\n### Items Requiring Attention (8 NOT-VERIFIABLE items)\n\n1. **EL-1.7 & EL-1.8**: No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations or vertical clearance dimensions to building faces and projections\n   \n2. **EL-1.18 & EL-1.20**: No cross-section or profile views showing vertical clearances between finished driveway grades and transmission line heights (30-foot minimum required for transmission)\n\n3. **EL-1.23**: Horizontal clearance dimensions ARE shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3'), but measurement origin (from outside conductor vs. pole centerline) cannot be verified\n\n4. **EL-1.31**: No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey provided—required to verify 30-foot transmission clearance requirement\n\n5. **EL-1.37**: Three mitigation trees shown on landscape plan within 10-15 feet of overhead transmission line, but specific tree species not identified—cannot verify utility-compatible species requirement\n\n6. **EL-1.45**: No construction logistics plan documenting staging areas and equipment operation zones with required 20-foot OSHA clearance from energized transmission lines\n\n### Compliance Confirmed\n\n**EL-1.46** ✓ **PASS**: 48-hour notification requirement is documented in Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes, item #3, requiring pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy before work begins.\n\n### Not Applicable Items (38 items)\n\nMost checklist items apply specifically to **distribution** facilities and are inapplicable when transmission facilities are present. An additional 6-8 items are N/A due to absence of triggering conditions (e.g., no gas pumps, no substations, no marquee signs proposed).\n\nAll 47 checklist items have been individually evaluated with detailed reasoning provided in the structured output."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","uuid":"e1d44c85-243b-43a5-a19a-c7d904a1f84c"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246638411,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":434245,"duration_api_ms":243732,"num_turns":34,"result":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping 1 (Electric Clearances - EL-1). Here's a summary of key findings:\n\n## REVIEW SUMMARY\n\n**Project**: Valley View Townhomes | **Grouping**: 1 — Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\n### Critical Findings\n\n**Infrastructure Type**: The site has **overhead electric TRANSMISSION facilities** (≥60kV per Sheet 3 \"Electric Transmission Notes\"), not distribution facilities. This is a critical distinction because transmission facilities have different clearance requirements under **UCM § 1.14.0** rather than distribution requirements under **UCM § 1.10.3**.\n\n### Items Requiring Attention (8 NOT-VERIFIABLE items)\n\n1. **EL-1.7 & EL-1.8**: No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations or vertical clearance dimensions to building faces and projections\n   \n2. **EL-1.18 & EL-1.20**: No cross-section or profile views showing vertical clearances between finished driveway grades and transmission line heights (30-foot minimum required for transmission)\n\n3. **EL-1.23**: Horizontal clearance dimensions ARE shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3'), but measurement origin (from outside conductor vs. pole centerline) cannot be verified\n\n4. **EL-1.31**: No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey provided—required to verify 30-foot transmission clearance requirement\n\n5. **EL-1.37**: Three mitigation trees shown on landscape plan within 10-15 feet of overhead transmission line, but specific tree species not identified—cannot verify utility-compatible species requirement\n\n6. **EL-1.45**: No construction logistics plan documenting staging areas and equipment operation zones with required 20-foot OSHA clearance from energized transmission lines\n\n### Compliance Confirmed\n\n**EL-1.46** ✓ **PASS**: 48-hour notification requirement is documented in Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes, item #3, requiring pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy before work begins.\n\n### Not Applicable Items (38 items)\n\nMost checklist items apply specifically to **distribution** facilities and are inapplicable when transmission facilities are present. An additional 6-8 items are N/A due to absence of triggering conditions (e.g., no gas pumps, no substations, no marquee signs proposed).\n\nAll 47 checklist items have been individually evaluated with detailed reasoning provided in the structured output.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"eedc0646-e80c-4971-bf87-8e70b8767067","total_cost_usd":0.3922932000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":11824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":139358,"cache_read_input_tokens":750267,"output_tokens":26249,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":139358},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11824,"outputTokens":26249,"cacheReadInputTokens":750267,"cacheCreationInputTokens":139358,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3922932000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This checklist item applies to distribution facilities (primary, neutral, secondary conductors). Site has overhead electric transmission lines (≥60kV) per Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3. Transmission clearance requirements are governed by UCM § 1.14.0, not UCM § 1.10.3.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 General Notes explicitly reference 'Electric Transmission Notes,' 'transmission easement,' 'transmission structures,' and 'transmission lines' throughout multiple note blocks (Blocks 13, 17, 19). The site plan shows overhead utility lines along property boundaries labeled as 'OHE' (Overhead Electric).","reasoning":"The applicability gate requires determining facility type first. The explicit, repeated use of 'transmission' throughout Sheet 3 notes (not 'distribution') establishes these are transmission facilities (≥60kV) per UCM § 1.17.0. Distribution facilities would be <60kV and labeled as 'distribution' or 'primary voltage.' Transmission facilities have separate clearance requirements under UCM § 1.14.0, making distribution-specific items like EL-1.1 inapplicable.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This item applies to distribution primary and neutral conductors only. Site has transmission facilities (governed by UCM § 1.14.0).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site documentation consistently identifies overhead facilities as transmission infrastructure, not distribution.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement; facility is transmission. Applicability gate: transmission present = distribution requirements do not apply.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This item applies to distribution facilities. Site has transmission facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building projections shown on site plan; overhead transmission lines present on boundary.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement for building projections. Facility is transmission, not distribution.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies proposed on site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows residential townhome development with parking, buildings, and detention pond. No gas pumps or fueling infrastructure visible.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: gas pump canopies are not present on this site plan. Item is not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No elevated walkways, stairs, or elevated platforms shown on site plan in conflict with overhead lines.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement; facility is transmission. Also, no elevated structures in conflict visible on plan.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This item applies to buildings near distribution facilities in ROW. Site has transmission facilities (UCM § 1.14.0 governs).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Buildings 1 and 8 are located on western side of site near Valley View Road (ROW). Overhead transmission lines shown on western and eastern property boundaries with horizontal clearances labeled: Building 1 = 26.1', Building 8 = 29.6'.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: transmission facilities (not distribution) are present per Sheet 3 notes. UCM § 1.10.3 applies to distribution facilities; transmission clearances follow UCM § 1.14.0 (30-foot road clearance). Distribution requirement EL-1.6 is inapplicable when transmission is present.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings (buildings 1-8)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations with clearance dimension annotations. Site plan is 2D top-down view only; no vertical elevation views are available.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed all sheet guides and content blocks; site plan (Sheet 9) is identified as a top-down plan view with building data tables and parking requirements. No building elevation sheets, cross-sections, or profile views showing vertical relationships between building roofs/projections and overhead conductors are present in the 39-sheet set.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations and locations on building elevation sheets to demonstrate clearances. Vision analysis confirmed Sheet 9 is purely plan view, containing no elevation data or conductor height information. The absence of building elevation sheets makes the required surveyed conductor elevation data unavailable for verification.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings and projections (buildings 1-8)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section or profile view exhibits provided showing dimension lines from outer conductor to building edges. Horizontal clearance dimensions shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3') but no vertical sections or enlarged details demonstrating clearances from conductor to building projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows horizontal clearance dimensions to overhead electric line (26.1' to Bldg 1, 29.6' to Bldg 8 on west; 21.3' to Bldgs 5-6 on east). Vision analysis of site plan and grading plan confirms these are 2D plan views only; no cross-sections or profile views showing vertical clearance dimensions exist.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires section and plan view exhibits with dimensions from outer conductor to outermost building edge and projections. The plans provide horizontal dimensions only. Vertical clearances cannot be assessed without profile/section views showing conductor elevation relative to roof/projection heights.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape legend shows wooden privacy fences (H.6) proposed on site plan, but no fences shown directly beneath or in contact with overhead transmission lines.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific clearance requirement (7.5-foot sky-to-ground). Facility is transmission. Also, no fence is positioned directly under the overhead line on plan view.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fence posts shown in conflict with existing electric poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows wooden privacy fences on landscape plan legend (H.6) but no fence post locations are dimensioned in relation to electric poles.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: this item applies when fence posts are proposed and overhead poles exist. While fences are proposed, no specific conflicts between fence posts and poles are apparent on the site plan.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation shown on or adjacent to the property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 notes reference transmission easement but no substation facilities are depicted on site plan, utility plan, or electrical design plan.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: 10-foot non-conductive isolation panel requirement applies only to fences adjacent to existing substation fences. No substation present; item inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fencing proposed or required within transmission easement. Detention pond shown in transmission easement instead.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows detention pond located in northeastern area; Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3 identify transmission easement. No fencing is shown within the transmission easement boundaries on site plan, grading plan, or landscape plan.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: fencing beneath/adjacent transmission lines triggers requirement for non-conductive material/grounding. No fence exists in transmission easement per plans. Detention pond is the structure shown, not fencing.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities. No vehicle barrier fencing shown beneath overhead lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No vehicle barrier posts or fencing are shown beneath transmission lines on site plan.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement; facility is transmission. Also, applicability gate: no vehicle barrier fencing in conflict visible.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities. Retaining walls are proposed but not directly beneath overhead transmission lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show retaining walls on perimeter and around detention pond. Overhead transmission lines shown on property boundaries. Retaining walls do not appear positioned directly beneath overhead line conductors.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific clearance requirement (7.5-foot sky-to-ground from distribution conductors). Facility is transmission. Also, no apparent conflict between wall locations and conductor positions on plan view.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation shown adjacent to site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls shown on site plan but no substation facilities visible on any sheet.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: 5-foot separation requirement applies only when retaining walls are adjacent to substation property. No substation shown; requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities. No emergency access structures such as bridges or elevated platforms are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings, parking, walkways, and detention pond. No bridges or elevated emergency access structures are shown on any sheet.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific clearance requirement. Facility is transmission. Also, no emergency access structures visible on plans.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining wall plan and section details provided on Sheets 38-39 but these do not include clearance dimensions from overhead transmission conductors.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement. Facility is transmission. Transmission clearance requirements are governed by UCM § 1.14.0, not § 1.10.3.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["driveways throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section or profile views provided showing vertical clearance from finished driveway grades to lowest point of overhead electric facilities. Grading plan provides top-down view with spot elevations but no section views with conductor heights shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) reviewed; vision analysis confirmed it is a 2D top-down plan view showing contours, building FFEs, and retaining wall locations but no cross-sections or profile views showing vertical relationships between driveway grades and overhead line elevations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires verification of minimum 16-foot (parking without trucks) or 18-foot (areas with truck traffic) vertical clearance for driveways beneath overhead facilities. Without section/profile views showing driveway elevation relative to conductor heights, clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities. No vehicle parking on concrete pads is shown directly beneath overhead transmission lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking areas (10 surface, 78 garage spaces) but no concrete parking pads are positioned directly beneath overhead transmission lines.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific vertical clearance requirement (12, 16, or 18 feet depending on use). Facility is transmission. Also, no parking pad is in conflict position on plan.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["driveways and site grading near transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vertical clearance sections or profile views provided showing finished driveway/road grades relative to overhead transmission line heights. Requirement: 30-foot minimum vertical clearance from road surface to electric transmission line. No dimension annotations or cross-sections demonstrating compliance exist.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan is 2D top-down view only. No cross-section or profile views provided showing vertical clearances between any finished grades and transmission line elevations. Transmission lines are shown on site boundaries per Sheet 3 notes, and driveways traverse site, but no vertical clearance documentation is present.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 requires minimum 30-foot vertical clearance from road/driveway surfaces to transmission lines. This cannot be verified without section views or mid-span clearance survey data showing conductor elevations relative to finished grades. The absence of such documentation makes compliance verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement applies only to highway and freeway grading with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures. Site has local streets only (Valley View Road is a Level 1 local street per facts.md), not highways or freeways.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md confirms Valley View Road is 'ASMP Street Level: 1 — Local Street' and is 'Not in AMTP (not classified as highway, arterial, expressway, or freeway).'","reasoning":"Applicability gate: 40-foot clearance requirement applies only to highway/freeway grades with distribution underbuilt. Site is local street development. Requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No proposed driveways shown in conflict with or immediately adjacent to existing electric poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows driveway layout and existing utility pole locations. No driveways are positioned within 30 feet of electric poles that would require relocation.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when driveways conflict with or are immediately adjacent to existing poles. No such conflict visible on site plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["western and eastern site boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions are shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3'), but measurement origin (from outside conductor vs. from pole centerline) cannot be verified from available documentation. UCM § 1.10.3 requires measurement from outside conductor, not pole centerline.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows horizontal clearance dimensions in decimal feet (26.1' to Bldg 1/western boundary, 29.6' to Bldg 8/western boundary, 21.3' to Bldgs 5-6/eastern boundary). Vision analysis of the plan indicates dimension lines are present but does not specify whether they originate from conductor wire or from pole structure.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 Measurement Methodology section states: 'All clearances must be measured from the outside conductor, never from the utility pole centerline or pole structure.' Without dimension line annotations clearly originating from the conductor wire (not the pole), the measurement origin is ambiguous. Plans do not include detailed callouts specifying 'measured from outside conductor' or 'from pole center,' making verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new streetlight poles are shown on site. Existing streetlights not shown in conflict with overhead lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Lighting requirements (Sheet 9 Block 1) specify full cut-off, fully shielded fixtures in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 but no pole-mounted streetlight locations beneath overhead lines are shown on photometric or site plan sheets.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when new streetlight poles are proposed and overhead lines exist. No new streetlight poles are shown under overhead lines on available plans.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No power poles are shown directly within or obstructing sidewalk alignments at property limits along Valley View Road right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows existing utility pole locations. Site plan shows proposed sidewalk alignment along Valley View Road. Poles do not appear to directly conflict with proposed sidewalk at property boundaries.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies when new/modified sidewalks intersect existing poles at property limits on ROW. No such conflict apparent on plans.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No enclosed trash areas or receptacles are shown located beneath overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Trash collection notes appear on Sheet 9 but trash enclosure locations are not shown under overhead lines on site plan.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when trash enclosures/receptacles are positioned beneath overhead facilities. No such configuration shown.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Item applies to distribution facilities and customer facilities under/over distribution lines. Site has transmission facilities. Detention pond is shown in transmission easement but transmission easement restrictions are addressed in Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes (structures in easement must be approved by Austin Energy; detention pond appears to satisfy easement compatibility).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Detention pond shown in northeastern site area within transmission easement per Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3. No permanent structures, habitable buildings, or customer facilities are shown positioned beneath overhead transmission lines.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific prohibition and clearance requirement. Facility is transmission. Also, detention pond in transmission easement does not constitute customer facility installation under distribution lines per checklist definition.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution service-drop requirement; site has transmission facilities. Water meter locations are shown on utility plan but not beneath distribution service drops.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan and utility tap plan reviewed. Water meters shown in utility system but no conflicts with overhead service drops apparent.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement (service-drop conductors). Facility is transmission.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Water lines shown on utility tap plan and site plan but facility is transmission.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific clearance requirement; facility is transmission.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building foundations are set back more than 5 feet from property lines where overhead facilities exist or are planned in adjacent ROW. Buildings shown on plan with adequate setbacks.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings with property lines; buildings appear to be set back more than 5 feet from property boundaries in areas where overhead transmission facilities exist.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when foundations within 5 feet of property line. Buildings appear to have adequate setbacks; requirement appears satisfied or inapplicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["buildings and driveways with overhead transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey provided showing pole locations and vertical clearances from overhead transmission facilities to site features. When vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or insufficient based on site plan data, surveyor verification is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) provides registered surveyor boundary and topographic data but does not include mid-span clearance measurements for overhead transmission line conductors relative to site features. No elevation data or mid-span clearance survey provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires registered surveyor mid-span clearance data when vertical clearances may be marginal. The absence of section views, conductor elevation data, and clearance verification makes it impossible to assess whether clearances are adequate. A mid-span clearance survey would be required to verify the 30-foot transmission clearance (EL-1.20) and other vertical requirements.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement applies only to new overhead electric lines crossing proposed or existing roadways. Site plan shows existing overhead transmission lines, not new construction.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan indicates existing overhead transmission facilities on property boundaries, not new lines being installed.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only to new overhead line installations. Existing facilities shown; requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement applies only when both secondary and primary overhead electric lines are shown crossing. Site has transmission lines only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electric Transmission Notes throughout Sheet 3 reference transmission facilities. No secondary or primary distribution line crossings are documented.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies to secondary/primary distribution line configurations. Site has transmission infrastructure only.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows residential townhome project. No marquee signs are shown or described in project scope.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: marquee signs not proposed; requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric lines for proposed development but no new power poles are proposed.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when new poles proposed for underground service conversion. Existing facilities present; new poles not proposed.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution facility requirement; site has transmission facilities. Decorative lighting shown on site plan does not conflict with overhead lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and landscape plan show site lighting requirements (full cut-off, fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5) but specific decorative light fixture locations are not shown beneath overhead transmission lines.","reasoning":"Distribution-specific requirement. Facility is transmission. Also, no decorative lighting shown in transmission line path.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape areas adjacent to overhead transmission line on southern/eastern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Three mitigation trees are shown on landscape plan within 10-15 feet of overhead electric line (southern boundary), but specific tree species are not identified. Requirement: trees within 50 lateral feet of overhead transmission conductors must be utility-compatible species (generally mature height ≤20 feet per ECM Appendix F). Species verification cannot be completed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) vision analysis identified three mitigation trees (marked 'M' in landscape legend key notes) located approximately 10-15 feet from overhead electric (OHE) line on southern boundary. Tree list (Sheet 32) catalogues existing surveyed trees but does not map which specific UC mitigation tree species will be planted in locations shown on landscape plan.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 and ECM § 2.4.1.D/2.4.2.C require trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors to be from Utility Compatible (UC) list in ECM Appendix F, generally limited to species with mature height ≤20 feet. Although landscape plan shows tree symbols and tree list exists, the landscape plan does not specify species names for the mitigation trees shown near the overhead line. Without species identification on the landscape plan or a cross-reference to the tree list, UC compatibility cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric meter obstructions are evident on site plan. Meter location access appears clear.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads, pull boxes, and meter locations. Landscape plan shows site features. No obstructions blocking meter access (fences, walls, vegetation, building projections) are apparent.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when meter locations are obstructed. Meters appear to have adequate access clearance per available plans.","tools_used":["Read","vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings not in immediate proximity to existing streetlight poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions survey shows utility pole locations; site plan shows building locations. No apparent conflicts between new buildings and existing streetlight poles.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies when new buildings proposed adjacent to existing streetlight poles. No such adjacency shown.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution pole down guy wires not shown in conflict with accessible paths, driveways, or site features. Transmission structures do not use down guys.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows transmission facilities (per Sheet 3 notes), which use different support structures than distribution poles. Down guy wires are associated with distribution pole design, not transmission structures.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: down guy wire conflicts apply to distribution poles. Site has transmission infrastructure, which uses alternative structural support (tower structures).","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Requirement applies to angled guy anchors from transmission structures. While transmission easement exists on site, no angled guy anchors from transmission towers are shown requiring dedicated easements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transmission easement noted on site plan and Electric Transmission Notes (Sheet 3) reference transmission structures, but no angled transmission guy anchor points are explicitly shown requiring 10-foot wide easements with 50-foot extensions.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies when transmission guy anchors exist or will exist on site requiring dedicated easements. Easement exists but specific guy anchor requirements not apparent; may be covered under general transmission easement already noted.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution pole down guy anchor easement requirement; site has transmission facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transmission infrastructure present; distribution down guys not applicable.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: down guy anchor easements apply to distribution poles only. Site has transmission.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No pole-mounted or pad-mounted transformers shown directly beneath overhead lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations but none are positioned directly under overhead transmission lines.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies when transformers shown and overhead lines directly above. No such configuration shown.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered/recessed installations with structures or canopies above) are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan shows open pad-mounted transformer locations, not niche/covered configurations.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: 35-foot vertical clearance requirement applies only to niche service configurations. No niche configurations shown; requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["entire construction site with overhead transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No construction logistics plan, equipment operation zone map, or work platform plan provided showing 10-foot radial clearance from overhead transmission lines. OSHA and Texas law require 20-foot clearance during construction near energized transmission lines (per Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes item #3). Construction staging clearance verification is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"General notes on Sheet 3 reference construction requirements and safety meetings (Electric Transmission Notes item #3 requires OSHA 20-foot clearance during construction) but no separate construction logistics plan, site logistics plan, or construction phasing plan is evident in the submitted documents showing staging areas, equipment operation zones, crane swing radius, or material storage areas with clearance dimensions relative to transmission lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 requires 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines for construction working clearances per OSHA 1910.333. Sheet 3 specifically requires 20-foot clearance during construction per transmission safety standards. Without a construction logistics plan documenting staging areas and clearances, compliance cannot be verified. The absence of this plan is itself a deficiency requiring submittal.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["overhead transmission line areas on and adjacent to site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes (Block 13), item #3 explicitly requires 48-hour notice to Austin Energy before construction begins near high-voltage overhead lines. Note states: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.' This satisfies the notification requirement of UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 General Notes block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes) contains item #3: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.' This language directly addresses the 48-hour advance notification requirement.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752.003 require plans to include a note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work near high-voltage lines. The plan explicitly documents this requirement with specific contact information and scheduling instructions, satisfying the regulatory requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations are shown on building elevation sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan and building sheets reviewed; no service-mast details shown for residential electrical service.","reasoning":"Applicability gate: applies only when service-mast through-roof installations shown on elevations. No such details provided; requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":["Read"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"fe1bef10-d729-4521-85c6-bbd7d32c74fd"}
