ance dimensions\n18. EL-13.28 - No 15-foot radial clearance documentation\n19. EL-13.31 - No cross-section drawings for vertical clearances\n20. EL-13.32 - Transformer pads not shown on grading plan; type not specified\n21. EL-13.35 - Easement widths not specified\n\nN/A conditions apply to 18 items where adjacent features like retaining walls, fences, stairwells, fire escapes, hydrants, dumpsters, bike racks, light poles, and niche configurations aren't present. One item passes: EL-13.20 shows five pads properly spaced beyond the 5-foot minimum requirement.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76a266aa-db0f-4287-949a-ca92ac9e73ec","uuid":"456fbf1e-793e-485b-8c8e-84d16ac2e823"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246678894,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W5FMRNBHMWY8T6ER9T8CB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 13: Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Total Checklist Items Evaluated:** 39\n\n**Status Breakdown:**\n- **FAIL:** 5 items\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE:** 15 items  \n- **N/A:** 18 items\n- **PASS:** 1 item\n\n## Critical Deficiencies Identified\n\n### FAIL Items (Must Be Addressed):\n\n1. **EL-13.33 – Property Location:** Two transformer pads (west of Buildings 2 and 8) are located OUTSIDE the main property boundary within a \"Sidewalk Easement,\" violating the requirement that all pad-mounted equipment be 100% on private property.\n\n2. **EL-13.34 – Prohibited Easements:** Two transformer pads are located in a sidewalk easement area, and the City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 acres, NE corner, Instrument 2011021137) documented in facts.md is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan. No written Austin Energy Design approval is documented for any easement conflicts.\n\n3. **EL-13.36 – Property Routing:** Electrical routing from the two off-property transformer pads cannot comply with the 100% private property requirement, since the pads themselves are outside property boundaries.\n\n4. **EL-13.37 – Pad Dimensions & AE Design Details:** Transformer pad dimensions are not labeled on any plan sheet. No references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail specifications are provided. Service type (single-phase vs. three-phase) is not specified. These are foundational requirements for verifying pad construction compliance.\n\n5. **EL-13.38 – Bollard Protection:** All five transformer pads are located within 4 feet of driveways, parking aisles, or vehicle circulation routes, yet NO bollards or protective posts are shown on the electrical plan. 4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards are required per AE Design specifications.\n\n### Major Information Gaps (Not-Verifiable Items):\n\nCritical deficiencies in plan documentation prevent verification of 15 additional requirements:\n- **No explicit clearance dimensions** to buildings, utilities, or overhead lines\n- **Access door orientation not specified** – impossible to verify hot-stick clearance (EL-13.10)\n- **Transformer type not identified** – cannot verify oil-filled equipment requirements  \n- **Transformer pads not shown on grading plan** – cannot verify drainage direction\n- **Transformer locations not marked on landscape plan** – cannot verify vegetation clearances\n- **Easement widths not specified** – accessibility requirements undocumented\n- **No cross-sections provided** for vertical clearance verification\n- **Cross-utility conflicts not analyzed** – multiple utilities shown with no separation dimensions\n\n## Documents Reviewed\n\n- Sheet 21 – Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n- Sheet 9 – Site Plan\n- Sheet 11 – Grading Plan\n- Sheets 31, 32, 35 – Landscape Plans\n- Sheets 22-25 – Construction Details\n- Facts.md – Site survey data\n- README.md – Project metadata\n\nThe applicant must address the five fail items and provide comprehensive documentation for the not-verifiable items before the transformer pad installation can proceed."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76a266aa-db0f-4287-949a-ca92ac9e73ec","uuid":"d25e082e-30c7-4c57-8dc2-7dc511c5aac8"}
{"level":30,"time":1778246678929,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":474933,"duration_api_ms":222137,"num_turns":29,"result":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 13: Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Total Checklist Items Evaluated:** 39\n\n**Status Breakdown:**\n- **FAIL:** 5 items\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE:** 15 items  \n- **N/A:** 18 items\n- **PASS:** 1 item\n\n## Critical Deficiencies Identified\n\n### FAIL Items (Must Be Addressed):\n\n1. **EL-13.33 – Property Location:** Two transformer pads (west of Buildings 2 and 8) are located OUTSIDE the main property boundary within a \"Sidewalk Easement,\" violating the requirement that all pad-mounted equipment be 100% on private property.\n\n2. **EL-13.34 – Prohibited Easements:** Two transformer pads are located in a sidewalk easement area, and the City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 acres, NE corner, Instrument 2011021137) documented in facts.md is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan. No written Austin Energy Design approval is documented for any easement conflicts.\n\n3. **EL-13.36 – Property Routing:** Electrical routing from the two off-property transformer pads cannot comply with the 100% private property requirement, since the pads themselves are outside property boundaries.\n\n4. **EL-13.37 – Pad Dimensions & AE Design Details:** Transformer pad dimensions are not labeled on any plan sheet. No references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail specifications are provided. Service type (single-phase vs. three-phase) is not specified. These are foundational requirements for verifying pad construction compliance.\n\n5. **EL-13.38 – Bollard Protection:** All five transformer pads are located within 4 feet of driveways, parking aisles, or vehicle circulation routes, yet NO bollards or protective posts are shown on the electrical plan. 4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards are required per AE Design specifications.\n\n### Major Information Gaps (Not-Verifiable Items):\n\nCritical deficiencies in plan documentation prevent verification of 15 additional requirements:\n- **No explicit clearance dimensions** to buildings, utilities, or overhead lines\n- **Access door orientation not specified** – impossible to verify hot-stick clearance (EL-13.10)\n- **Transformer type not identified** – cannot verify oil-filled equipment requirements  \n- **Transformer pads not shown on grading plan** – cannot verify drainage direction\n- **Transformer locations not marked on landscape plan** – cannot verify vegetation clearances\n- **Easement widths not specified** – accessibility requirements undocumented\n- **No cross-sections provided** for vertical clearance verification\n- **Cross-utility conflicts not analyzed** – multiple utilities shown with no separation dimensions\n\n## Documents Reviewed\n\n- Sheet 21 – Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n- Sheet 9 – Site Plan\n- Sheet 11 – Grading Plan\n- Sheets 31, 32, 35 – Landscape Plans\n- Sheets 22-25 – Construction Details\n- Facts.md – Site survey data\n- README.md – Project metadata\n\nThe applicant must address the five fail items and provide comprehensive documentation for the not-verifiable items before the transformer pad installation can proceed.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"76a266aa-db0f-4287-949a-ca92ac9e73ec","total_cost_usd":0.40733465,"usage":{"input_tokens":212,"cache_creation_input_tokens":132471,"cache_read_input_tokens":1180339,"output_tokens":24700,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":132471},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":212,"outputTokens":24700,"cacheReadInputTokens":1180339,"cacheCreationInputTokens":132471,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.40733465,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis estimates clearances of 5-10 feet and 10-15 feet from buildings; however, no explicit dimension callouts are provided on the electrical plan to verify that minimum 5-foot clearances are maintained.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified five transformer pads with visual distance estimates to buildings ranging from 5-15 feet, but no explicit dimension lines or numerical clearance callouts are shown on the plan.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimensions on the plan, visual estimates are insufficient to definitively verify compliance with the 5-foot clearance requirement. Dimensions must be labeled on construction documents.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) does not depict retaining walls in proximity to the five identified transformer pads.","reasoning":"The applicability condition is the presence of retaining walls adjacent to transformers. No retaining walls are shown adjacent to any transformer pads on the electrical plan, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences or gates are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not depict fence or gate locations in relation to the five transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when fences or gates are adjacent to transformer pads. Since no fences are shown adjacent to any of the five pads on the electrical plan, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearances less than 5 feet to buildings are shown on the electrical plan; all estimated clearances are 5-15 feet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis indicates all five transformer pads maintain clearances estimated between 5-15 feet from adjacent buildings, not less than 5 feet.","reasoning":"The requirement for reduced clearance documentation (3 feet) is only applicable when plans actually show clearances less than 5 feet. Since no such reduced clearances are proposed, the requirement for written approval does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Building elevation zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are shown on the electrical plan, but building elevation sheets do not contain callouts or dimensions showing balcony or overhang locations relative to the transformer pads, preventing verification of 5-foot lateral clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows transformer pad locations but does not reference or coordinate with building elevations to identify balcony or overhang positions.","reasoning":"To verify 5-foot clearance from balconies/overhangs, building elevation sheets would need to show these features with dimensions relative to transformer pad locations. This coordination is not evident on the electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Building window/door zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan; building elevations are not coordinated with transformer locations to verify 12-foot clearances from windows, doors, or ventilating ducts.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not specify transformer type (oil-filled or dry-type) and does not show window/door locations relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment and requires both transformer type specification and building elevation coordination showing window/door positions. Neither is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk easements are labeled on the electrical plan, but specific sidewalk locations and distances from transformer pads are not dimensioned on the plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis identified a 'Sidewalk Easement' on the plan near transformer locations, but no specific dimension callouts show the distance from transformer pads to sidewalk back-of-line.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimensions showing sidewalk locations relative to transformer pads, the 2-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from the available plan documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not depict stairwell locations in relation to the five transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when stairwells adjacent to transformers are present. No such stairwells are shown on the electrical plan, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Fire escape zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified; fire escape locations are not shown on the electrical plan relative to transformer pads, preventing verification of 20-foot clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not identify transformer type or show fire escape locations relative to the transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment and requires coordination with building elevation/fire escape design. Neither transformer type specification nor fire escape locations are provided on the electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door orientation and location are not identified on the electrical plan. Without knowing which side of each pad is the access door side, the 10-foot hot-stick clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 shows five transformer pads but does not identify which face of each pad is the access door orientation.","reasoning":"Hot-stick access clearances are measured from the access door side of the pad. Since access door orientation is not specified on the plan, it is impossible to verify compliance with the 10-foot clearance requirement for this critical safety zone.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer locations face confined spaces (niches, vaults, or notched-out building areas). All five transformer pads are located in open areas outside building footprints.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis shows all five transformer pads are located outside building footprints, not within notched-out areas, niches, or fully enclosed spaces.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when transformers face confined spaces. Since all pads are in open locations on the site, the 15-foot confined-space clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrant locations are not shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not depict fire hydrant locations in relation to the five transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when fire hydrants are adjacent to transformers. No fire hydrants are shown adjacent to any transformer pads on the electrical plan, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Tree/vegetation zones within 10-15 lateral feet of transformer pads and overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree and vegetation symbols but does not explicitly identify which trees are within 10 lateral feet of specific transformer pad locations or 15 lateral feet of overhead conductors. Plant list (Sheets 32, 35) identifies species but does not correlate species with proximity zones or provide utility-compatible classifications per ECM Appendix F.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows tree symbols and the plant schedule lists Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel, Dwarf Palmetto, shrubs, and groundcovers, but transformer pad locations are not marked on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations clearly marked on the landscape plan and cross-referenced with tree locations, specific tree-to-pad distances cannot be verified. The plant list does not include utility-compatible status designations from ECM Appendix F.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Shrub/vegetation zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows shrub and groundcover planting symbols and plant schedule specifies shrub types (Dwarf Palmetto, Big Muhly, Gulf Muhly, Texas Sage, Dwarf Wax Myrtle) but does not correlate specific shrub locations to transformer pad access door orientations or verify 10-foot and 5-foot lateral clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan and Sheet 35 plant schedules document shrub species and quantities but do not explicitly reference transformer pad locations or access door orientations.","reasoning":"Without transformer pads marked on the landscape plan and access door orientations specified, the lateral clearance requirements from shrub locations cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Tree zones within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows tree locations and plant schedule identifies tree species, but transformer pad locations are not marked on the landscape plan, and no root barrier details are shown in the construction detail sheets for trees in proximity to transformer pads.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant list (Sheets 32, 35) shows tree species and quantities, but transformer pad locations are not correlated on the landscape plan. No root barrier specifications are provided.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations clearly marked on the landscape plan, trees within 20 feet cannot be identified, and without root barrier detail specifications provided, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpster locations are shown on the electrical plan adjacent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not depict dumpster or trash collection enclosure locations in relation to the five transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when dumpsters are adjacent to transformers. No dumpsters are shown adjacent to any transformer pads on the electrical plan, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bike racks are located at the site (41 total spaces per site plan, Sheet 9) but their specific locations are not correlated with transformer pad locations on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows bicycle parking exists (39 long-term, 2 short-term), but the electrical plan (Sheet 21) does not show bike rack locations relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Without bike rack locations specifically marked on the electrical plan relative to transformer pads, adjacency and clearances cannot be evaluated. The absence of bike racks shown on the electrical plan suggests they are not within the 5-foot clearance zone of any transformer pad.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations are not shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not show specific light pole locations in relation to the five transformer pads.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when light poles are adjacent to transformers. No light poles are shown adjacent to any transformer pads on the electrical plan, so the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fire lane zones near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) may designate fire lanes, but the electrical plan (Sheet 21) does not show fire lane locations relative to transformer pads with dimension callouts demonstrating 15-foot clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan is noted in the site plan index (Sheet 10) but the electrical plan does not coordinate transformer pad locations with fire lane designations.","reasoning":"Without explicit coordinate reference between fire lane locations and transformer pads on the electrical plan, the 15-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from the electrical drawing alone.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan with visual spacing estimated at 15-30+ feet between pads, exceeding the 5-foot minimum separation requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis identified five transformer pads distributed across the site at the northwest, west-central, southwest, east-central, and southeast locations. Visual spacing between adjacent pads appears to range from 15-30+ feet based on the 1:20 scale.","reasoning":"All five pads are spatially separated by distances well in excess of the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement. Although not dimensioned, visual scale analysis confirms adequate separation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water utility zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water supply lines are labeled on the electrical plan with 'W' callouts near transformer pads, but no dimension callouts specify the clearance distance from transformer pads to water lines. Clearance compliance cannot be verified without explicit dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that water lines labeled 'W' are routed near several transformer pads, particularly along the western side of the site, but no numeric clearance dimensions are shown.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts showing clearance distances between transformer pads and water supply lines, compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified from the plan documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Wastewater utility zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines are labeled on the electrical plan with 'WW' callouts near transformer pads, but no dimension callouts specify the clearance distance from transformer pads to wastewater lines. Clearance compliance cannot be verified without explicit dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that wastewater lines labeled 'WW' are shown on the electrical plan near transformer pad locations, but no numeric clearance dimensions are provided.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts showing clearance distances between transformer pads and wastewater lines, compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified from the plan documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Storm drain utility zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain infrastructure is shown on the Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12) and general utilities are referenced on the electrical plan (Sheet 21), but no explicit dimension callouts show clearance distances from transformer pads to storm drain lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set includes a dedicated Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12) and the electrical plan references general utilities, but specific clearance dimensions between transformer pads and storm drain lines are not provided on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts on the electrical plan showing clearance distances to storm drain infrastructure, compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified from the electrical drawing.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Gas utility zones adjacent to transformer pads (if applicable)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Gas infrastructure is not clearly shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) relative to transformer pad locations. The plan does not specify whether gas service is present on the site or what clearance distances are maintained.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 did not identify gas lines labeled or shown in relation to the five transformer pads. The electrical plan notes reference water and wastewater branches but do not mention gas infrastructure.","reasoning":"Without clear depiction of gas infrastructure on the electrical plan and without dimension callouts if gas service is present, compliance with the 24-36 inch minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Underground utility zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric, telecommunications) are identified on the electrical plan, but no explicit horizontal or vertical clearance dimensions are provided showing 12-inch minimum separations between transformer pads and these utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multiple utility lines (W, WW, SD, electric conduits) are depicted on Sheet 21 near transformer pads, but no numeric clearance dimensions are shown.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts showing 12-inch horizontal and vertical separations from transformer pads to other underground utilities, compliance cannot be verified from the plan documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads and underground facilities relative to other utilities and structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical plan shows multiple utility lines and transformer pads, but does not explicitly analyze or document whether transformer pads or AE underground facilities are located directly over or under other utility lines, or whether customer buildings/parking are located over AE facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows multiple utility infrastructure elements and transformer pad locations, but does not provide cross-utility analysis or notations indicating vertical stacking conflicts.","reasoning":"Without explicit analysis documenting that no conflicts exist between transformer pads/AE facilities and other underground utilities or structures, compliance with the non-overlapping requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric distribution lines (OHE) are shown on the electrical plan near several transformer pad locations (particularly on western and southern property edges), but no explicit dimension callouts show the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance distances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis identified overhead electric lines (-OHE-) labeled on Sheet 21 running along western and southern property perimeters near transformer pads, but no numeric clearance dimensions are provided.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts demonstrating 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead conductors, compliance cannot be verified from the plan documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead distribution conductor zones adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on the plan but are not analyzed with 15-foot radius clearance circles or dimension callouts. No explicit documentation confirms that transformer locations and proposed facilities maintain the 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines (-OHE-) are shown on Sheet 21, but no 15-foot radius clearance zones or dimension callouts are provided relative to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Without explicit radial clearance documentation or dimension callouts showing compliance with the 15-foot radius requirement from conductors, compliance cannot be verified from the plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer is proposed to be located in a niche, enclosed area, or notched-out building configuration. All five transformer pads are shown located outside building footprints in open areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows all five transformer pads located outside building perimeters in open site areas.","reasoning":"The niche service requirement is only applicable when transformers are specifically designed to be located within building footprints with AE equipment accessible from outside. No such niche configuration is proposed, so this requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Niche service is not proposed. All transformer pads are located outside building footprints.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No niche or enclosed transformer installation is shown on any plan sheet.","reasoning":"Since niche service is not part of this project scope, requirements for 3-hour fire walls, ventilation specifications, and AE Design consultation do not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Vertical clearance zones with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided on any plan sheet showing vertical clearances from ground to overhead structures (building overhangs, canopies, garage structures) at transformer pad locations. While overhead structures may exist (buildings, parking structures), vertical clearance documentation is absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan set review shows building cross-sections and elevations exist (referenced in index) but specific cross-sections documenting vertical clearances at transformer pad locations are not provided.","reasoning":"Cross-section drawings are required when overhead structures exist above or near transformer locations to verify adequate vertical clearance (minimum 35 feet in niches, plus overhead distribution clearances). Their absence prevents verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Grading/drainage zones around transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The Grading Plan (Sheet 11) does not depict transformer pad locations, making it impossible to verify whether surface drainage slopes are directed away from buildings as required for oil-filled equipment. Additionally, the electrical plan does not specify whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows building locations and general site drainage, but transformer pads are not identified or labeled on the grading drawing. Sheet 21 does not specify transformer type.","reasoning":"Without transformer pads shown on the grading plan and without transformer type specification (oil-filled vs. dry-type), compliance with drainage direction requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Two transformer pads located on western property edge (west of Buildings 2 and 8)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis indicates that two of the five transformer pads (located west of Buildings 2 and 8) are positioned OUTSIDE the main property boundary, within a 'Sidewalk Easement' area between the private property line and the public right-of-way. All pad-mounted transformer equipment must be located 100% on private property, not in public right-of-way or easements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found that two transformer pad locations are drawn to the west (outside) of the heavy dashed-dotted property boundary line and are positioned within a labeled 'Sidewalk Easement' area.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.4 footnote 4 explicitly requires all padmount equipment to be installed on customer's property, not in public right-of-way. A sidewalk easement located between the property line and the ROW constitutes a public utility area, not private property. Transformer pads cannot be placed in such easements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Two transformer pads within sidewalk easement (west of Buildings 2 and 8); all five transformer pads relative to drainage easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two transformer pads appear to be located within a 'Sidewalk Easement' area. Additionally, the facts.md document identifies a perpetual City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 acres, NE corner, Instrument 2011021137) that is not depicted on the submitted site plan. Transformer pads cannot be placed in drainage easements, sewer easements, water easements, or electrical easements under overhead lines without explicit Austin Energy Design written approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found two transformer pads positioned in a 'Sidewalk Easement' on the electrical plan. Facts.md documents a City of Austin drainage easement covering the NE corner (0.130 acres) that is NOT shown on the submitted plans.","reasoning":"Two pads are located in prohibited easement areas (sidewalk easement). Additionally, the City drainage easement in the NE corner is not depicted on the electrical plan, and none of the five transformer pad locations are verified to be clear of this or other prohibitive easements. No written AE Design approval is documented.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dashed rectangular boundaries are shown around the five transformer pad locations, with one labeled 'Vault Easement' (near Bldg 8). However, no easement widths or dimensions are specified for any of the five locations. Austin Energy Design accessibility requirements determine the required easement width, but this width is not documented on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis identified dashed boundary lines around the five transformer pads, with one explicitly labeled 'Vault Easement,' but no numeric width dimensions are provided for any easement boundary.","reasoning":"While easement boundaries are graphically depicted, the width specifications required by Austin Energy Design for accessibility are not labeled on the plan. Compliance with AE Design accessibility requirements cannot be verified without explicit width dimensions.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters, particularly for the two pads located in sidewalk easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing lines are shown from transformer pads to meters on Sheet 21, but the routing paths are not explicitly verified to remain 100% on private property. Given that two transformer pads are located in the 'Sidewalk Easement' (outside private property), the electrical conduit routing from those pads would also be outside private property, violating the requirement that electrical routing be 100% on private property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that two transformer pads are located outside the private property boundary within a sidewalk easement. Electrical routing lines visible on the plan would necessarily extend from these off-property pads.","reasoning":"If transformer pads are not on private property (as documented in EL-13.33), then electrical routing from those pads cannot be 100% on private property. The requirement mandates all routing from transformer to meter remain on customer property.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not labeled on any plan sheet (estimated 8'x8' to 10'x10' by visual scale only). No references to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail specifications are provided. The electrical specifications do not identify the service type (single-phase vs. three-phase). Without this documentation, transformer pad construction dimensions cannot be verified to match AE Design-approved specifications for the specified service type.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found no explicit dimensions labeling any transformer pad. The electrical plan contains no references to AE Design-approved details, standards, or part numbers. No service type specification is provided.","reasoning":"Pad-mounted transformers must be installed on AE Design-approved concrete pads with dimensions determined by AE Design based on service type and load requirements. Without pad dimensions labeled and without AE Design detail references, compliance with approved specifications cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis confirms that all five transformer pads are located immediately adjacent to or within 4 feet of driveways, parking aisles, or vehicle circulation routes. However, NO bollards or protective posts are shown on the electrical plan. The plan lacks any callouts, notations, or specifications for 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards required by AE Design equipment pad details when pads are within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified all five transformer pads positioned within 4 feet of vehicle routes/driveways. No bollard symbols, dimension callouts, or specifications are shown on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"When equipment pads are installed within 4 feet of parking or traffic areas, 4-inch diameter galvanized bollards are required per AE Design specifications to prevent vehicle contact. The complete absence of bollard details on the plan indicates non-compliance with this safety requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are shown to be located directly under or over the overhead electric distribution facilities depicted on the electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows overhead electric lines (-OHE-) running along the western and southern property perimeters. Building footprints and parking structures do not appear to be positioned directly beneath these lines.","reasoning":"This requirement is only applicable when customer facilities are proposed to be located under or over AE overhead distribution facilities. Since no such configuration is shown, the requirement does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7da7cc9a-d1f7-4f81-9fde-b91b9acc03c6"}
