12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to underground utilities (conduits, communication cables, etc.).\"}\n  ]\n\nDetail 5 (13:EL-13.26):\n- Text: \"No utility coordination drawing, conflict analysis, or cross-section details verify that transformer pads are not located over/under other utility lines or that customer structures are not installed over AE underground facilities.\"\n- Citation: \"UCM § 1.10.5.B\"\n- SourceId: \"13:EL-13.26\"\n- Confidence: 2\n- RunComments: [\n    {runNum: 2, status: \"nv\", comment: \"The electrical plan shows multiple utility lines and transformer pads, but does not explicitly analyze or document whether transformer pads or AE underground facilities are located directly over or under other utility lines, or whether customer buildings/parking are located over AE facilities.\"},\n    {runNum: 3, status: \"nv\", comment: \"No utility coordination drawing, conflict analysis, or cross-section details verify that transformer pads are not located over/under other utility lines or that customer structures are not installed over AE underground facilities.\"}\n  ]\n\n---\n\n### Comment 6: Overhead Distribution Line Clearances\n\nHeadline: \"Missing clearance verification to overhead distribution lines\"\nSummary: \"Overhead distribution lines are shown on site plans but required clearances to transformer pad locations and customer facilities are not documented with dimension callouts or cross-sections.\"\nSheets: [21, 31]\nApplicableArea: \"Utilities & Infrastructure\"\nSeverity: 2\nConfidence: 3\nCrossDep: \"Overhead utility provider coordination needed to verify clearance compliance.\"\nAttn: \"Provide cross-sections showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance; verify 15-foot radial clearance from conductor centerlines; confirm customer structures do not exceed overhead line clearance envelopes\"\n\nDetails:\n\nDetail 1 (13:EL-13.27):\n- Text: \"Overhead distribution lines shown along property perimeter but minimum 7.5