{"level":30,"time":1778246926132,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3W60KQ17VB1KA6QWBBJ6E8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GaMDPvuP3XXubpgFhGVPhT","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"comments":[{"headline":"Missing building elevation sheets with overhead conductor clearances","summary":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are included in the site plan package. Vertical clearances from building edges and projections to overhead electric lines cannot be verified.","sheets":[1,4,9,11,21],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Building elevation sheets with registered surveyor conductor elevation data and clearance annotations entirely absent from plan set. Site plan shows only 2D top-down views.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are included in the plan set. Required documentation is missing."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations with clearance dimension annotations. Site plan is 2D top-down view only; no vertical elevation views are available."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan package. Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are not documented on any elevation sheets because such sheets do not exist. Registered surveyor data for conductor elevation is absent."}]},{"text":"Buildings 1-2 located 25.8-26.1 feet from western property boundary where overhead lines exist, but no surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.1","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings are shown on site plan with overhead electric lines depicted on property boundaries, but no clearance dimensions or surveyed conductor elevation data are provided. Horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified from submitted documents."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings 1 and 2 are located approximately 25.8 to 26.1 feet from the western property boundary where overhead electric lines are shown. However, surveyed elevations of the overhead conductors are not provided, and no building elevation sheets with clearance dimensions are included. Vertical clearances cannot be verified without conductor elevation data."}]},{"text":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies) lack evaluation for clearances from overhead conductors. No elevation documentation or surveyor conductor elevation data provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets or section views are provided showing vertical clearances from building projections to overhead electric conductors. Clearance compliance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets are provided in the site plan set. Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies) cannot be evaluated for clearances from overhead conductors without elevation documentation and conductor survey data."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing section views showing vertical overhead conductor clearances","summary":"Section and profile views with vertical clearance dimension annotations from outside conductors to buildings, driveways, roads, and retaining walls are not provided. Vertical clearance compliance cannot be documented.","sheets":[9,11,38,39],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead lines but no section views or enlarged details with dimension lines from outside conductor to building edges provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead electric lines but no section views or enlarged details with clearance dimensions from outside conductor to building edges are provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No section or profile view exhibits provided showing dimension lines from outer conductor to building edges. Horizontal clearance dimensions shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3') but no vertical sections or enlarged details demonstrating clearances from conductor to building projections."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan exhibits showing dimension lines from the outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings and projections are not provided. No cross-sections depict clearance verification from conductors to site features."}]},{"text":"Driveways and parking areas shown without section views or vertical clearance dimensions from finished driveway grades to overhead lines. Surveyed mid-span clearance data absent.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveways and parking areas are shown but no section views or vertical clearance dimensions are documented. Surveyed mid-span clearance data is not provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section or profile views provided showing vertical clearance from finished driveway grades to lowest point of overhead electric facilities. Grading plan provides top-down view with spot elevations but no section views with conductor heights shown."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveways are proposed throughout the site. Finished driveway grade elevations are shown on grading plan, but no surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided, and no vertical clearance dimensions are documented. Mid-span clearance verification is absent."}]},{"text":"No vertical clearance sections or profile views provided showing finished driveway/road grades relative to overhead transmission line heights. 30-foot minimum vertical clearance requirement not demonstrated.","citation":"UCM § 1.14.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.20","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transmission facilities are noted on Sheet 3 but grading plan does not identify transmission line crossing locations or document 30-foot vertical clearance dimensions."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No vertical clearance sections or profile views provided showing finished driveway/road grades relative to overhead transmission line heights. Requirement: 30-foot minimum vertical clearance from road surface to electric transmission line. No dimension annotations or cross-sections demonstrating compliance exist."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes) indicates transmission facilities affect the site. Driveway grades are shown on grading plan, but no surveyed transmission conductor elevations are provided, and no vertical clearance dimensions document the 30-foot minimum clearance requirement."}]},{"text":"Retaining walls (up to 14 feet) lack section views with clearance dimension annotations from outside conductors to wall faces. Required section exhibits missing.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.17","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining wall sections are provided but do not include clearance dimension annotations from outside conductor to wall face. Required section exhibits with clearance dimensions are missing."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining wall sections are shown on Sheets 38-39 with structural details, rebar specifications, and footing dimensions. However, these sections do NOT show overhead electric conductor locations or clearance dimension annotations from outer conductors to outermost edge of walls."}]},{"text":"Retaining walls proposed along southern, eastern, and northeast boundaries near overhead lines, but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor to wall faces documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are proposed but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor to wall face are documented on site plan or section views."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Multiple retaining walls are proposed along southern, eastern, and northeast boundaries where overhead electric lines exist. Vision analysis shows walls run parallel to OHE line on southern boundary, but no specific clearance dimensions from outside electric line to wall faces are provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Clearance dimension annotations from overhead conductors missing or incorrect","summary":"Clearance dimensions are missing or measured from incorrect reference points (pole centerline vs. outside conductor). Dimension annotations from outside conductors to buildings and customer facilities required by code are absent or not verifiable.","sheets":[9,21,38],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Verify measurement origin for any existing dimension annotations; confirm whether dimensions shown originate from outside conductor per UCM § 1.10.3.","details":[{"text":"Clearance dimensions shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3'), but measurement origin (outside conductor vs. pole centerline) cannot be verified. UCM § 1.10.3 requires measurement from outside conductor, not pole centerline.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Clearance dimensions, if any, are measured from property lines or pole centerline rather than from the outside conductor as required by code. Dimension annotations must originate from the actual conductor position."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Clearance dimensions are shown on site plan (26.1', 29.6', 21.3'), but measurement origin (from outside conductor vs. from pole centerline) cannot be verified from available documentation. UCM § 1.10.3 requires measurement from outside conductor, not pole centerline."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets from overhead electric conductors to site features. Where clearance dimensions should exist (showing measurement from outside conductor, not pole center), they are absent entirely. Critical measurement annotations are missing."}]},{"text":"Overhead distribution conductors shown on site plan, but no dimensions show radial distances from outside conductors to customer facilities (transformers, pull boxes, meters). Voltage classification not documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown on site plan but conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) and voltage classification are not labeled. No 15-foot radial clearance dimensions are documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution conductors are shown on site plan, but no dimensions are provided showing radial distances from outside conductors to customer facilities (transformers, pull boxes, electrical meters). Voltage classification of overhead lines is not documented, preventing verification of 15-foot radial clearance requirement."}]},{"text":"Buildings located adjacent to property boundaries where overhead electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW. Clearance dimensions from outside conductor not documented on site plan.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings are adjacent to property boundaries where overhead electric facilities exist. Clearance dimensions from outside conductor are not documented on site plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings are located adjacent to Valley View Road where overhead electric facilities exist or may be relocated. Relationship between building setback and electric facility location in ROW is not documented. Surveyed location of facilities in adjacent ROW is not provided."}]},{"text":"Overhead electric facilities exist on multiple site boundaries. Proposed driveways, parking, and retaining walls in proximity to overhead lines lack registered surveyor data for pole locations, mid-span clearances, and conductor elevations.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveway grades may have marginal vertical clearance from overhead lines, but registered surveyor mid-span clearance verification is not provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey provided showing pole locations and vertical clearances from overhead transmission facilities to site features. When vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or insufficient based on site plan data, surveyor verification is required."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric facilities exist on multiple boundaries of the site. Proposed driveways, parking areas, and retaining walls are located in proximity to overhead lines. No registered surveyor data is provided showing pole locations, mid-span clearances, or conductor elevations. Survey of electrical infrastructure clearances is entirely absent."}]}]},{"headline":"Tree species utility compatibility not verified for overhead lines","summary":"Landscape plan shows proposed tree plantings near overhead electric transmission lines, but tree species are not identified or cross-referenced against utility-compatible (UC) species requirements. Compliance cannot be verified.","sheets":[31,32,35],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"Verify tree species against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible (UC) list; confirm mature height ≤20 feet for trees within 50 lateral feet of overhead transmission conductors.","details":[{"text":"Proposed trees throughout site, including areas in proximity to overhead electric lines on western, northern, and southern boundaries, not identified by species or cross-referenced against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible (UC) list. Lateral distance annotations absent.","citation":"ECM § 2.4.1.D; ECM § 2.4.2.C; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows plantings but does not identify proposed tree species or verify lateral clearance distances from overhead electric lines. Utility-compatibility verification is not provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Three mitigation trees are shown on landscape plan within 10-15 feet of overhead electric line (southern boundary), but specific tree species are not identified. Requirement: trees within 50 lateral feet of overhead transmission conductors must be utility-compatible species (generally mature height ≤20 feet per ECM Appendix F). Species verification cannot be completed."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows proposed tree plantings throughout site, including areas in proximity to overhead electric lines on western, northern, and southern boundaries. However, tree species are not cross-referenced against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible (UC) list, and no lateral distance annotations show distance from proposed trees to overhead conductors. Compliance with tree species restrictions cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Construction staging plan with equipment clearances not documented","summary":"No construction staging plan, equipment operation zone diagram, or work platform plan documents 10-foot radial clearance from overhead transmission lines during construction. Construction clearance verification absent.","sheets":[3,5],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Construction Management - verify staging areas and crane operations maintain code clearances from energized transmission lines","attn":"Confirm OSHA and Texas law requirements: 20-foot clearance during construction near energized transmission lines per Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes.","details":[{"text":"Construction logistics plan, equipment operation zone map, and work platform plan showing 10-foot radial clearance from overhead transmission lines not provided. Staging areas, crane swing radius, and material storage locations lack documented clearance verification.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.45","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but no construction staging plan or equipment operation zone diagram documents 10-foot radial clearance during construction."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No construction logistics plan, equipment operation zone map, or work platform plan provided showing 10-foot radial clearance from overhead transmission lines. OSHA and Texas law require 20-foot clearance during construction near energized transmission lines (per Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes item #3). Construction staging clearance verification is not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sequence of construction is outlined on Sheet 3. Erosion control plan (Sheet 5) shows temporary controls, but a detailed construction staging area plan showing equipment placement, crane swing radius, and material storage locations is not provided. Verification that staging areas maintain 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines cannot be determined."}]}]},{"headline":"Fencing, pond enclosure, and sidewalk clearances not documented","summary":"Perimeter fencing, pond fence, and sidewalks lack clearance dimension annotations from outside overhead conductors. Fencing material specifications and grounding details for areas near transmission lines absent.","sheets":[4,9,31,38],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"For fencing beneath transmission lines: verify material (conductive vs. non-conductive) and grounding specifications on construction details.","details":[{"text":"Perimeter fencing shown on property boundaries near overhead lines, but no dimension annotations show clearance distance from outside conductor. Clearance verification not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.9","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fencing is shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor are documented. Clearance compliance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences are shown on site plan (pond perimeter fence, wood fence on eastern boundary, eastern boundary wood fence), but no dimension annotations show clearance distance from outside conductor of overhead electric lines. Clearance verification is not provided."}]},{"text":"Utility poles and fence post locations shown on site plan and survey, but no horizontal dimensions provided between fence post locations and pole centerlines.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fence and pole locations are shown but horizontal clearance dimensions between fence posts and electric poles are not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility poles are shown on existing survey and site plan. Fence post locations are shown, but no horizontal dimensions are provided between fence post locations and pole centerlines."}]},{"text":"Fencing proposed on site near transmission facilities. Fence material specifications (conductive vs. non-conductive) and grounding details not provided on construction detail sheets.","citation":"UCM § 1.14.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.12","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fencing is shown but no documentation addresses whether it is beneath transmission lines or specifies material (conductive vs. non-conductive) and grounding details."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fencing is proposed on site. Transmission facilities appear to affect the site per Block 13 notes. Fence material specifications and grounding details are not provided on construction detail sheets to verify non-conductive material or proper grounding for fences near transmission lines."}]},{"text":"Pond perimeter fence exists in area with adjacent overhead electric line. No section exhibit shows vertical and horizontal clearance dimensions from outermost electric line to fence.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.13","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Pond perimeter fence exists in area with adjacent overhead electric line. No section exhibit shows vertical and horizontal clearance dimensions from outermost electric line to the fence. Clearance verification is absent."}]},{"text":"Sidewalks proposed along western property boundary (Valley View Road) where existing power poles shown near property corners. Relationship between sidewalk alignment and pole locations not dimensioned or verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalks are shown at property frontage where utility poles exist, but conflict resolution or clearance dimensions are not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalks are shown along the western property boundary (Valley View Road). Existing power poles are shown on the survey near property corners. Relationship between sidewalk alignment and pole locations at property ends is not dimensioned or verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility easements, property lines, and infrastructure conflicts not documented","summary":"Buildings are not verified as located outside transmission easements. Down guy wire locations, anchor easement boundaries, property line clearances, and line crossing angles not documented or analyzed for conflicts.","sheets":[2,3,4,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Public Works / Right-of-Way Management - coordinate on easement boundaries and transmission facility locations in adjacent ROW","attn":"Verify down guy wire locations on existing and adjacent properties; confirm building locations outside transmission easement boundaries; document line crossing orientation angles.","details":[{"text":"Buildings proposed without documented verification that they are located outside transmission easement boundaries. Transmission easement restrictions noted on Sheet 3 but building compliance not addressed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Buildings are proposed on site without documented verification that they are outside transmission easement boundaries. Transmission easement restrictions are noted on Sheet 3 but building compliance is not addressed."}]},{"text":"Building locations and property lines shown on site plan, but no documentation identifies foundations within 5 feet of property line or addresses clearance space for adjacent electric facilities.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.30","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Building locations and property lines are shown but no documentation identifies foundations within 5 feet of property line or addresses clearance space for adjacent electric facilities."}]},{"text":"Overhead line crossings of Valley View Road not documented with angle annotations to verify 90-degree crossing orientation per standard practice.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.32","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead line crossings of Valley View Road are not documented with angle annotations to verify 90-degree crossing orientation."}]},{"text":"Utility poles shown on existing survey and site plan. Down guy wire locations not explicitly depicted on any plan sheet, though such infrastructure frequently exists at utility poles. Potential conflicts with proposed accessible paths and driveways cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.17.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.40","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility poles are shown on existing conditions survey but down guy wire locations are not clearly identified. Conflict resolution with proposed driveways is not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles on and adjacent to property. Down guy wires from these poles are not explicitly depicted on any plan sheet, though such infrastructure frequently exists at utility pole locations. Potential conflicts with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features cannot be verified without complete down guy wire documentation."}]},{"text":"Transmission facilities affect site per Block 13 notes. Plat sheet shows easement boundaries but does not explicitly identify down guy anchor easements. Required 10-foot-wide easements extending 5 feet past ground entry points not documented if down guy anchors exist.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.42","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility poles are shown but down guy anchor locations and dedicated easement boundaries (10' wide × 5' extension) are not explicitly documented on easement exhibit."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plat sheet (Sheet 2) shows easement boundaries but does not explicitly identify down guy anchor easements. If down guy anchors from poles near the property exist, dedicated 10-foot-wide easements extending 5 feet past ground entry points are required but not documented."}]},{"text":"Transmission facilities affect site. Guy easement boundaries (10' wide ± 50' extension) not explicitly shown on easement exhibit or site plan.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.41","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transmission facilities are noted but guy easement boundaries (10' wide ± 50' extension) are not explicitly shown on easement exhibit or site plan."}]}]},{"headline":"Site utilities, equipment, and features lack overhead line clearance documentation","summary":"Pedestrian walkways, parking areas, trash enclosures, water utilities, site lighting, and electrical equipment locations shown on plans but lack clearance dimension annotations from overhead lines. Conductor types and working clearances for meter pads not documented.","sheets":[9,10,19,20,21,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"For electric meter pads: verify 30-inch front working space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9; confirm no obstructions from buildings, fences, walls, or landscaping.","details":[{"text":"Elevated walkways and accessible ramps shown on site plans without section views demonstrating 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductors. Conductor elevations not surveyed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Pedestrian walkways are shown on site plan, but insufficient documentation regarding whether they are elevated structures or at-grade. Section views showing clearance verification not provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Elevated walkways and accessible ramps are shown on site plans, but no section views demonstrate the 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductors. Conductor elevations are not surveyed."}]},{"text":"Parking areas shown on site plan without documentation addressing vehicle clearance from overhead lines or identification of areas with overhead line crossing concerns.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.19","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Parking areas are shown but no documentation addresses vehicle clearance from overhead lines or indicates which areas have overhead line crossing concerns."}]},{"text":"Trash collection and enclosed trash areas shown on site plan. Clearance verification from trash receptacle locations to overhead electric lines not documented; raised height considerations during service not addressed.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.26","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash collection areas are shown but no documentation addresses whether they are beneath overhead lines or whether trash bin service clearances have been verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash collection is addressed in site plan notes (Block 9 of Sheet 3). Trash enclosure locations are shown on site plan. Clearance verification from trash receptacle locations to overhead electric lines is not documented, and raised height considerations during service are not addressed."}]},{"text":"Water meter locations shown on electrical design plan, but no dimension shows clearance from water meter location to overhead electric service drops.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3; UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.28","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations are shown but clearance from overhead electric service drop conductors is not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed water meter connection point, but no dimension shows clearance from water meter location to any overhead electric service drops. Clearance verification is absent."}]},{"text":"Water utility plan shows water line routing, but clearance dimensions from water lines to overhead electrical distribution poles and conductors not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.29","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Water lines are shown but clearance dimensions from overhead distribution facilities are not documented on site plan or utility sections."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Water utility plan shows water line routing, but clearance dimensions from water lines to overhead electrical distribution poles and conductors are not provided. Clearance verification is absent."}]},{"text":"Site plan and electrical design plan show overhead and underground electrical service infrastructure, but primary vs. secondary overhead electric line types and their crossing relationships not documented.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.33","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but does not document secondary vs. primary conductor types or their crossing relationships."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows underground electrical service infrastructure. Utility plan does not clearly distinguish between primary and secondary overhead electric lines where they cross each other. Documentation of overhead line crossing details is not provided."}]},{"text":"Site plan addresses exterior lighting requirements. Fire Protection Plan shows lighting locations, but no dimension annotations show clearance distances from decorative lighting fixtures to overhead electric lines.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.36","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Decorative lighting locations are shown but clearance from overhead electric lines is not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) addresses exterior lighting requirements noting full cut-off fixture requirements. Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows lighting locations. However, no dimension annotations show clearance distances from decorative lighting fixtures to overhead electric lines, and no relocation notes are provided."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan shows proposed meter pad locations, but no enlarged detail views verify that required working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) are maintained free from obstructions.","citation":"UCM § 1.9.3.1","sourceId":"1:EL-1.38","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Meter locations are shown but no enlarged details verify that required working clearances (30\" × 36\" × 6.5'h) are maintained free from obstructions."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows meter pad locations. However, no enlarged detail views verify that working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9) are maintained. No analysis of obstructions from buildings, fences, walls, or landscaping is provided."}]},{"text":"Proposed buildings located near Valley View Road where streetlight poles may exist. No dimension shows clearance distance from building locations to existing streetlight pole locations.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.39","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Building locations and pole locations are shown but clearance dimensions from buildings to streetlight poles are not documented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Proposed buildings are located near Valley View Road where streetlight poles may exist. No dimension shows clearance distance from building locations to existing streetlight pole locations. Clearance verification is absent."}]},{"text":"Transformer locations shown on electrical design plan relative to overhead lines, but section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to transformer tops not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.43","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer locations are shown but section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to transformer tops are not provided."}]}]}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbf6244c-82ca-4498-85ed-9099636fbccb","uuid":"f7789ce1-d892-47b2-a8f1-8257a4bb5f49"}
