{"level":30,"time":1778247027110,"pid":122,"hostname":"4de9b0d3-b46","step":"organize-sections-simplified","step":"organize-sections-simplified","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR3WG5KG444YK7X59Y6227S8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the manifest. Let me organize the 21 comments into sections following the procedure:\n\n**Step 1: Group by code citation and physical element**\n\nPrimary citations and their comments:\n- UCM § 1.10.3 (Overhead conductor clearances): 1-0, 1-1, 1-2, 1-5, 1-6, 1-7, 13-5\n- UCM § 1.10.10.4 (Overhead distribution/tree compatibility): 1-3, 2-0, 2-2, 2-3\n- UCM § 1.10.4 (Transformer pads): 13-0, 13-1, 13-2, 13-6\n- UCM § 1.10.2 (Construction staging): 1-4\n- UCM § 2.9.1.B.2 (Underground utilities): 13-4\n- Reviewer Convention (Fire/Tree docs): 13-7, 2-1, 13-8\n\n**Step 2-4: Create sections with canonical names**\n\nThe comments are heavily focused on electrical/utility clearances. Let me group logically:\n\n1. **Building Design & Setbacks** - Building elevations and overhead clearances\n   - 1-0 (sev 3, conf 3): Missing building elevation sheets\n   - 1-1 (sev 3, conf 3): Missing section views\n   - 1-2 (sev 3, conf 2): Clearance annotations missing\n   - 2-0 (sev 3, conf 2): Overhead distribution violations\n\n2. **Infrastructure & Utilities** - Transformer pads, electrical, utilities\n   - 13-0 (sev 3, conf 3): Transformer outside property\n   - 13-2 (sev 2, conf 3): Access door clearance\n   - 13-4 (sev 2, conf 3): Underground utilities clearance\n   - 13-5 (sev 2, conf 3): Overhead distribution verification\n   - 13-6 (sev 2, conf 3): Transformer pad details\n   - 13-1 (sev 2, conf 2): Missing clearance to buildings\n   - 1-5 (sev 2, conf 2): Fencing/pond clearances\n   - 1-6 (sev 2, conf 2): Utility easements/conflicts\n   - 1-7 (sev 2, conf 2): Site utilities\n   - 2-3 (sev 2, conf 1): Transmission infrastructure\n   - 13-8 (sev 1, conf 2): Vertical clearances\n\n3. **Street Trees & Landscaping** - Ensuring plantings won't interfere with utilities\n   - 1-3 (sev 2, conf 3): Tree species compatibility\n   - 13-3 (sev 2, conf 3): Tree/shrub compatibility\n   - 2-1 (sev 2, conf 2): Tree species documentation\n   - 2-2 (sev 2, conf 2): Underground equipment clearances\n\n4. **Plan Documentation & Administrative** - Fire access and project documentation\n   - 1-4 (sev 2, conf 3): Construction staging plan\n   - 13-7 (sev 1, conf 2): Fire lane and hydrants\n\nI need to reconsider where 2-2 belongs. The comment about underground electrical equipment clearances and root barriers is fundamentally about landscaping's impact on utilities, so it fits better in the Street Trees & Landscaping section. Now ordering by severity and confidence within each section. The sections themselves rank by their maximum severity: Building Design & Setbacks has the highest at severity 3 with four items, Infrastructure & Utilities follows with one severity 3 item and multiple severity 2 items, while Street Trees & Landscaping and Plan Documentation & Administrative both max out at severity 2.\n\nWithin each section, I'm arranging by severity descending, then confidence descending. For Building Design & Setbacks, that's 1-0 and 1-1 (both s3, c3), then 1-2 (s3, c2), then 2-0 (s3, c2). Infrastructure & Utilities starts with 13-0 (s3, c3), followed by the four severity 2, confidence 3 items (13-2, 13-4, 13-5, 13-6), then the severity 2, confidence 2 items, severity 2 confidence 1, and finally 13-8 at severity 1. Street Trees & Landscaping leads with 1-3 and 13-3 (both s2, c3), then 2-1 and 2-2 (both s2, c2).\n\nFor Plan Documentation & Administrative, 1-4 comes first at s2, c3, followed by 13-7 at s1, c2. I'll structure the output to present these organized sections clearly.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,